  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""quick-start""><a class=""header"" href=""#quick-start"">Q"
  & "uick start</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Install</strong> via Alire: <code>alr install co"
  & "vex gnatprove &amp;&amp; export PATH=""$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
  & """</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Assess</strong> your project: <code>adacovex --t"
  & "arget=. --dal=C</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Serve</strong> the dashboard: <code>adacovex --t"
  & "arget=. --serve --port=8080</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>That is all you need for a local compliance assessment. F"
  & "or CI or release"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "workflows, see <a href=""#adacovex-cicd"">CI/CD</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex is distributed as the <code>covex</code> Alire c"
  & "rate, a release bundle on"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "GitHub, or a source build. All three routes produce the same"
  & " binary"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>adacovex</code>, with a <code>covex</code> alias on L"
  & "inux).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""option-1-declare-it-in-your-projects-alire-manifest-"
  & "recommended""><a class=""header"" href=""#option-1-declare-it-in"
  & "-your-projects-alire-manifest-recommended"">Option 1: declare"
  & " it in your project&#8217;s Alire manifest (recommended)</a>"
  & "</h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Put <code>covex</code> in your project&#8217;s <code>alir"
  & "e-dev.toml</code> (never <code>alire.toml</code>, so release"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "builds stay clean), alongside <code>gnatprove</code>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-toml""># &lt;project&gt;/alire-dev"
  & ".toml"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "[[depends-on]]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "covex = ""*"""
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove = ""^16.1.0"""
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Then <code>alr build</code> produces <code>bin/adacovex</"
  & "code> inside the project. <code>covex prove</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "deploys the pinned gnatprove crate standalone via <code>alr "
  & "-n get</code> and runs it"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directly. Each project pins its own exact toolchain version."
  & " No global install"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is needed:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">alr build"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "./bin/adacovex --target=. --dal=C"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "./bin/adacovex prove --target=.   # deploys gnatprove via al"
  & "r get, then runs it"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""option-2-alr-install-global-to-path""><a class=""heade"
  & "r"" href=""#option-2-alr-install-global-to-path"">Option 2: <co"
  & "de>alr install</code> (global, to <code>$PATH</code>)</a></h"
  & "2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">alr install covex gnatprove"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "export PATH=""$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"""
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>covex</code> is the Alire crate name for adacovex"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<a href=""https://alire.ada.dev/crates/covex"">crate page</a>"
  & "). Once on <code>$PATH</code>, it scans"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the current directory by default. A <code>gnatprove</code> i"
  & "nstalled this way is picked up"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "from <code>$PATH</code> by <code>covex prove</code> when the"
  & " target project declares no manifest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dependency of its own.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""option-3-download-a-release-bundle-from-github""><a c"
  & "lass=""header"" href=""#option-3-download-a-release-bundle-from"
  & "-github"">Option 3: download a release bundle from GitHub</a>"
  & "</h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag publishes `adacovex-vX. Y"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Z.tar.gz` on the <a href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/ad"
  & "acovex/releases"">GitHub Releases page</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">curl -fsSL https://raw.gith"
  & "ubusercontent.com/bladeacer/adacovex/main/install.sh | bash"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Bundles are attested with <a href=""https://github.com/act"
  & "ions/attest""><code>actions/attest</code></a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Release binaries are <strong>Linux x86-64 only</strong>. "
  & "Other platforms build from source"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "via Alire (see <a href=""#platform-support"">Platforms</a>).</"
  & "p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""building-from-source""><a class=""header"" href=""#build"
  & "ing-from-source"">Building from source</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">git clone --depth 1 https:/"
  & "/github.com/bladeacer/adacovex.git"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cd adacovex &amp;&amp; make build   # or: --branch vX.Y.Z fo"
  & "r a released tag"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make build</code> produces <code>bin/adacovex</code"
  & "> (with a <code>bin/covex</code> alias). A stock Alire"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "toolchain (<code>gnat_native</code> + <code>gprbuild</code>)"
  & " plus the standard GNAT runtime is all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that is needed. No other dependencies.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""version-source-per-installation-method""><a class=""he"
  & "ader"" href=""#version-source-per-installation-method"">Version"
  & " source per installation method</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex --version</code> (and the man page, the SB"
  & "OM tool version, and the result"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cache namespace) resolve the version from <code>tools/gen-ve"
  & "rsion.py</code>. The version"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "depends on the installation method:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> &#8211; release builds (th"
  & "e shipped binary always reports the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tag it was built from).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>alire/alire-dev.toml</code> &#8211; source checkou"
  & "ts (<code>version = ""x.y.z""</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>alire.toml</code> &#8211; dependency-managed insta"
  & "lls: the toml associated with the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>covex</code> binary for dependency management carries "
  & "the release version.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""keeping-the-man-page-in-sync""><a class=""header"" href"
  & "=""#keeping-the-man-page-in-sync"">Keeping the man page in syn"
  & "c</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> installs the man page (which em"
  & "beds the version) into"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>~/.local/share/man</code>. It refreshes <code>mandb</c"
  & "ode> when present. <code>adacovex man --check</code> exits 0"
  & " when the installed page matches the binary. A shell prompt"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hook can auto-update. <code>man --force</code> overwrites an"
  & " up-to-date page (for example"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to repair a hand-edited one).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When man-db is missing, the page still installs. Read it "
  & "with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>man -l ~/.local/share/man/man1/adacovex.1</code>. <cod"
  & "e>adacovex status</code> reports mandb"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "availability up front. See <a href=""#local-man-page-linuxwsl"
  & """>Platforms &#8211; local man page</a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "for the install roots and man-db behaviour.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""adacovex-cli-reference""><a class=""header"" href=""#ada"
  & "covex-cli-reference"">adacovex CLI Reference</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This page is the quick reference. It shows usage, the ful"
  & "l flag table, and a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "short note per flag. Feature-specific detail is in dedicated"
  & " pages (linked"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "from each section):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the <a href=""#web-dashboard-and-json-api"">web dashboard<"
  & "/a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the <a href=""#the-sbom-subcommand-1""><code>sbom</code> s"
  & "ubcommand</a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">VCS s"
  & "upport</a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the <a href=""#status-subcommand"">platforms/<code>status<"
  & "/code></a> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#installing-adacovex"">installation</a> pages</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#adacovex-architecture-decisions"">Architecture<"
  & "/a> for design detail such as result caching and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the patch system</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""usage""><a class=""header"" href=""#usage"">Usage</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>adacovex [options]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex sbom [--format=cyclonedx-json|spdx-json|md] [--out="
  & "PATH]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "           [--standard=NAME|--dal=LEVEL|--asil=LEVEL|--class"
  & "=LEVEL]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex prove [--target=PATH] [prove options]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex status [--target=PATH]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex man [--check|--force] [--dir=PATH]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex completion [bash|fish|zsh|pwsh]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""flags""><a class=""header"" href=""#flags"">Flags</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Mode</th><th>Descriptio"
  & "n</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--target=PATH</code></td><td><code>.</code> (C"
  & "WD)</td><td>both</td><td>Target project root directory</td><"
  & "/tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--manifest=PATH</code></td><td>auto-detected</"
  & "td><td>both</td><td>Override project manifest path</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--dal=LEVEL</code></td><td><code>C</code></td>"
  & "<td>both</td><td>DO-178C DAL level (A-E, also the shared rig"
  & "our tier)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--asil=LEVEL</code></td><td>-</td><td>both</td"
  & "><td>ISO 26262 level: <code>A</code>|<code>B</code>|<code>C<"
  & "/code>|<code>D</code>|<code>QM</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--class=LEVEL</code></td><td>-</td><td>both</t"
  & "d><td>IEC 62304 safety class: <code>A</code>|<code>B</code>|"
  & "<code>C</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--standard=NAME</code></td><td><code>do178c</c"
  & "ode></td><td>both</td><td><code>do178c</code>|<code>iso26262"
  & "</code>|<code>iec62304</code>|<code>all</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--serve</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td><t"
  & "d>Start HTTP dashboard server (standard-aware, light/dark/sy"
  & "stem themes)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--serve-workers=N</code></td><td><code>4</code"
  & "></td><td>serve</td><td>HTTP server task-pool worker count</"
  & "td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--theme=NAME</code></td><td><code>system</code"
  & "></td><td>serve</td><td>Dashboard theme: <code>light</code>|"
  & "<code>dark</code>|<code>system</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--port=N</code></td><td><code>8080</code></td>"
  & "<td>serve</td><td>Dashboard server port</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--tz=ZONE</code> / <code>--timezone=ZONE</code"
  & "></td><td>OS timezone</td><td>both</td><td>Display timezone "
  & "(IANA name or UTC/GMT offset)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--excludes=EXT,EXT</code></td><td>empty</td><t"
  & "d>complexity</td><td>Skip comma-separated file extensions</t"
  & "d></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--emit-svg=PATH</code></td><td><code>&lt;targe"
  & "t&gt;/docs/badges</code></td><td>both</td><td>Output directo"
  & "ry for SVG badges</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--no-svg</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td><"
  & "td>Suppress SVG badge output</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--emit-markdown=PATH</code></td><td>off</td><t"
  & "d>both</td><td>Output directory for Markdown reports</td></t"
  & "r>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code></td><td>off</td><td"
  & ">both</td><td>Write a JSON export of metrics + dependency gr"
  & "aph to PATH</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--completion[=SHELL]</code></td><td>-</td><td>"
  & "-</td><td>Print shell completion script (bash/fish/zsh/pwsh,"
  & " auto-detected) and exit</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--skip-dir=NAME</code></td><td><code>demo,deps"
  & ",examples</code></td><td>relaxed</td><td>Directory name to s"
  & "kip (repeatable)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--relaxed</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td>"
  & "<td>Disable strict mode (skip dirs, no patches)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--compare-base=REF</code></td><td>off</td><td>"
  & "both</td><td>Differential mode vs a base rev (git/hg/svn/fos"
  & "sil/jj)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--coverage-delta=REF</code></td><td>off</td><t"
  & "d>both</td><td>Docstring-coverage gate vs a base rev (git/hg"
  & "/svn/fossil/jj)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--cache</code></td><td>on</td><td>both</td><td"
  & ">Enable on-disk result caching</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--no-cache</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td"
  & "><td>Disable result caching (always re-scan/re-parse/re-prov"
  & "e)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--cache-dir=PATH</code></td><td><code>~/.adaco"
  & "vex/cache/&lt;ver&gt;/&lt;schema&gt;</code></td><td>both</td"
  & "><td>Cache directory for analysis results</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--cache-max=N</code></td><td><code>4096</code>"
  & "</td><td>both</td><td>Max cache entries before oldest-first "
  & "eviction</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--no-sbom</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td>"
  & "<td>Skip the automatic SBOM written at the end of every asse"
  & "ssment</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--sbom-format=FMT</code></td><td><code>cyclone"
  & "dx-json</code></td><td>both</td><td>Format of the automatic "
  & "SBOM: <code>cyclonedx-json</code>|<code>spdx-json</code>|<co"
  & "de>md</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--require-spark=LVL</code></td><td>off</td><td"
  & ">both</td><td>Fail loudly (exit 1) if SPARK level &lt; LVL ("
  & "Stone..Platinum)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--require-docstrings=PCT</code></td><td>off</t"
  & "d><td>both</td><td>Fail loudly if docstring coverage &lt; PC"
  & "T% (0-100)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--require-tests=N</code></td><td>off</td><td>b"
  & "oth</td><td>Fail loudly if passing test count &lt; N</td></t"
  & "r>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--require-proof=PCT</code></td><td>off</td><td"
  & ">both</td><td>Fail loudly if proved-VC coverage &lt; PCT% (0"
  & "-100)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--verbose</code></td><td>off</td><td>both</td>"
  & "<td>Verbose diagnostics</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--version</code></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>P"
  & "rint the bundled version and exit</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>man</code></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>Install"
  & " the man page into the local man database</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>man --check</code></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td"
  & ">Exit 0 if the installed man page matches the binary version"
  & ", 1 otherwise</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>man --force</code></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td"
  & ">Reinstall the man page even when it already matches (repair"
  & ")</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>man --dir=PATH</code></td><td><code>~/.local/s"
  & "hare/man</code></td><td>-</td><td>Install the man page under"
  & " <code>PATH/man1</code> instead</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--help</code></td><td>-</td><td>both</td><td>P"
  & "rint usage and exit</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>prove</code>-mode flags are also accepted by the ma"
  & "in command. They are validated"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "only in prove mode. The flags are: <code>--jobs</code>/<code"
  & ">-j</code>, <code>--level</code>, <code>--timeout</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--steps</code>, <code>--memlimit</code>, <code>--force"
  & "</code>, <code>--no-loop-unrolling</code>, <code>--no-inlini"
  & "ng</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--suppress-warnings</code>, <code>--quiet</code>. See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#the-prove-subcommand"">The <code>prove</code> subco"
  & "mmand</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""flag-details""><a class=""header"" href=""#flag-details"""
  & ">Flag details</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--targetpath""><a class=""header"" href=""#--targetpath"""
  & "><code>--target=PATH</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Project to analyse. Relative paths are resolved against t"
  & "he current working"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory to an absolute path. The path determines the root "
  & "directory for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "source scanning, manifest detection, SVG badge output, and p"
  & "atch file"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resolution. Default: the current working directory.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--manifestpath""><a class=""header"" href=""#--manifestp"
  & "ath""><code>--manifest=PATH</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Override the project manifest file. Auto-detected from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/alire-dev.toml</code> or <code>&lt;targ"
  & "et&gt;/alire.toml</code> (dev first). The manifest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "path is shown in stderr output and used by <code>adacovex sb"
  & "om</code> to resolve the root"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "project metadata for the dependency graph.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--dallevel""><a class=""header"" href=""#--dallevel""><co"
  & "de>--dal=LEVEL</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>DO-178C DAL level (and the shared rigour tier): <code>A</"
  & "code>, <code>B</code>, <code>C</code>, <code>D</code>, or <c"
  & "ode>E</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(case-insensitive). It determines the minimum SPARK proof le"
  & "vel required and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the specific criteria checked. This tier is shared across st"
  & "andards."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--dal=C</code> is DAL-C under DO-178C, ASIL B under IS"
  & "O 26262, and safety Class A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "under IEC 62304. See <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.h"
  & "tml"">DAL levels</a> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#compliance-standards-do-178c--iso-26262--iec-62304"
  & """>Standards</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--asillevel""><a class=""header"" href=""#--asillevel""><"
  & "code>--asil=LEVEL</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>ISO 26262 Automotive Safety Integrity Level: <code>A</cod"
  & "e>, <code>B</code>, <code>C</code>, <code>D</code>, or <code"
  & ">QM</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(case-insensitive). It sets the standard to <code>iso26262</"
  & "code> and maps the ASIL level"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to the shared rigour tier (ASIL D -&gt; DAL A, ASIL C -&gt; "
  & "DAL B, ASIL B -&gt; DAL C,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ASIL A -&gt; DAL D, QM -&gt; DAL E). As a result, <code>--as"
  & "il=B</code> is the clearest spelling"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "of &#8220;assess this project at ASIL B&#8221;. See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-asil-levels.html"">ASIL Levels</a>"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--classlevel""><a class=""header"" href=""#--classlevel"""
  & "><code>--class=LEVEL</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>IEC 62304 software safety class: <code>A</code>, <code>B<"
  & "/code>, or <code>C</code> (case-insensitive). It sets"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the standard to <code>iec62304</code> and maps the class to "
  & "the shared rigour tier"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(Class C -&gt; DAL A, Class B -&gt; DAL B, Class A -&gt; DAL"
  & " C). As a result,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--class=A</code> is the clearest spelling of &#8220;as"
  & "sess this project at safety Class"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "A&#8221;. See <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-class-levels.html"">"
  & "Safety Classes</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--standardname""><a class=""header"" href=""#--standardn"
  & "ame""><code>--standard=NAME</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Select the compliance standard used to label the assessme"
  & "nt (default"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>do178c</code>). The evidence checks are identical acro"
  & "ss standards. Only the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "integrity-level names change in the report and badges:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>do178c</code> &#8211; DAL A&#8211;E (avionics)</li"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>iso26262</code> &#8211; ASIL D / C / B / A / QM (a"
  & "utomotive)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>iec62304</code> &#8211; Class C / B / A / no class"
  & " (medical-device software)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>all</code> &#8211; run one assessment at the share"
  & "d tier and emit badges/reports for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "every standard (<code>do178c.svg</code>, <code>iso26262.svg<"
  & "/code>, <code>iec62304.svg</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Accepted case-insensitively, with or without the hyphen/s"
  & "pace (<code>ISO-26262</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>iec62304</code>, and more). See <a href=""#compliance-s"
  & "tandards-do-178c--iso-26262--iec-62304"">Standards</a> for th"
  & "e full tier"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "mapping.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When both a dedicated level flag (<code>--asil</code> / <"
  & "code>--class</code>) and <code>--standard</code> are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "passed, the dedicated flag sets the standard. <code>--standa"
  & "rd</code> is ignored for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "labelling (last-write-wins per field). The shared tier is al"
  & "ways whatever the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "level flag (or <code>--dal</code>) resolved to.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""status""><a class=""header"" href=""#status""><code>statu"
  & "s</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex status [--target=PATH]</code> reports tool"
  & "chain and platform state. It"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "does not run an assessment. It does not download or deploy a"
  & "nything. It"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "reports the following:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>whether Alire is installed</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>how gnatprove is resolved</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the host CPU count and CI status (and the resulting defa"
  & "ult <code>-j</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "parallelism)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>a <strong>VCS report</strong> (which VCS tools are on <c"
  & "ode>$PATH</code> and which manages the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "target &#8211; see <a href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-as"
  & "sessment"">VCS support</a>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>mandb availability</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the effective display timezone, the current date/time in"
  & " it, and how many"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dated release changelogs the target carries</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex status --tz=ZONE</code> (or <code>--timezo"
  & "ne=ZONE</code>) overrides the display"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "timezone for the report. It shows the effective timezone, th"
  & "e current date"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and time in that zone, and how many dated release changelogs"
  & " the target"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "carries. Exit <code>0</code> when a usable gnatprove is dete"
  & "ctable without a download."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Exit <code>1</code> otherwise; for full detail see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#status-subcommand"">Platforms &#8211; <code>status<"
  & "/code> subcommand</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex status --export</code> prints the report a"
  & "s machine-readable JSON on"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "stdout; <code>status --export=PATH</code> writes it to <code"
  & ">PATH</code>. Scripts and CI can"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "consume it without parsing prose. <code>adacovex status --me"
  & "trics</code> prints the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same data as compact <code>key=value</code> lines, one per l"
  & "ine, for shell scripts."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Both flags only work with the <code>status</code> subcommand"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""complexity""><a class=""header"" href=""#complexity""><co"
  & "de>complexity</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex complexity [--target=PATH] [--excludes=EXT"
  & ",EXT]</code> runs a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cyclomatic-complexity and LOC check across the target&#8217;"
  & "s source files in many"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "languages. <code>--excludes=EXT,EXT</code> skips comma-separ"
  & "ated file extensions (for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "example <code>md,rst</code>) and only works with the <code>c"
  & "omplexity</code> subcommand. It prints"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a tokei-style summary (files, lines, code, comments, blanks)"
  & " plus a per-file"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "table of <code>Lines=</code>, <code>Code=</code>, <code>Comm"
  & "ents=</code>, <code>Blanks=</code>, the codebase loc"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "percentage, and the cyclomatic complexity <code>cx=</code>. "
  & "The gate fails when a file"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "or function exceeds the thresholds (defaults: 4 000 LOC, 10%"
  & " of codebase per"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "file, 120 per function, 600 per file).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Exit <code>0</code> when all gates pass. Exit <code>1</co"
  & "de> otherwise. This replaces the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "previous Python <code>check-complexity.py</code> script and "
  & "is wired into"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make complexity-check</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""the-prove-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-p"
  & "rove-subcommand"">The <code>prove</code> subcommand</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex prove --target=PATH</code> resolves a gnat"
  & "prove installation and runs it against the target. It then f"
  & "alls through to the normal assessment pipeline. The pipeline"
  & " parses the freshly generated proof summary. As a result, on"
  & "e command both proves and assesses.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For the full guide to proving and writing SPARK proofs (c"
  & "ontracts, VC categories, proof patches for vendored deps), s"
  & "ee <a href=""#proving-and-writing-spark-proofs"">Proving and w"
  & "riting proofs</a>. gnatprove is resolved in this order: mani"
  & "fest pin &gt; global pin &gt; <code>$PATH</code> &gt; cached"
  & " toolchain &gt; download. The target does not need to declar"
  & "e gnatprove. Full detail: <a href=""#gnatprove-toolchain-reso"
  & "lution-prove-subcommand"">Architecture &#8211; GNATprove tool"
  & "chain resolution</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The proof summary is written to <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/"
  & "gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code> (the same location the assess"
  & "ment discovers). The SVG badges are emitted as usual. The re"
  & "sult cache serves unchanged targets. <code>--force</code> by"
  & "passes the cache and forces a full gnatprove reanalysis. Whe"
  & "n the target carries proof patches (<code>.adacovex/patches/"
  & "</code>), gnatprove runs against a patched tree copy at <cod"
  & "e>&lt;target&gt;/obj/adacovex-proof/</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Vendored dependencies then participate in the proof witho"
  & "ut their sources being touched. See <a href=""#proof-patches-"
  & "proving-vendored-dependencies"">Proving and writing proofs</a"
  & "> for how to write them, and <a href=""#proof-patches-spark-c"
  & "ontracts-over-vendored-dependencies"">Architecture &#8211; Pr"
  & "oof patches</a> for the design.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--jobs=N</code>, <code>-j N</code></td><td>aut"
  & "o</td><td>GNATprove parallelism: auto-detect (max(1, cores-2"
  & "), all cores in CI), <code>0</code> = all cores, <code>N</co"
  & "de> = pin N processes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--level=N</code></td><td>tool default</td><td>"
  & "GNATprove proof effort, 0-4</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--timeout=N</code></td><td>tool default</td><t"
  & "d>Per-check prover timeout in seconds</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--steps=N</code></td><td><code>10000</code></t"
  & "d><td>Max proof steps (reproducible budget, an explicit valu"
  & "e overrides the default)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--memlimit=N</code></td><td>tool default</td><"
  & "td>Prover memory limit in MB</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--force</code></td><td>off</td><td>Force full "
  & "gnatprove reanalysis (<code>-f</code>). Also bypasses the re"
  & "sult cache</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--no-loop-unrolling</code></td><td>always on</"
  & "td><td>Disable automatic loop unrolling. Loop unrolling is a"
  & "lways disabled, so GNATprove never emits the purely-informat"
  & "ional <code>cannot unroll loop (too many loop iterations) [i"
  & "nfo-unrolling-inlining]</code> notice. It is proof-neutral f"
  & "or the dogfood targets (720/720 adacovex, 589/589 Ada_CRDT V"
  & "Cs, 0 unproved). Flag kept for compatibility</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--no-inlining</code></td><td>off</td><td>Disab"
  & "le contextual analysis inlining</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--quiet</code></td><td>on</td><td>Hide GNATpro"
  & "ve&#8217;s benign info messages (the default suppression set"
  & ", the loop-unrolling/inlining notice blocks) from stdout. It"
  & " is active by default for local runs. <code>--verbose</code>"
  & " always shows every message and wins over it. CI passes <cod"
  & "e>--verbose</code>, so CI output stays authoritative. This i"
  & "s the explicit form of the default</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--suppress-warnings</code></td><td>on</td><td>"
  & "Alias of <code>--quiet</code> (the default suppression set)."
  & " Kept for compatibility</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--suppress-warnings=SETS</code></td><td>on</td"
  & "><td>Hide GNATprove info messages whose tags match the comma"
  & "-separated suppression-set names (for example <code>--suppre"
  & "ss-warnings=unrolling-inlining,xyz</code>). A set name <code"
  & ">S</code> suppresses blocks tagged <code>[info-S]</code> (or"
  & " bare <code>[S]</code>). <code>--verbose</code> always shows"
  & " every message</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>prove</code> accepts all assessment flags too (<cod"
  & "e>--dal</code>, <code>--standard</code>, the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--require-*</code> gates, <code>--emit-svg</code>, and"
  & " more), so CI gates apply to the proof"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "run directly. <code>--force</code> is shared with <code>man "
  & "--force</code> (see below). The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "remaining prove flags are validated only in prove mode.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""automatic-sbom---no-sbom----sbom-format""><a class=""h"
  & "eader"" href=""#automatic-sbom---no-sbom----sbom-format"">Autom"
  & "atic SBOM (<code>--no-sbom</code> / <code>--sbom-format</cod"
  & "e>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every assessment writes a proof-aware SBOM by default (th"
  & "e pipeline&#8217;s last"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "step): <code>&lt;target&gt;/sbom.json</code> (CycloneDX 1.5)"
  & ", <code>&lt;target&gt;/sbom.spdx.json</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(SPDX 2.3), or <code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/SBOM.md<"
  & "/code> depending on"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--sbom-format</code> (default <code>cyclonedx-json</co"
  & "de>). <code>--no-sbom</code> skips it entirely."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "These are separate from the dedicated <a href=""#the-sbom-sub"
  & "command-1""><code>sbom</code> subcommand</a>, which"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "writes a single SBOM at an explicit path and exits.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--serve""><a class=""header"" href=""#--serve""><code>--s"
  & "erve</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A <strong>switch</strong>: when given, adacovex scans and"
  & " assesses the target, then starts the built-in HTTP/1.1 web "
  & "dashboard on <code>--port</code> (default <code>8080</code>)"
  & " and blocks until interrupted. Passing <code>--serve</code> "
  & "is the only way to start the server; omitting it (the defaul"
  & "t, <code>off</code>) renders and exits without serving. Ther"
  & "e is no <code>--no-serve</code>, because the flag already co"
  & "ntrols it. It serves an HTML dashboard at <code>/</code>, a "
  & "JSON API at <code>/api/metrics</code>, the SVG badges at <co"
  & "de>/badge/*.svg</code>, and the bundled offline manual at <c"
  & "ode>/docs</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The dashboard is standard-aware (it defaults to all stand"
  & "ards) and supports light, dark, and system themes.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Full detail, the JSON schema, the theme-resolution order,"
  & " and embedding tips are in <a href=""#web-dashboard-and-json-"
  & "api"">Web dashboard and JSON API</a>. Related flags: <code>--"
  & "port</code>, <code>--serve-workers</code>, <code>--theme</co"
  & "de>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--themename""><a class=""header"" href=""#--themename""><"
  & "code>--theme=NAME</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Dashboard colour theme for <code>--serve</code>: <code>sy"
  & "stem</code> (default, follows <code>prefers-color-scheme</co"
  & "de>), <code>light</code>, or <code>dark</code> (case-insensi"
  & "tive). It sets the initial dropdown selection in the served "
  & "page. The header dropdown can switch live afterwards, and <s"
  & "trong>Save settings</strong> persists the choice in <code>lo"
  & "calStorage</code> (no cookies). Only relevant with <code>--s"
  & "erve</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>See <a href=""#themes"">dashboard themes</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--portn""><a class=""header"" href=""#--portn""><code>--p"
  & "ort=N</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HTTP server port when <code>--serve</code> is used. Must "
  & "be a valid <code>Positive</code> integer."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Only relevant with <code>--serve</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--serve-workersn""><a class=""header"" href=""#--serve-w"
  & "orkersn""><code>--serve-workers=N</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HTTP server task-pool worker count when <code>--serve</co"
  & "de> is used. Default is <code>4</code>."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Raise it to handle more concurrent dashboard requests, or lo"
  & "wer it to use"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "less memory. It must be a valid <code>Positive</code> intege"
  & "r and only works with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--serve</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--tzzone----timezonezone""><a class=""header"" href=""#-"
  & "-tzzone----timezonezone""><code>--tz=ZONE</code> / <code>--ti"
  & "mezone=ZONE</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Display timezone for the status report.  Accepts a well-k"
  & "nown IANA name"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(for example <code>Asia/Singapore</code>) or a fixed UTC/GMT"
  & " offset (<code>UTC+8</code>, <code>GMT+8</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>UTC+08</code>, <code>GMT+08</code>, <code>UTC+08:30</c"
  & "ode>).  Without it adacovex uses the operating"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "system&#8217;s timezone.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A named zone resolves from a built-in table of common IAN"
  & "A names.  A zone"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that may observe daylight saving time, or one the table lack"
  & "s, is probed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "against the platform tzdata (<code>zdump</code> + <code>date"
  & " +%z</code>) for the DST-correct"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "current offset, with the table as the fallback when the prob"
  & "e is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "unavailable.  Values are matched case-insensitively, and a b"
  & "ad value fails"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "loudly.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--emit-svgpath""><a class=""header"" href=""#--emit-svgp"
  & "ath""><code>--emit-svg=PATH</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Write SVG badges to a directory. Default <code>&lt;target"
  & "&gt;/docs/badges</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(project-scoped). Creates:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>spark.svg</code> &#8211; SPARK assurance level (St"
  & "one through Platinum)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>tests.svg</code> &#8211; test pass/fail count</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>do178c.svg</code> / <code>iso26262.svg</code> / <c"
  & "ode>iec62304.svg</code> &#8211; compliance status for the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "selected standard (Achieved / Unmet), or all three with <cod"
  & "e>--standard=all</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>docs.svg</code> &#8211; docstring coverage percent"
  & "age</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--no-svg</code> overrides and disables SVG output e"
  & "ntirely.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--no-svg""><a class=""header"" href=""#--no-svg""><code>-"
  & "-no-svg</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Suppress all SVG badge output. Overrides <code>--emit-svg"
  & "</code> if both are given.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--emit-metricspath""><a class=""header"" href=""#--emit-"
  & "metricspath""><code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>After the assessment, it writes a machine-readable JSON e"
  & "xport to <code>PATH</code>:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>{""metrics"": {...}, ""dependencies"": {...}}</code>.  <co"
  & "de>metrics</code> is the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "object the dashboard JSON API serves at <code>/api/metrics</"
  & "code>.  <code>dependencies</code> is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the resolved dependency graph (name, version, scope, parent,"
  & " purl, kind) at"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>/api/deps</code>.  It is useful for scripting gates, e"
  & "xternal dashboards, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "archiving assessment results. The composite GitHub Action up"
  & "loads it as a CI"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "artifact when <code>emit-metrics</code> is set.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--emit-markdownpath""><a class=""header"" href=""#--emit"
  & "-markdownpath""><code>--emit-markdown=PATH</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Write compliance reports to a directory. Creates two file"
  & "s:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>VERIFICATION.md</code> &#8211; full verification r"
  & "eport with all metrics</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>TRACE.md</code> &#8211; HLR traceability matrix (s"
  & "ource-to-requirement mapping)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--skip-dirname""><a class=""header"" href=""#--skip-dirn"
  & "ame""><code>--skip-dir=NAME</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Add a directory name to the scanner&#8217;s skip list (re"
  & "peatable). Directories whose"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "simple name matches an entry are not recursed into during so"
  & "urce scanning."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Only effective in relaxed mode. In strict mode (default) the"
  & " skip list is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "always empty.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--relaxed""><a class=""header"" href=""#--relaxed""><code"
  & ">--relaxed</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Disable strict mode. Enables the skip list (default <code"
  & ">demo,deps,examples</code> plus"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "any <code>--skip-dir</code> entries) and does NOT apply <cod"
  & "e>.adacovex/patches/</code>. See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relaxed mode</a>"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--compare-baseref""><a class=""header"" href=""#--compar"
  & "e-baseref""><code>--compare-base=REF</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Differential mode: snapshot a base revision and print a s"
  & "ide-by-side comparison against the current tree (packages, s"
  & "ubprograms, docstring %, HLR traced, orphan tags, SPARK leve"
  & "l, VCs proved, tests, DAL status). Exit <code>0</code> only "
  & "if there are no regressions AND the current DAL is Achieved."
  & " Exit <code>1</code> otherwise. Works on <strong>git, Mercur"
  & "ial, Subversion, Fossil, and jj</strong>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Full detail and the per-VCS snapshot mechanisms are in <a"
  & " href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">VCS support"
  & " and differential assessment</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--coverage-deltaref""><a class=""header"" href=""#--cove"
  & "rage-deltaref""><code>--coverage-delta=REF</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Lightweight docstring-coverage gate for PR-style CI check"
  & "s. Scans sources + patches + computes docstring metrics on b"
  & "oth a base revision and the current tree (no GNATprove/tests"
  & "/DAL), prints a compact coverage table plus a machine-parsea"
  & "ble <code>coverage_delta:</code> line, and cleans up the sna"
  & "pshot. Exit <code>0</code> if current docstring coverage is "
  & "<code>&gt;=</code> the base. Exit <code>1</code> if coverage"
  & " regressed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Mutually exclusive with <code>--compare-base</code>. See "
  & "<a href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">VCS suppo"
  & "rt and differential assessment</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--version""><a class=""header"" href=""#--version""><code"
  & ">--version</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Print the bundled version (<code>adacovex vX. Y. Z</code>"
  & ") and exit, without scanning or assessing. The version sourc"
  & "e depends on the <strong>installation method</strong> (<code"
  & ">ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> for release builds, <code>alire-dev"
  & ".toml</code> for source checkouts, <code>alire.toml</code> f"
  & "or dependency-managed installs).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The same constant drives the man page, the SBOM tool vers"
  & "ion, and the result-cache namespace. As a result, they canno"
  & "t drift. Full detail: <a href=""#version-source-per-installat"
  & "ion-method"">Installation &#8211; version source</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""completion""><a class=""header"" href=""#completion""><co"
  & "de>completion</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex completion [SHELL]</code> (also <code>adac"
  & "ovex --completion[=SHELL]</code>) prints"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a static shell-completion script to stdout and exits.  <code"
  & ">SHELL</code> is one of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>bash</code>, <code>fish</code>, <code>zsh</code>, <cod"
  & "e>pwsh</code>, when omitted it is auto-detected from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>$SHELL</code>, falling back to bash for unknown or emp"
  & "ty shells.  Typical setup:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">eval ""$(adacovex completion"
  & ")""        # bash (default)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "source &lt;(adacovex completion zsh)    # zsh"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex completion fish | source    # fish"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex completion pwsh | Invoke-Expression   # PowerShell"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The scripts complete the subcommands and every long flag "
  & "from the binary&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "own flag table, so the completion set cannot drift from the "
  & "CLI. The flag"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "list embeds at generation time. Re-run <code>adacovex comple"
  & "tion</code> after upgrading"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex (a shell prompt hook that regenerates on version ch"
  & "ange works well).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""man""><a class=""header"" href=""#man""><code>man</code><"
  & "/a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>man</code> subcommand installs the adacovex man"
  & " page into the <strong>local man"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "database</strong> (Linux/WSL, no root required) and refreshe"
  & "s the index with <code>mandb</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "when present. <code>adacovex man --check</code> exits 0 when"
  & " the installed page matches"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the binary. It exits 1 otherwise (a shell prompt hook can au"
  & "to-update as a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "result). <code>--dir=PATH</code> overrides the install root."
  & " Full detail, exit codes,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and the prompt-hook recipe are in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#keeping-the-man-page-in-sync"">Installation &#8211;"
  & " keeping the man page in sync</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""vcs-support""><a class=""header"" href=""#vcs-support"">V"
  & "CS support</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>A version control system is not required for base"
  & " adacovex functionality</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compliance assessme"
  & "nt, SBOM generation, dashboards, caching). A VCS is only nee"
  & "ded for the differential modes (<code>--compare-base</code> "
  & "/ <code>--coverage-delta</code>). Those modes snapshot a bas"
  & "e revision across <strong>git, Mercurial, Subversion, Fossil"
  & ", and jj</strong> without touching the working tree. Detecti"
  & "on is marker-file based (<code>.git</code> / <code>.jj</code"
  & "> / <code>.hg</code> / <code>.svn</code> / <code>.fslckout</"
  & "code> / <code>_FOSSIL_</code>) with a command-probe fallback"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Full detail, the snapshot mechanism per VCS, and the Subv"
  & "ersion/Fossil UX notes are in <a href=""#vcs-support-and-diff"
  & "erential-assessment"">VCS support and differential assessment"
  & "</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""ci-threshold-gates---require-""><a class=""header"" hre"
  & "f=""#ci-threshold-gates---require-"">CI threshold gates (<code"
  & ">--require-*</code>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The four <code>--require-*</code> flags add explicit mini"
  & "mum-bar checks on top of the DAL"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "criteria. They are off by default. When set, the assessment "
  & "fails loudly"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(exit code <code>1</code>, with an explicit <code>CI GATE:</"
  & "code> reason printed to the report) if the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "target does not meet the required level:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex --target=. --requi"
  & "re-spark=Platinum --require-docstrings=100 \"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "         --require-tests=1173 --require-proof=100"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>require-spark</code> compares the honest assessed "
  & "SPARK level (Stone..Platinum).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>require-docstrings</code> and <code>require-proof<"
  & "/code> take a percentage (0-100).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>require-tests</code> takes a count of passing test"
  & "s.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>CI that pins a gnatprove version (manifest or global <cod"
  & "e>adacovex.toml</code> pin)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "must set these to the values that version actually achieves."
  & " A stricter"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "prover can legitimately leave more VCs unproved. As a result"
  & ", gate on the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "results of the prover you pin.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""result-caching---cache----no-cache----cache-dir----c"
  & "ache-max""><a class=""header"" href=""#result-caching---cache---"
  & "-no-cache----cache-dir----cache-max"">Result caching (<code>-"
  & "-cache</code> / <code>--no-cache</code> / <code>--cache-dir<"
  & "/code> / <code>--cache-max</code>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex persists parsed analysis results on disk, so unc"
  & "hanged inputs are not re-scanned, re-parsed, or re-proved. E"
  & "very entry is keyed by a namespace prefix plus the SHA-256 o"
  & "f the artifact(s) it was derived from. An unchanged manifest"
  & "/lockfile/.gpr set serves the cached dependency graph. Uncha"
  & "nged HLR.md/LLR.md serve the cached requirement parses. <cod"
  & "e>--no-cache</code> bypasses it entirely. <code>--cache-dir<"
  & "/code> relocates it. <code>--cache-max</code> (default <code"
  & ">4096</code>) caps entries before oldest-first eviction.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The ANSI report shows a <code>result cache: X hit(s), Y m"
  & "iss(es), Z evicted</code> line per run. Full design (schema "
  & "namespace, eviction, overflow safety, <code>--target</code> "
  & "normalization) is in <a href=""#result-caching-1"">Architectur"
  & "e &#8211; Result caching</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--verbose""><a class=""header"" href=""#--verbose""><code"
  & ">--verbose</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Print pipeline step diagnostics to stderr.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""--help-and-contextual-help""><a class=""header"" href="""
  & "#--help-and-contextual-help""><code>--help</code> and context"
  & "ual <code>help</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--help</code> prints all options, defaults, and exa"
  & "mples to stdout, then exits. No"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scanning or assessment is performed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Contextual help</strong>: the <code>help</code> k"
  & "eyword prints flag/subcommand-specific text"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "instead of the full usage. The topic can be given in either "
  & "order, with or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "without the leading <code>--</code>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>adacovex help serve        # or: help --serve, --"
  & "serve help"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex help standard     # standard / dal / asil / class"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex help sbom         # subcommands: sbom, prove, statu"
  & "s, man"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex help theme        # every flag has a topic (port, t"
  & "arget, ...)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex help              # no topic: full usage"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The topic is case-insensitive and an <code>=value</code> "
  & "suffix is ignored"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>help --standard=all</code> == <code>help standard</co"
  & "de>). Unknown topics print the full"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "usage with an &#8220;Unknown topic&#8221; notice. Contextual"
  & " help exits <code>0</code> and never"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scans or assesses.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""strict-vs-relaxed-mode""><a class=""header"" href=""#str"
  & "ict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relaxed mode</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Strict (default)</th><th>Relaxed (<co"
  & "de>--relaxed</code>)</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Directory exclusions</td><td><code>.git</code>, <cod"
  & "e>obj</code>, <code>tests</code>, <code>config</code>, <code"
  & ">.adacovex</code> only</td><td>Same + <code>demo,deps,exampl"
  & "es</code> + <code>--skip-dir</code> additions</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Vendored code</td><td>Scanned and counted</td><td>Sk"
  & "ipped</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Patch files</td><td>Applied from <code>.adacovex/pat"
  & "ches/</code> (docstrings always, SPARK proof aspects in prov"
  & "e mode)</td><td>Not applied</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Use case</td><td>Full compliance audit</td><td>Quick"
  & " assessment of production code</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Patch files can carry more than docstrings. A patch with "
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Pre</code> / <code>Post</code> / <code>Global</code> a"
  & "spects is a <strong>proof patch</strong> that adds SPARK"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contracts to vendored code in prove mode (spec patches <code"
  & ">.ads</code>, and body"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "patches <code>.adb</code> opt the vendored body into the pro"
  & "of). Why they exist, how"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to write them, worked examples, and pitfalls are in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">Provi"
  & "ng and writing proofs &#8211; proof patches</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""exit-codes""><a class=""header"" href=""#exit-codes"">Exi"
  & "t codes</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>0</code></td><td>Success (DAL achieved, all ch"
  & "ecks pass, <code>--version</code>, man page installed/up-to-"
  & "date)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>Compliance failure (DAL unmet"
  & ", tests failing, a <code>--require-*</code> CI gate unmet, d"
  & "ifferential regression, <code>man --check</code> finding a n"
  & "ewer version available or none installed, and more)</td></tr"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""terminal-colour""><a class=""header"" href=""#terminal-c"
  & "olour"">Terminal colour</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex colours its terminal output (red for failures, g"
  & "reen for passes,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bold for headings) so the important lines stand out.  Colour"
  & " is enabled by"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "default on a normal terminal.  It is suppressed automaticall"
  & "y when the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "output would not take it:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>NO_COLOR</code> is set (the cross-tool opt-out con"
  & "vention);</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>a CI variable is set (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and mor"
  & "e), so CI logs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "stay plain and machine-readable;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>TERM</code> is <code>dumb</code> (or set to an emp"
  & "ty value).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""the-sbom-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-sb"
  & "om-subcommand"">The <code>sbom</code> subcommand</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex sbom</code> resolves the target project&#8"
  & "217;s dependency graph from its Alire"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest, <code>alire/alire.lock</code>, and the root <code>"
  & ".gpr</code> <code>with</code> clauses, then writes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a proof-aware software bill of materials in CycloneDX 1.5 JS"
  & "ON or SPDX 2.3"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JSON. It is <strong>standard-aware</strong> (it defaults to "
  & "all standards), honours"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> for byte-for-byte determinist"
  & "ic output, and is mutually"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "exclusive with <code>--compare-base</code> / <code>--coverag"
  & "e-delta</code>. Full detail (usage,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "properties, determinism, exit codes) is in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#the-sbom-subcommand-1"">The <code>sbom</code> subco"
  & "mmand</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""examples""><a class=""header"" href=""#examples"">Example"
  & "s</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash""># Self-assessment (strict m"
  & "ode, 100% docs required)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=."
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# ISO 26262 assessment at ASIL B (dedicated flag)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --asil=B"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# IEC 62304 assessment at safety Class A (dedicated flag)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --class=A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# ISO 26262 assessment at rigour tier C (ASIL B) via --stand"
  & "ard"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --standard=iso26262 --dal=C"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Emit badges for every standard at the shared tier"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --standard=all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Report toolchain + platform status"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex status --target=."
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Assess a CRDT library at DAL-C in relaxed mode"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=../Ada_CRDT --dal=C --relaxed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# DAL-A assessment (requires Gold SPARK)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --dal=A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Without SVG output"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=../Ada_CRDT --no-svg"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Custom skip dirs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=../Ada_CRDT --relaxed --skip-dir=vendor"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# With Markdown reports"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --emit-markdown=docs/compliance"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Web dashboard on custom port"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --serve --port=9090"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Differential assessment vs a git base revision"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex --target=. --compare-base=HEAD"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Proof-aware SBOM (CycloneDX 1.5 JSON; all standards by def"
  & "ault)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex sbom --format=cyclonedx-json --target=. --dal=C"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# SBOM for a single standard (ISO 26262 at ASIL B)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex sbom --format=cyclonedx-json --target=. --asil=B"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# SPDX 2.3 SBOM at IEC 62304 Class A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex sbom --format=spdx-json --target=. --class=A --out="
  & "sbom.spdx.json"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# Proof-aware SBOM (SPDX 2.3 JSON) at a custom path"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex sbom --format=spdx-json --out=docs/compliance/sbom."
  & "spdx.json"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""target-project-requirements""><a class=""header"" href="
  & """#target-project-requirements"">Target project requirements</"
  & "a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex assesses an <strong>Ada/SPARK project</strong>. "
  & "The target root can be the repository root or a subdirectory"
  & " (via <code>--target=PATH</code>). For a meaningful report, "
  & "the target must provide the items that follow. Any missing i"
  & "tem shows as <code>N/A</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>DAL checks that depend on the missing item report <code>U"
  & "nmet</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""what-the-target-provides""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
  & "hat-the-target-provides"">What the target provides</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Ada source files</strong> (<code>.ads</code>) und"
  & "er the target root &#8211; scanned for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subprogram declarations, docstrings, and HLR traceability ta"
  & "gs. See the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-docstring-spec.html"">docstring sp"
  & "ec</a> for the annotation"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "format and coverage rules.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>GNATprove output</strong> &#8211; a <code>gnatpro"
  & "ve.out</code> summary, discovered in this"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "order:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code><"
  & "/li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/gnatprove.out</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Or run <code>adacovex prove</code> (or the GitHub Action "
  & "with <code>prove: true</code>) to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "generate a fresh summary before you assess.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Test results</strong> &#8211; a test-summary file"
  & ", auto-discovered from a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "conventional name at the project root or under <code>docs/</"
  & "code> (for example"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>test_result.md</code>, <code>test_results.md</code>, <"
  & "code>test-result.md</code>, <code>tests.md</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>test_result.txt</code>, <code>test_results.log</code>,"
  & " <code>docs/test_result.md</code>, &#8230;)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Supported formats come from your runner&#8217;s log or a sum"
  & "mary file:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Markdown tables: the native <code>test_runner</code> lay"
  & "out"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>| Category | N | PASS |</code> and the AUnit-report la"
  & "yout"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>| - | Category | N | PASS |</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>TAP (<code>ok</code>/<code>not ok</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>GNU Automake (<code>PASS:</code>/<code>FAIL:</code>)</li"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Maven Surefire (<code>Tests run: N</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Unity (<code>N Tests M Failures</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>See the <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-test-format.html"">test"
  & " format spec</a> for the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "detailed rules (what each line looks like and which line win"
  & "s when formats"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "mix).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>HLR / LLR documents</strong> (for DAL assessment)"
  & " &#8211;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> and optio"
  & "nally"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/LLR.md</code>, followin"
  & "g the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-docstring-spec.html#hlr-traceabil"
  & "ity-tags"">HLR traceability-tag format</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""missing-data""><a class=""header"" href=""#missing-data"""
  & ">Missing data</a></h2>"
