  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""non-ada-projects""><a class=""header"" href=""#non-ada-p"
  & "rojects"">Non-Ada projects</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex currently targets Ada/SPARK sources. Non-Ada pro"
  & "jects (C/C++, Python,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JS, and more) that want the compliance/SBOM tooling provide "
  & "their own"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code> to man"
  & "age the Ada dependencies needed to build"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex itself. Running <code>adacovex</code> from such a r"
  & "epo scans it and uses its"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>We are working on support for other languages. Watch for "
  & "updates.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""vendored-code-and-strict-mode""><a class=""header"" hre"
  & "f=""#vendored-code-and-strict-mode"">Vendored code and strict "
  & "mode</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>By default (strict mode) adacovex scans and counts every "
  & "directory except the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "always-excluded ones. Vendored code is included. For third-p"
  & "arty code you"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cannot modify, use docstring <strong>patch files</strong> at"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;"
  & "</code> (see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#patch-system"">Architecture &#8211; Patch System</a"
  & ">). Or run in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "relaxed mode (<code>--relaxed</code>, skip dirs, no patches)"
  & " (see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relaxed mode</a>"
  & ").</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Vendored code can also take part in the <strong>SPARK pro"
  & "of</strong>. A patch carrying <code>SPARK_Mode</code> / <cod"
  & "e>Pre</code> / <code>Post</code> / <code>Global</code> aspec"
  & "ts is a <em>proof patch</em>. The <code>prove</code> subcomm"
  & "and merges it into a patched tree copy. The copy uses <code>"
  & ".ads</code> spec contracts and <code>.adb</code> body patche"
  & "s that opt a SPARK-clean vendored body into the proof.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>See <a href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"
  & """>Proving and writing proofs</a> for how to write them. See "
  & "<a href=""#proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-depend"
  & "encies"">Architecture &#8211; Proof patches</a> for the desig"
  & "n.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""web-dashboard-and-json-api""><a class=""header"" href="""
  & "#web-dashboard-and-json-api"">Web dashboard and JSON API</a><"
  & "/h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex --target=. --serve --port=8080</code> runs"
  & " the full assessment and then"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "starts a built-in HTTP/1.1 server (no external web stack) th"
  & "at serves a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>viewable HTML dashboard</strong> plus a machine-read"
  & "able JSON API and the SVG"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "badges. The server blocks until interrupted &#8211; run it i"
  & "n its own terminal, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "as a background process when scripting.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex --target=. --serve"
  & " --port=8080"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "# in another terminal:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "curl http://localhost:8080/api/metrics"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""how-to-use-the-dashboard""><a class=""header"" href=""#h"
  & "ow-to-use-the-dashboard"">How to use the dashboard</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> in a browser. The"
  & " page is a single self-contained"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "document (no external assets) with hash-routed tabs. Use the"
  & " header dropdown to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "switch themes (light / dark / system) and <strong>Save setti"
  & "ngs</strong> to persist your"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "choice.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""overview-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#overview-tab"""
  & ">Overview tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_overvi"
  & "ew.png"" alt=""Preview of Overview tab""><span class=""img-wrapp"
  & "er""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_overview.png"" alt="""
  & "Preview of Overview tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Start here. The <strong>Robustness tier</strong> (S / A /"
  & " B / C / D) is a single letter that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "summarises five quality axes: Docs, Proof, Tests, Compliance"
  & ", and Deps. An <strong>S</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "means the project is healthy across the board. A <strong>D</"
  & "strong> means one or more axes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "are below 50%. Below that:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>SPARK radar</strong> &#8211; proved verification"
  & " conditions per check category (flow,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "initialization, runtime, assertions, functional). A balanced"
  & " polygon means"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "every category has strong coverage. A spike in one corner an"
  & "d a flat line in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "another means the proof effort is uneven.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tests donut</strong> &#8211; passed vs failed te"
  & "sts. A full green arc means 100%"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "passing. Any red slice means the test suite has failures tha"
  & "t must be fixed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "before the project can be assessed as <code>Achieved</code>."
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Doc coverage donut</strong> &#8211; documented s"
  & "ubprograms as a percentage of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "total. Strict mode requires 100%. A shortfall here shows exa"
  & "ctly how many"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subprograms are missing <code>--</code> docstrings.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Dependency scope ring</strong> &#8211; the resol"
  & "ved graph broken down by scope"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(base / dev / transitive / vendored / system / test).  It si"
  & "ts in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same row as the doc-coverage donut so the Overview uses its "
  & "width well."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Each coloured segment is hoverable: hovering shows the scope"
  & " name and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "its component count (for example <code>test: 3</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Proof check bars scale with the category&#8217;s magnitud"
  & "e, the same way as the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "test-category bars: a 407-VC category reads as a longer bar "
  & "than a 56-VC"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "one, so relative proof effort is visible at a glance.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""proof-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-tab"">Proof"
  & " tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_proof."
  & "png"" alt=""Preview of Proof tab""><span class=""img-wrapper""><i"
  & "mg src=""../media/dashboard_preview_proof.png"" alt=""Preview o"
  & "f Proof tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Shows the SPARK level (Stone .. Platinum) and per-categor"
  & "y VC counts. The mini <strong>VCs proved / total</strong> at"
  & " the top is the headline number. Click into a category to se"
  & "e the breakdown.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>If a category is low, that is where the proof effort must"
  & " focus.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""tests-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#tests-tab"">Tests"
  & " tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_tests."
  & "png"" alt=""Preview of Tests tab""><span class=""img-wrapper""><i"
  & "mg src=""../media/dashboard_preview_tests.png"" alt=""Preview o"
  & "f Tests tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every test category with its count and Pass / Fail. A sin"
  & "gle failing category"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is enough to fail the compliance gate (<code>Tests passing</"
  & "code> must be <code>Yes</code> for every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tier except QM / DAL-E).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""compliance-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#compliance-"
  & "tab"">Compliance tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_compli"
  & "ance.png"" alt=""Preview of Compliance tab""><span class=""img-w"
  & "rapper""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_compliance.png"""
  & " alt=""Preview of Compliance tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Shows the target integrity level, overall <code>Achieved<"
  & "/code> / <code>Unmet</code>, HLRs traced,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "orphan-tag state, and every unmet criterion. Use this to ver"
  & "ify that every HLR"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is tagged in source and that no tags are orphaned (tagged bu"
  & "t not defined in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>HLR.md</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""dependencies-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#dependenc"
  & "ies-tab"">Dependencies tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_depend"
  & "encies.png"" alt=""Preview of Dependencies tab""><span class=""i"
  & "mg-wrapper""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_dependencie"
  & "s.png"" alt=""Preview of Dependencies tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>An interactive dependency tree (or diagram) of every comp"
  & "onent in the graph. Use the filter input and scope checkboxe"
  & "s to focus on base, dev, transitive, vendored, or system dep"
  & "endencies. Click a node to see its licence, PURL, parent, an"
  & "d a registry link. Use this tab to audit your supply chain: "
  & "confirm every vendored licence is compatible, see which syst"
  & "em tools the build needs (the <code>system</code> scope), an"
  & "d trace each component back to its source.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The diagram view (toggle <strong>Tree / Diagram</strong>)"
  & " renders the same graph as a directed diagram.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""charts-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#charts-tab"">Cha"
  & "rts tab</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"""
  & " type=""checkbox""><img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_charts"
  & ".png"" alt=""Preview of Charts tab""><span class=""img-wrapper"">"
  & "<img src=""../media/dashboard_preview_charts.png"" alt=""Previe"
  & "w of Charts tab""></span></label></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Six CSS-only cards (donut, column, bar, radial gauge, pie"
  & ", polar ring) that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "show the same data as the Overview tab in a different format"
  & ". Use this to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "compare SPARK proof, test results, doc coverage, and depende"
  & "ncy scope at a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "glance.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""interpreting-the-charts""><a class=""header"" href=""#in"
  & "terpreting-the-charts"">Interpreting the charts</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Green / full arcs</strong> &#8211; the metric is"
  & " at 100% or close to it.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Red slices or flat corners</strong> &#8211; ther"
  & "e is a regression or missing data.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Scope rings</strong> &#8211; a large vendored we"
  & "dge means strict-mode docstrings are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "being suppressed by patches. If you see no wedge, vendored c"
  & "ode can be"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "uncovered.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tier letter drops</strong> &#8211; a drop from <"
  & "code>A</code> to <code>C</code> means the average across all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "five axes fell. Check the axis table to see which one regres"
  & "sed.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The same data is available headlessly at <code>/api/metri"
  & "cs</code> and via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code> (<code>{""metrics"":..., ""dep"
  & "endencies"":...}</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Path</th><th>Content</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /</code></td><td>HTML dashboard (tabbed)</"
  & "td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/metrics</code></td><td>JSON object wi"
  & "th the key assessment metrics</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/deps</code></td><td>JSON dependency g"
  & "raph (same data as the Dependencies tab)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/endpoints</code></td><td>JSON endpoin"
  & "t catalog (the list the API playground builds its UI from)</"
  & "td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /docs</code></td><td>The bundled offline m"
  & "anual: the mdBook manual built into the binary (HTML, no ext"
  & "ernal assets)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/spark.svg</code></td><td>SPARK assu"
  & "rance level badge</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/tests.svg</code></td><td>Test pass/"
  & "fail badge</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/do178c.svg</code></td><td>DO-178C c"
  & "ompliance badge (Achieved / Unmet)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/iso26262.svg</code></td><td>ISO 262"
  & "62 compliance badge</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/iec62304.svg</code></td><td>IEC 623"
  & "04 compliance badge</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>anything else</td><td><code>404 Not Found</code></td"
  & "></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The server runs a small HTTP/1.1 implementation with a 4-"
  & "worker task pool"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(configurable with <code>--serve-workers=N</code>, which is "
  & "a related flag of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--serve</code>) and serves requests until the process "
  & "is interrupted (Ctrl-C)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Query strings and URL fragments are stripped before routing,"
  & " so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>/?theme=light</code>, <code>/api/metrics?x=1</code> an"
  & "d <code>/api/deps#top</code> reach the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "handlers as <code>/</code>, <code>/api/metrics</code> and <c"
  & "ode>/api/deps</code> instead of 404ing.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""bundled-offline-manual""><a class=""header"" href=""#bun"
  & "dled-offline-manual"">Bundled offline manual</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>--serve</code> server also serves the <strong>b"
  & "undled offline manual</strong> at <code>/docs</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(both spellings, with and without the trailing slash, reach "
  & "the same page)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The manual is the same Markdown source that powers the Read "
  & "the Docs site"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>docs/</code>, an mdBook project with <code>book.toml<"
  & "/code> and <code>SUMMARY.md</code>); at build"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "time <code>tools/gen-docs.py</code> runs <code>mdbook build<"
  & "/code> and inlines the resulting"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>print.html</code> into the binary (<code>src/adacovex-"
  & "docs_template.ads</code>), so the page"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is fully self-contained: stylesheets are inlined, external f"
  & "onts and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "interactive scripts are dropped, and the HTML stays pure ASC"
  & "II.  Users on a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "machine without a network connection can still open the manu"
  & "al from the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dashboard &#8211; the footer <strong>Manual</strong> link an"
  & "d the API playground&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>/docs</code> endpoint both point at it.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""the-html-dashboard""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-htm"
  & "l-dashboard"">The HTML dashboard</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The page is a single self-contained document (no external"
  & " assets), bundled"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "into the binary from <strong>modular resources</strong> &#82"
  & "11; <code>resources/dashboard.html</code> is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "just the page skeleton. Author styles and scripts are split "
  & "into focused"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "modules under <code>resources/css/</code> (<code>dashboard.c"
  & "ss</code>, which also styles the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hand-rolled donut rings and bar charts) and <code>resources/"
  & "js/</code> (<code>theme.js</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>tabs.js</code>, <code>deps.js</code>, <code>details.js"
  & "</code>, <code>nomnoml.js</code>, <code>search.js</code>, <c"
  & "ode>api.js</code>)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The vendored libraries (<code>graphre.js</code> / <code>nomn"
  & "oml.js</code> / <code>flexsearch.js</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>yace.js</code>) sit at <code>resources/</code>, clearl"
  & "y separate from the authored <code>js/</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "modules so a scan of the tree can tell dependency JavaScript"
  & " from dashboard"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JavaScript at a glance; they are inlined into the template a"
  & "t build time by"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code>, which also <strong>mini"
  & "fies</strong> the author CSS/JS"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(comments and whitespace stripped, vendored files are inline"
  & "d byte-for-byte"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "so their tokenizer regexes stay intact).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The resulting <code>adacovex</code> binary - whether a Gi"
  & "tHub release artifact or an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Alire crate binary - is completely self-contained. The dashb"
  & "oard has no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "external asset references and works offline.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Edit the individual <code>resources/</code> files, never "
  & "the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "generated <code>src/adacovex-dashboard_template.ads</code>. "
  & "<code>make build</code> regenerates it"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>gen-dashboard.py --check</code> (wired into <code>"
  & "make check</code>) fails when it"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "drifts.  Content is organised into <strong>clickable tabs</s"
  & "trong> (hash-routed,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "keyboard-accessible, persisted in <code>localStorage</code>)"
  & ":</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Overview</strong> &#8211; status badges (live <c"
  & "ode>/badge/*.svg</code> preview), source overview"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(packages scanned, subprograms, docstring %), and quick stat"
  & "s (SPARK level,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "VCs proved, tests, compliance, dependency count), plus the a"
  & "t-a-glance"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "collation charts below the stats: a <strong>Robustness radar"
  & " with a tier rating</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(S/A/B/C/D from the average of five quality axes), the per-c"
  & "heck-type"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>SPARK radar</strong>, a tests <strong>donut</strong>"
  & " and a doc-coverage <strong>radial gauge</strong>. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "badge row doubles as a preview for the generated <code>docs/"
  & "badges/*.svg</code> files."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "See <a href=""#robustness-tier"">Robustness tier</a> for how t"
  & "he rating is derived.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Proof</strong> &#8211; the SPARK level (Stone..P"
  & "latinum) and, per check category"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(flow, initialization, runtime, assertions, functional), tot"
  & "al and proved"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "counts plus a mini <strong>VCs proved/total</strong> column "
  & "at the top of the tab.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tests</strong> &#8211; every test category with "
  & "count and Pass/Fail plus a mini"
  & ASCII.LF
