  & "numbers as the full-size charts.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""standard-awareness""><a class=""header"" href=""#standar"
  & "d-awareness"">Standard-awareness</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Like the <code>sbom</code> subcommand, the dashboard <str"
  & "ong>defaults to all standards</strong> when"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "no <code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code> / <code>--c"
  & "lass</code> flag is given. The status badges and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the compliance card list every standard&#8217;s label at the"
  & " shared tier (DAL-C,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ASIL B, Class A). An explicit standard flag narrows the dash"
  & "board to that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "single standard (for example <code>--asil=B</code> shows onl"
  & "y ISO 26262 at ASIL B). See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#compliance-standards-do-178c--iso-26262--iec-62304"
  & """>Standards</a> for the cross-standard tier mapping.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""the-json-api""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-json-api"""
  & ">The JSON API</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>/api/metrics</code> is a plain HTTP GET, so scripts"
  & " and CI can consume the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "assessment without parsing HTML:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-json"">{""spark_level"":""Platinum"","""
  & "total_vcs"":723,""proved_vcs"":723,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & " ""tests_passed"":1173,""tests_failed"":0,""doc_coverage"":100,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & " ""standard"":""all"",""level"":""DAL-C"",""dal_status"":""Achieved"","
  & ASCII.LF
  & " ""standards"":{""DO-178C"":{""level"":""DAL-C"",""status"":""Achieved"""
  & "},"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "               ""ISO 26262"":{""level"":""ASIL B"",""status"":""Achie"
  & "ved""},"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "               ""IEC 62304"":{""level"":""Class A"",""status"":""Achi"
  & "eved""}}}"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>spark_level</code></td><td>Assessed SPARK leve"
  & "l (<code>Stone</code>..<code>Platinum</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>total_vcs</code> / <code>proved_vcs</code></td"
  & "><td>GNATprove verification-condition counts</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>tests_passed</code> / <code>tests_failed</code"
  & "></td><td>Test-result counts</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>doc_coverage</code></td><td>Docstring coverage"
  & ", 0-100</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>standard</code></td><td><code>do178c</code> | "
  & "<code>iso26262</code> | <code>iec62304</code> | <code>all</c"
  & "ode></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>level</code></td><td>Level label for the top-l"
  & "evel target (<code>DAL-C</code>, <code>ASIL B</code>, &#8230"
  & ";)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>dal_status</code></td><td><code>Achieved</code"
  & "> or <code>Unmet</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>standards</code></td><td>Per-standard <code>le"
  & "vel</code> / <code>status</code> object (present when <code>"
  & "standard</code> is <code>all</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>/api/deps</code> serves the resolved dependency gra"
  & "ph as JSON (the same data the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SBOM embeds, minus the SBOM envelope):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-json"">[{""name"":""gnat_arm_elf"",""ve"
  & "rsion"":""13.2.1"",""scope"":""dev"","
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  ""parent"":""adacovex"",""kind"":""dependency"",""purl"":""pkg:generi"
  & "c/gnat_arm_elf@13.2.1"","
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  ""lang"":"""",""website"":"""",""description"":""System tool referenc"
  & "ed by the project (dev dependency)""},"
  & ASCII.LF
  & " ...]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>name</code> / <code>version</code></td><td>Com"
  & "ponent name and version</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td><code>base</code> | <code"
  & ">dev</code> | <code>transitive</code> | <code>vendored</code"
  & "> | <code>system</code> (a system tool is a <code>system</co"
  & "de>-scope dependency with a <code>pkg:generic/*</code> PURL)"
  & "</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>parent</code></td><td>Parent component name (<"
  & "code>(root)</code> for the root, or the index as <code>0</co"
  & "de>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>kind</code></td><td><code>root</code> or <code"
  & ">dependency</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>purl</code></td><td>Package URL when derivable"
  & "</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>lang</code></td><td>Primary language when know"
  & "n</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>website</code></td><td>Resolved source URL whe"
  & "n known</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>Short description ("
  & "for example a system-tool note) when present</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>On-disk, the same export is available via <code>--emit-me"
  & "trics=PATH</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>{""metrics"": {...}, ""dependencies"": [...]}</code> afte"
  & "r any assessment).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""api-playground""><a class=""header"" href=""#api-playgro"
  & "und"">API playground</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <strong>API</strong> tab turns the dashboard into a s"
  & "mall interactive REST client."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Every route the server dispatches on is listed as a clickabl"
  & "e button,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "grouped by purpose:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Metrics</strong> &#8211; <code>GET /api/metrics<"
  & "/code> (JSON).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Dependencies</strong> &#8211; <code>GET /api/dep"
  & "s</code> (JSON).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Badges</strong> &#8211; each <code>GET /badge/*."
  & "svg</code> endpoint (SVG).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Documentation</strong> &#8211; <code>GET /docs</"
  & "code>, the bundled offline manual (HTML).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>API</strong> &#8211; <code>GET /api/endpoints</c"
  & "ode>, the endpoint catalog the playground is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "built from.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A filter input searches the endpoints as you type (matchi"
  & "ng path, purpose,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and group name), so you can jump straight to <code>metrics</"
  & "code> or <code>badge</code>. Clicking"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "an endpoint issues a live <code>fetch</code> against the ser"
  & "ving origin and previews"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the response:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>JSON endpoints are pretty-printed (two-space indent) and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>syntax-highlighted</strong> with the vendored <a hre"
  & "f=""https://github.com/petersolopov/yace"">yace</a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tokenizer (<code>window.YaceTok</code>). A JSON-key rule col"
  & "ours object keys"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "separately from string values, so the payload reads like an "
  & "IDE view."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Endpoint paths that appear inside the JSON payload (for exam"
  & "ple the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>/api/...</code> and <code>/badge/...</code> values in "
  & "<code>/api/endpoints</code>) become clickable"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "links to the live endpoints, and every endpoint button&#8217"
  & ";s path is itself a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "link that opens the raw URL in a new tab.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>SVG badge endpoints show the live image above the raw ma"
  & "rkup.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The <code>/docs</code> endpoint shows the bundled offlin"
  & "e manual (the same page the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "footer <strong>Manual</strong> link opens).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A toolbar on the result offers <strong>Copy</strong> (cli"
  & "pboard) and <strong>Download</strong> (saves"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the raw response body to a file) for the JSON API response, "
  & "so the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "playground doubles as a lightweight HTTP client without leav"
  & "ing the browser."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The first endpoint (<code>/api/metrics</code>) runs automati"
  & "cally so the tab always"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "opens with a live preview. The endpoint list is <strong>not "
  & "hardcoded</strong> in client"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JavaScript: the playground fetches it from <code>GET /api/en"
  & "dpoints</code>, the single"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "source of truth the server declares. Each request is made li"
  & "ve against the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "instance, so what you preview is exactly what <code>curl</co"
  & "de> returns.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""themes""><a class=""header"" href=""#themes"">Themes</a><"
  & "/h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The dashboard supports <strong>light</strong>, <strong>da"
  & "rk</strong>, and <strong>system</strong> themes. Colours are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "driven by CSS custom properties, and a header dropdown switc"
  & "hes live between"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "them. <strong>Save settings</strong> persists the current se"
  & "lection in <code>localStorage</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(no cookies, key <code>adacovex-theme</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Theme resolution on page load:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>a <code>?theme=light|dark|system</code> query parameter "
  & "on the dashboard URL."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "It always wins. This is the supported way to pin the theme w"
  & "hen embedding"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the dashboard in an iframe. The server strips the query stri"
  & "ng before"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "routing, so <code>http://localhost:8080/?theme=light</code> "
  & "(and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>?theme=dark</code> / <code>?theme=system</code>) serve"
  & "s the themed dashboard instead of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "404ing.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>otherwise the explicit CLI theme (<code>--theme=light</c"
  & "ode> / <code>--theme=dark</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>otherwise the saved <code>localStorage</code> choice, if"
  & " one was saved.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>otherwise the system theme (<code>prefers-color-scheme</"
  & "code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--theme</code> only sets the <em>initial</em> selec"
  & "tion. The dropdown and Save settings"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "still override it afterwards in the browser.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""related-cli-flags""><a class=""header"" href=""#related-"
  & "cli-flags"">Related CLI flags</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--serve</code></td><td>off</td><td>Run the pip"
  & "eline, then spawn the HTTP dashboard server (blocking) on th"
  & "e port. It is a switch: passing <code>--serve</code> is the "
  & "only way to start the server, and omitting it (the default, "
  & "<code>off</code>) renders and exits without serving. There i"
  & "s no <code>--no-serve</code>, because a flag already control"
  & "s it</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--port=N</code></td><td><code>8080</code></td>"
  & "<td>Server port (a valid <code>Positive</code> integer)</td>"
  & "</tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--serve-workers=N</code></td><td><code>4</code"
  & "></td><td>HTTP server task-pool worker count for <code>--ser"
  & "ve</code> (a valid <code>Positive</code> integer, capped at "
  & "256). Only relevant with <code>--serve</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--theme=NAME</code></td><td><code>system</code"
  & "></td><td>Initial dashboard theme: <code>light</code> | <cod"
  & "e>dark</code> | <code>system</code> (case-insensitive)</td><"
  & "/tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""the-sbom-subcommand-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-"
  & "sbom-subcommand-1"">The <code>sbom</code> subcommand</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""when-and-why-to-generate-an-sbom""><a class=""header"" "
  & "href=""#when-and-why-to-generate-an-sbom"">When and why to gen"
  & "erate an SBOM</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) is a structured inven"
  & "tory of every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "component in your project, plus its provenance, licence, and"
  & " (in adacovex&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "case) its SPARK proof level and compliance context. Generate"
  & " one in these"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cases:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Auditing or certifying</strong> &#8211; an SBOM "
  & "is a standard artifact for safety"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "certification (DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62304). It shows the "
  & "auditor exactly"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "which Ada/Alire components are in scope and which are proved"
  & " / not proved.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Shifting left on supply-chain security</strong> "
  & "&#8211; the dependency graph exposes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "transitive dependencies, their licences, and their PURLs so "
  & "you can review"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "them before a release.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Embedding in CI</strong> &#8211; the proof-aware"
  & " SBOM carries the assessed standard and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "level, so downstream tooling (policy engines, compliance das"
  & "hboards) can"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "consume it without re-parsing markdown reports.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Reproducible builds</strong> &#8211; adacovex ho"
  & "nours <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code>, so the SBOM"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "timestamp is deterministic when tied to a git commit.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex sbom</code> resolves the target project&#8"
  & "217;s dependency graph from its Alire"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest (<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</co"
  & "de>), the solved-crate list in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire/alire.lock</code>, and the root <code>.gpr</code"
  & "> <code>with</code> clauses, then writes a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof-aware software bill of materials in CycloneDX 1.5 JSON"
  & ", SPDX 2.3 JSON,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "or Markdown.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""how-to-read-the-output""><a class=""header"" href=""#how"
  & "-to-read-the-output"">How to read the output</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Choose the format that matches your toolchain:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>CycloneDX 1.5 JSON</strong> (<code>--format=cycl"
  & "onedx-json</code>) &#8211; drop into any CycloneDX"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "consumer (Dependency-Track, OWASP Dependency-Check, and more"
  & "). The root"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "component"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "carries <code>adacovex:proof_level</code>, <code>adacovex:st"
  & "andard</code>, <code>adacovex:dal_target</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>adacovex:level</code>. Every dependency has a <cod"
  & "e>language</code> field inferred from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "file extensions or declared ecosystems.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>SPDX 2.3 JSON</strong> (<code>--format=spdx-json"
  & "</code>) &#8211; compatible with SPDX-aware tools"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(FOSSA, Snyk, ScanCode). The adacovex properties appear as"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>attributionTexts</code> on the root package.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Markdown</strong> (<code>--format=md</code>) &#8"
  & "211; human-readable table, useful for audits and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "reports. Default path is <code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/complianc"
  & "e/SBOM.md</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""key-fields""><a class=""header"" href=""#key-fields"">Key"
  & " fields</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Where it appears</th><th>Meaning</th><"
  & "/tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:proof_level</code></td><td>Root compo"
  & "nent</td><td>Assessed SPARK level (<code>Stone</code> .. <co"
  & "de>Platinum</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:standard</code></td><td>Root componen"
  & "t</td><td>Compliance standard (<code>DO-178C</code>, <code>I"
  & "SO 26262</code>, <code>IEC 62304</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:dal_target</code></td><td>Root compon"
  & "ent</td><td>Shared rigour tier (<code>DAL-A</code> .. <code>"
  & "DAL-E</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:level</code></td><td>Root component</"
  & "td><td>Standard-specific label (<code>DAL-C</code>, <code>AS"
  & "IL B</code>, <code>Class A</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>language</code></td><td>Every component</td><t"
  & "d>Implementation language(s) inferred from file extensions</"
  & "td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>purl</code></td><td>Every component</td><td>Pa"
  & "ckage URL for registry linking</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Dependencies report <code>adacovex:proof_level = ""Not pro"
  & "ved""</code> because adacovex only"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proves the target itself. The SBOM is mutually exclusive wit"
  & "h <code>--compare-base</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>--coverage-delta</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""usage-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#usage-1"">Usage</a>"
  & "</h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>adacovex sbom [--format=cyclonedx-json|spdx-json|"
  & "md] [--out=PATH]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "           [--standard=NAME|--dal=LEVEL|--asil=LEVEL|--class"
  & "=LEVEL]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Default output</strong>: <code>&lt;target&gt;/sb"
  & "om.json</code> for <code>cyclonedx-json</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/sbom.spdx.json</code> for <code>spdx-js"
  & "on</code>, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/SBOM.md</code> for <cod"
  & "e>md</code>. The containing directory is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "created automatically.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Exit code</strong>: <code>0</code> when the SBOM"
  & " was written, <code>1</code> otherwise. If the target"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "has no Alire manifest the SBOM cannot be generated (the GitH"
  & "ub Action"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "reports this as a warning without failing the job).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""standard-awareness-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#stand"
  & "ard-awareness-1"">Standard-awareness</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>sbom</code> subcommand accepts the same standar"
  & "d flags as the assessment"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>--standard</code>, <code>--dal</code>, <code>--asil</"
  & "code>, <code>--class</code>) and <strong>defaults to all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "standards</strong>: without an explicit standard flag the SB"
  & "OM carries the joined"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "DO-178C / ISO 26262 / IEC 62304 properties at the shared DAL"
  & " tier."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--standard=iso26262</code> / <code>--asil=B</code> nar"
  & "rows it to ISO 26262 at ASIL B, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--class=A</code> to IEC 62304 at Class A. See <a href="
  & """#compliance-standards-do-178c--iso-26262--iec-62304"">Standa"
  & "rds</a> for the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cross-standard tier mapping.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""properties""><a class=""header"" href=""#properties"">Pro"
  & "perties</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Only the root component &#8211; the project adacovex actu"
  & "ally assessed &#8211; carries:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex:proof_level</code> &#8211; <code>Stone</c"
  & "ode>..<code>Platinum</code>, the honest assessed level.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex:standard</code> &#8211; <code>DO-178C</co"
  & "de> / <code>ISO 26262</code> / <code>IEC 62304</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex:dal_target</code> &#8211; <code>DAL-A</co"
  & "de>..<code>DAL-D</code> (omitted for <code>DAL-E</code>).</l"
  & "i>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex:level</code> &#8211; the standard-specifi"
  & "c label (<code>DAL-C</code> / <code>ASIL B</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Class A</code>, omitted for <code>DAL-E</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Dependency components report <code>adacovex:proof_level ="
  & " ""Not proved""</code> (adacovex"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "only proves the target itself, never third-party dependencie"
  & "s). Properties are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "encoded as <code>attributionTexts</code> in SPDX.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""determinism""><a class=""header"" href=""#determinism"">D"
  & "eterminism</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>metadata.timestamp</code> / <code>creationInfo."
  & "created</code> field honors the <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</cod"
  & "e> environment variable (reproducible-builds convention). Wh"
  & "en set to a Unix epoch second count, the timestamp is derive"
  & "d from it in UTC via pure integer math. As a result, SBOM ou"
  & "tput is byte-for-byte deterministic across runs and machines"
  & ". To tie it to a specific git commit, run <code>export SOURC"
  & "E_DATE_EPOCH=$(git -C &lt;target&gt; log -1 --format=%ct)</c"
  & "ode> before adacovex.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The bundled <code>make</code> targets (<code>run-self</co"
  & "de>, <code>run-ada-crdt</code>, <code>prove</code>, <code>re"
  & "lease</code>, and Ada_CRDT&#8217;s <code>prove</code>/<code>"
  & "badges</code>) already set it from the target&#8217;s git <c"
  & "ode>HEAD</code> commit time.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""exclusivity-and-ordering""><a class=""header"" href=""#e"
  & "xclusivity-and-ordering"">Exclusivity and ordering</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>sbom</code> is mutually exclusive with <code>--comp"
  & "are-base</code> and <code>--coverage-delta</code>. It"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scans sources, parses proof/test results, and assesses DAL f"
  & "irst. As a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "result, the emitted properties reflect the real assessment s"
  & "tate.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Both formats validate against the official"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://github.com/CycloneDX/specification"">Cyclone"
  & "DX 1.5</a> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://spdx.dev"">SPDX 2.3</a> JSON schemas (see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.html"">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a"
  & ">).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""language-detection""><a class=""header"" href=""#languag"
  & "e-detection"">Language detection</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every dependency component carries a <code>language</code"
  & "> field (CycloneDX JSON /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>components[].properties</code> under <code>""name"": ""ad"
  & "acovex:language""</code>, or the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Markdown table&#8217;s <code>Language</code> column) describ"
  & "ing the implementation language(s)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "of that dependency.  Detection follows the component&#8217;s"
  & " origin, most specific"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "first.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""manifest-declared-ecosystems""><a class=""header"" href"
  & "=""#manifest-declared-ecosystems"">Manifest-declared ecosystem"
  & "s</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A vendored manifest maps directly onto its language and P"
  & "URL type:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Manifest file</th><th>PURL type</th><th>Language</th"
  & "></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>package.json</code></td><td><code>pkg:npm</cod"
  & "e></td><td>JavaScript</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Cargo.toml</code></td><td><code>pkg:cargo</cod"
  & "e></td><td>Rust</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>go.mod</code></td><td><code>pkg:golang</code><"
  & "/td><td>Go</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>pyproject.toml</code></td><td><code>pkg:pypi</"
  & "code></td><td>Python</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>requirements*.txt</code></td><td><code>pkg:pyp"
  & "i</code></td><td>Python</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>composer.json</code></td><td><code>pkg:compose"
  & "r</code></td><td>PHP</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Gemfile</code></td><td><code>pkg:gem</code></t"
  & "d><td>Ruby</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>pom.xml</code></td><td><code>pkg:maven</code><"
  & "/td><td>Java</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Package.swift</code></td><td><code>pkg:swift</"
  & "code></td><td>Swift</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Alire manifest</td><td><code>pkg:alire</code></td><t"
  & "d>Ada</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>.gpr</code> project file</td><td><code>pkg:gpr"
  & "</code></td><td>Ada</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""extension-based-inference""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
  & "extension-based-inference"">Extension-based inference</a></h3"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For every other component &#8211; vendored trees, <code>v"
  & "endor/</code>, <code>node_modules</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resources, loose source drops, and individual files inside <"
  & "code>resources/</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>assets/</code>, and <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> &#"
  & "8211; adacovex infers the language from the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>file extensions actually present</strong>.  The exte"
  & "nsion is the source of truth: a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.py</code> file reports Python even when a <code>Cargo"
  & ".toml</code> sits next to it, and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest language only breaks ties.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Supported extensions:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Ada</strong>: <code>.ads</code>, <code>.adb</cod"
  & "e>, <code>.ada</code>, <code>.gpr</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>JavaScript</strong>: <code>.js</code>, <code>.mj"
  & "s</code>, <code>.cjs</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>TypeScript</strong>: <code>.ts</code>, <code>.ts"
  & "x</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>CSS</strong>: <code>.css</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>HTML</strong>: <code>.html</code>, <code>.htm</c"
  & "ode></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Python</strong>: <code>.py</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Go</strong>: <code>.go</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Rust</strong>: <code>.rs</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>C</strong>: <code>.c</code>, <code>.h</code></li"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>C++</strong>: <code>.cpp</code>, <code>.cc</code"
  & ">, <code>.cxx</code>, <code>.hpp</code>, <code>.hh</code>, <"
  & "code>.hxx</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>C#</strong>: <code>.cs</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Java</strong>: <code>.java</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Ruby</strong>: <code>.rb</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>PHP</strong>: <code>.php</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Swift</strong>: <code>.swift</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Kotlin</strong>: <code>.kt</code>, <code>.kts</c"
  & "ode></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Scala</strong>: <code>.scala</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>OCaml</strong>: <code>.ml</code>, <code>.mli</co"
  & "de></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Lua</strong>: <code>.lua</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Perl</strong>: <code>.pl</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Haskell</strong>: <code>.hs</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Elixir</strong>: <code>.ex</code>, <code>.exs</c"
  & "ode></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Erlang</strong>: <code>.erl</code>, <code>.hrl</"
  & "code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Clojure</strong>: <code>.clj</code>, <code>.cljs"
  & "</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Dart</strong>: <code>.dart</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Shell</strong>: <code>.sh</code>, <code>.bash</c"
  & "ode></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>PowerShell</strong>: <code>.ps1</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>SQL</strong>: <code>.sql</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Fortran</strong>: <code>.f</code>, <code>.f90</c"
  & "ode>, <code>.f95</code>, <code>.f03</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Assembly</strong>: <code>.s</code>, <code>.asm</"
  & "code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>R</strong>: <code>.r</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Julia</strong>: <code>.jl</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Zig</strong>: <code>.zig</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>VHDL</strong>: <code>.vhd</code>, <code>.vhdl</c"
  & "ode></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tcl</strong>: <code>.tcl</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A directory that mixes languages reports its <strong>top "
  & "3</strong> languages by file count"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(for example <code>""Ada; C; C++""</code>), so a mixed-languag"
  & "e vendored drop is summarised"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by what it actually contains rather than by a single guess.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""licence-resolution""><a class=""header"" href=""#licence"
  & "-resolution"">Licence resolution</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Vendored manifest ecosystems report their licence from th"
  & "e local manifest:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>package.json</code> (<code>license</code>) for npm/pnp"
  & "m, <code>Cargo.toml</code> for cargo,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>pyproject.toml</code> / <code>composer.json</code> for"
  & " pypi / composer. When the local"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest carries no licence, adacovex resolves the version, "
  & "website, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "licence from the package registry as a best-effort, online f"
  & "allback. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resolver dispatches on the ecosystem (the PURL type) through"
  & " a single static"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "table, so adding a language is one row rather than a new cod"
  & "e path:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>npm</strong> &#8211; <code>npm view &lt;pkg&gt; "
  & "version license homepage --json</code>, parsed for the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "three fields from one JSON object.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>pnpm</strong> &#8211; <code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt"
  & "; version license homepage --json</code>, likewise.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>cargo</strong> (Rust) &#8211; <code>cargo search"
  & " &lt;pkg&gt;</code>, with the SPDX id read from the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>(license: ...)</code> token in the output.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>go</strong> and other ecosystems with no portabl"
  & "e, reliable registry query keep"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "an empty licence; the vendored manifest scanner still reads "
  & "any in-repo"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "licence file for them.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The npm and pnpm rows answer for all three fields with a "
  & "single <code>--json</code> call,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "so each component boots node once instead of once per field "
  & "&#8211; a 3x reduction"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "in subprocess starts that keeps the graph build responsive o"
  & "n vendored"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JavaScript trees. The fallback runs only when the offline re"
  & "ad finds nothing,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "so a vendored package that ships a licence never touches the"
  & " network. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resolved licence flows into every SBOM format (CycloneDX <co"
  & "de>licenses</code>, SPDX"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>licenseConcluded</code> / <code>licenseDeclared</code>"
  & ", Markdown <code>License</code> column) and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dashboard detail panel; the resolved version and website app"
  & "ear in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dashboard detail panel and the <code>/api/deps</code> JSON.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The resolver caches each answer in a per-project store un"
  & "der the project&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "result cache (the same <code>--cache-dir</code> the scan use"
  & "s), keyed by the target"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory as well as the ecosystem and package name, with a "
  & "7-day TTL, the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same scheme as the system-tool version probes.  The content-"
  & "addressed result"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cache does not cover these registry calls (each one boots no"
  & "de for npm/pnpm),"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "so without this layer a warm run still re-paid them; the met"
  & "a cache makes every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "repeat run serve the licence, version, and website from disk"
  & " with no subprocess"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "spawn, and two projects that share a cache directory never s"
  & "erve each other&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resolved licence or version.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Bundled dashboard assets (FlexSearch, nomnoml, graphre) r"
  & "esolve"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "their licence and website live from the package registry whe"
  & "n a loose vendored"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "copy is scanned, preferring <code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt; lice"
  & "nse</code> and falling back to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>npm</code>, <code>yarn</code>, then <code>bun</code> &"
  & "#8211; the same preference chain as every JavaScript"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "component (see <a href=""#licence-resolution"">Licence resolut"
  & "ion</a>).  The SBOM and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Credits tab therefore track the real upstream licence instea"
  & "d of a hard-coded"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "copy.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""system-dependencies""><a class=""header"" href=""#system"
  & "-dependencies"">System dependencies</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> scans the project&#"
  & "8217;s build and dev files (Makefiles,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "shell scripts, Python tools, CI workflows, GPR files, Ada so"
  & "urces) for a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "curated set of known system binaries, then keeps only the to"
  & "ols that are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "installed on <code>PATH</code>. Each becomes a <code>system<"
  & "/code>-scope component of the root with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a <code>pkg:generic/&lt;name&gt;</code> PURL, a resolved <co"
  & "de>version</code> (from <code>&lt;tool&gt; --version</code>)"
  & ","
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and no external link or licence &#8211; by design adacovex p"
  & "rovisions only the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "version for system tools and never guesses a repository or l"
  & "icence for them."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>system</code> is a first-class dependency scope, disti"
  & "nct from <code>base</code>, <code>dev</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>transitive</code>, <code>vendored</code>, and <code>te"
  & "st</code>; the dashboard gives it its own filter"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "checkbox, badge colour, and legend entry, and the SBOM lists"
  & " it under"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>system</code> scope.  The dashboard marks these with a"
  & " <code>system</code> scope badge and a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "note in the detail panel.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The result shows up in the dashboard Dependency tab (per-"
  & "dependency detail"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "popup) and in every SBOM renderer: CycloneDX <code>component"
  & "s[].language</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SPDX/JSON <code>adacovex:language</code> property, and the M"
  & "arkdown table&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Language</code> column.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""test-dependencies""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-dep"
  & "endencies"">Test dependencies</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A dependency used only by the project&#8217;s tests is cl"
  & "assified <code>test</code> (the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> property value <code>""test""<"
  & "/code>).  adacovex recognises"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "test-only declarations in every supported ecosystem&#8217;s "
  & "manifest, in addition"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to the Alire <code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> sections and t"
  & "est project files:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Manifest file</th><th>Test label</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>package.json</code></td><td>a dependency secti"
  & "on whose key contains <code>test</code> (for example <code>t"
  & "estDependencies</code> or <code>devTestDependencies</code>);"
  & " a name whose last segment starts or ends with <code>test</c"
  & "ode> (for example <code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>vites"
  & "t</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Cargo.toml</code></td><td>the <code>[dev-depen"
  & "dencies]</code> section (Cargo&#8217;s test-only section); a"
  & "ny section whose name contains <code>test</code> (for exampl"
  & "e <code>[target.'cfg(test)'.dependencies]</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>go.mod</code></td><td>no native test-only sect"
  & "ion: the name heuristic is the signal (a module path whose l"
  & "ast path segment starts or ends with <code>test</code>, for "
  & "example <code>github.com/stretchr/testify</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>composer.json</code></td><td>the <code>require"
  & "-dev</code> section</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Gemfile</code></td><td>gems inside a <code>gro"
  & "up :test</code> block (any group name containing <code>test<"
  & "/code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>pom.xml</code></td><td><code>&lt;dependency&gt"
  & ";</code> blocks whose <code>&lt;scope&gt;</code> is <code>te"
  & "st</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>pyproject.toml</code></td><td>optional-depende"
  & "ncies extras whose name contains <code>test</code> (for exam"
  & "ple the <code>test</code> extra); Poetry sections such as <c"
  & "ode>[tool.poetry.group.test.dependencies]</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Package.swift</code></td><td>dependencies decl"
  & "ared inside a <code>.testTarget(...)</code> block</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>requirements*.txt</code></td><td>no native tes"
  & "t section: the name heuristic is the signal</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A vendored component (for example a package under <code>n"
  & "ode_modules</code> or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>vendor/</code>) is classified <code>test</code> when t"
  & "he project manifest that owns the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendor directory declares it under one of these test labels,"
  & " or when its"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "name carries the test label.  The name heuristic works acros"
  & "s every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "supported ecosystem &#8211; not just npm: it checks the full"
  & " name and then the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "last segment after any <code>/</code> or <code>:</code>, so "
  & "<code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>test-case</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>github.com/stretchr/testify</code> and <code>org.testn"
  & "g:testng</code> are all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "test-labelled.  The heuristic also applies to <strong>lockfi"
  & "le-resolved names</strong>:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> / <code>package-lock.json</code>"
  & " / <code>yarn.lock</code> entries next to an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "owner <code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code> cra"
  & "te names, and <code>alire.lock</code> crates"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that the manifest sets leave transitive.  The e2e fixture&#8"
  & "217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>@playwright/test</code> is the canonical example: it s"
  & "tays a <code>devDependencies</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "entry of <code>tests/e2e/package.json</code> (and a <code>pn"
  & "pm-lock.yaml</code> entry) and is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "classified <code>test</code> by name.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""compliance-standards-do-178c--iso-26262--iec-62304"">"
  & "<a class=""header"" href=""#compliance-standards-do-178c--iso-2"
  & "6262--iec-62304"">Compliance Standards (DO-178C / ISO 26262 /"
  & " IEC 62304)</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""what-are-these-standards""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
  & "hat-are-these-standards"">What are these standards?</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>DO-178C</strong> is the avionics software standar"
  & "d. It defines how to design,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "implement, verify, and certify software that flies airplanes"
  & ". Every line of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "safety-critical flight software is assessed at one of five <"
  & "strong>DAL</strong> (Development"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Assurance Level) tiers, from <strong>DAL-E</strong> (no safe"
  & "ty effect) to <strong>DAL-A</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(catastrophic failure can bring down the aircraft).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>ISO 26262</strong> is the automotive functional-s"
  & "afety standard. It applies the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "rigor to road-vehicle software (braking, steering, powertrai"
  & "n). Its integrity"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "levels are called <strong>ASIL</strong> (Automotive Safety I"
  & "ntegrity Level), from <strong>QM</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(quality management, no hazard) to <strong>ASIL D</strong> ("
  & "highest hazard).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>IEC 62304</strong> is the medical-device software"
  & " lifecycle standard. It classifies"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "software into <strong>safety classes</strong> A, B, and C ba"
  & "sed on the severity of harm a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "failure can cause.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>All three demand the same underlying evidence:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> &#8211; every "
  & "high-level requirement (HLR) is traced"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by a <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code> tag in source.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>No orphan tags</strong> &#8211; every tag in sou"
  & "rce maps to a defined HLR.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tests passing</strong> &#8211; the test suite ha"
  & "s zero failures (except at the lowest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tier).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> &#8211; the formal-"
  & "proof bar for the selected rigor tier.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex computes all four checks once and re-labels the "
  & "result per standard."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The same inputs feed the same outputs. Only the integrity-le"
  & "vel label changes.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""when-to-use-which-standard""><a class=""header"" href="""
  & "#when-to-use-which-standard"">When to use which standard</a><"
  & "/h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Domain</th><th>Standard</th><th>CLI flag</th><th>Lev"
  & "els</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Avionics</td><td>DO-178C</td><td><code>--dal=</code>"
  & "</td><td>A, B, C, D, E</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Automotive</td><td>ISO 26262</td><td><code>--asil=</"
  & "code></td><td>A, B, C, D, QM</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Medical</td><td>IEC 62304</td><td><code>--class=</co"
  & "de></td><td>A, B, C</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>If your project targets multiple domains, <code>--standar"
  & "d=all</code> runs one assessment"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and emits badges and reports for every standard without re-s"
  & "canning.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""what-the-rigor-tiers-mean""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
  & "what-the-rigor-tiers-mean"">What the rigor tiers mean</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Rigor tier</th><th>DO-178C</th><th>ISO 26262</th><th"
  & ">IEC 62304</th><th>Min SPARK</th><th>Tests</th><th>HLRs</th>"
  & "</tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Catastrophic</td><td>DAL A</td><td>ASIL D</td><td>Cl"
  & "ass C</td><td>Gold</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Hazardous</td><td>DAL B</td><td>ASIL C</td><td>Class"
  & " B</td><td>Silver</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Major</td><td>DAL C</td><td>ASIL B</td><td>Class A</"
  & "td><td>Bronze</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Minor</td><td>DAL D</td><td>ASIL A</td><td>&#8211;</"
  & "td><td>Stone</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>No safety effect</td><td>DAL E</td><td>QM</td><td>&#"
  & "8211;</td><td>&#8211;</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The tier placement is a per-project policy choice. The st"
  & "andards do not define a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "one-to-one correspondence. adacovex&#8217;s default mapping "
  & "is shown above. Use"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--standard=NAME</code> to select the labelling standar"
  & "d. Use <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> to pin"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the shared rigor tier.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""rigor-tier-mapping""><a class=""header"" href=""#rigor-t"
  & "ier-mapping"">Rigor-tier mapping</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Rigor tier</th><th>DO-178C</th><th>ISO 26262</th><th"
  & ">IEC 62304</th><th>Min SPARK</th><th>Tests</th><th>HLRs</th>"
  & "</tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Catastrophic</td><td>DAL A</td><td>ASIL D</td><td>Cl"
  & "ass C</td><td>Gold</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Hazardous</td><td>DAL B</td><td>ASIL C</td><td>Class"
  & " B</td><td>Silver</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Major</td><td>DAL C</td><td>ASIL B</td><td>Class A</"
  & "td><td>Bronze</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Minor</td><td>DAL D</td><td>ASIL A</td><td>&#8211;</"
  & "td><td>Stone</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>No safety effect</td><td>DAL E</td><td>QM</td><td>&#"
  & "8211;</td><td>&#8211;</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The exact tier placement of each standard&#8217;s levels "
  & "is a per-project policy"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "choice. The standards do not define a one-to-one corresponde"
  & "nce. The table"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "above is adacovex&#8217;s default mapping. <code>--standard="
  & "NAME</code> selects the labelling"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "standard. <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> pins the shared rigor tie"
  & "r (see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#implementation"">Implementation</a>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""assessment-criteria-shared""><a class=""header"" href="""
  & "#assessment-criteria-shared"">Assessment criteria (shared)</a"
  & "></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The four checks stay identical across standards. Only the"
  & " names change:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> &#8211; every "
  & "HLR defined in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> is traced by a <code>-- "
  & "HLR-XXXX</code> tag in source.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>No orphan tags</strong> &#8211; every in-source "
  & "HLR maps to a defined HLR.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Tests passing</strong> &#8211; zero failures (no"
  & "t enforced at the lowest tier).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> &#8211; the proof b"
  & "ar for the selected rigor tier.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Because the checks are shared, <strong>the compliance art"
  & "ifacts are identical too</strong>:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ISO 26262 and IEC 62304 require no different evidence or doc"
  & "uments than"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "DO-178C. The same inputs (<code>HLR.md</code>, source tracea"
  & "bility, proof summary, test"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "summary) feed the same outputs (<code>VERIFICATION.md</code>"
  & ", <code>TRACE.md</code>, the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof-aware SBOM, and the compliance SVG badges) for every s"
  & "tandard. Only the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "integrity-level label printed inside them changes (<code>DAL"
  & "-C</code>, <code>ASIL B</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Class A</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""selecting-a-standard-on-the-cli""><a class=""header"" h"
  & "ref=""#selecting-a-standard-on-the-cli"">Selecting a standard "
  & "on the CLI</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Each standard has a dedicated level flag, so your intent "
  & "is unambiguous on the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "command line (full flag details in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#adacovex-cli-reference"">CLI reference</a>). The fl"
  & "ags all resolve to the same shared"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "rigor tier:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Standard</th><th>Flag</th><th>Levels</th><th>Example"
  & " (tier)</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>DO-178C</td><td><code>--dal=</code></td><td>A, B, C,"
  & " D, E</td><td><code>--dal=C</code> -&gt; DAL-C (Major)</td><"
  & "/tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>ISO 26262</td><td><code>--asil=</code></td><td>A, B,"
  & " C, D, QM</td><td><code>--asil=B</code> -&gt; ASIL B (Major)"
  & "</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>IEC 62304</td><td><code>--class=</code></td><td>A, B"
  & ", C</td><td><code>--class=A</code> -&gt; Class A (Major)</td"
  & "></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>You can also use <code>--standard=iso26262 --dal=C</code>"
  & " to get the same result as"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--asil=B</code>. The dedicated flags exist so a reader"
  & " of the command line can see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "&#8220;ASIL B&#8221; (or &#8220;Class A&#8221;) without deco"
  & "ding the shared tier.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--standard=all</code> runs <strong>one</strong> ass"
  & "essment at the shared tier and emits badges"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and reports for <strong>every</strong> standard &#8211; <cod"
  & "e>do178c.svg</code>, <code>iso26262.svg</code>, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>iec62304.svg</code> &#8211; without re-scanning, re-pr"
  & "oving, or re-parsing anything. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "evidence is identical across standards. The three badges the"
  & "refore always"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "agree on Achieved/Unmet. Only the level label changes.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""dashboard-and-sbom-standard-awareness""><a class=""hea"
  & "der"" href=""#dashboard-and-sbom-standard-awareness"">Dashboard"
  & " and SBOM standard-awareness</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The served <a href=""#web-dashboard-and-json-api"">dashboar"
  & "d</a> (<code>--serve</code>) and the proof-aware"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#the-sbom-subcommand-1"">SBOM</a> both record the as"
  & "sessment standard and its native level"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "label, so a browser or a CycloneDX / SPDX / Markdown consume"
  & "r sees the right"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "name for the selected standard."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Like the <code>sbom</code> subcommand, <code>--serve</code> "
  & "<strong>defaults to all standards</strong> when no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code> / <code>--clas"
  & "s</code> flag is given. The dashboard renders"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "every standard&#8217;s level at the shared tier. An explicit"
  & " standard flag"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "narrows it. The SBOM&#8217;s <code>adacovex:standard</code> "
  & "/ <code>adacovex:level</code> properties:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th><code>--</code> flag</th><th><code>adacovex:standard"
  & "</code></th><th><code>adacovex:level</code></th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--dal=C</code></td><td><code>DO-178C</code></t"
  & "d><td><code>DAL-C</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--asil=B</code></td><td><code>ISO 26262</code>"
  & "</td><td><code>ASIL B</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--class=A</code></td><td><code>IEC 62304</code"
  & "></td><td><code>Class A</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>--standard=all</code></td><td><code>DO-178C, I"
  & "SO 26262, IEC 62304</code></td><td><code>DAL-C / ASIL B / Cl"
  & "ass A</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>adacovex:dal_target</code> property always carr"
  & "ies the shared tier (<code>DAL-A</code>.."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>DAL-D</code>) regardless of the labelling standard. <c"
  & "ode>--standard=all</code> joins all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "three standard names and level labels into the single <code>"
  & "adacovex:standard</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>adacovex:level</code> properties. One document carries"
  & " every standard&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "assessment.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""implementation""><a class=""header"" href=""#implementat"
  & "ion"">Implementation</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Compliance_Standard</code> type (<code>DO_178C</co"
  & "de>, <code>ISO_26262</code>, <code>IEC_62304</code>) with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>To_String</code> / <code>To_Standard</code> / <code>St"
  & "andard_Slug</code> conversions and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dedicated <code>To_ASIL</code> / <code>To_Class</code> level"
  & " parsers in <code>Adacovex.Types</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>--standard=NAME</code> CLI flag (default <code>do1"
  & "78c</code>, plus <code>all</code>) selects the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "labelling standard. <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> is the shared r"
  & "igor tier (A&#8211;E). The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dedicated <code>--asil=LEVEL</code> / <code>--class=LEVEL</c"
  & "ode> flags set both the standard and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the tier in one step.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Types.Standard_Level_Name</code> maps a standard +"
  & " tier to its label (<code>DAL-C</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>ASIL B</code>, <code>Class A</code>, and more). <code>"
  & "Assess_Standard</code> runs the same evidence"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "checks as <code>Assess_DAL</code> while recording the standa"
  & "rd. Every renderer"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(ANSI report, SVG badge, HTML dashboard, JSON API, Markdown "
  & "report, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SBOM) then prints the standard-specific level without re-run"
  & "ning scanning,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof parsing, or test parsing.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Min_SPARK_For</code> still drives the per-tier pro"
  & "of bar. The tiers share one"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "lookup because the standards only re-label the levels.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Each standard has a dedicated reference page with its lev"
  & "el definitions and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "criteria:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DO-178C DAL "
  & "levels</a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-asil-levels.html"">ISO 26262 A"
  & "SIL levels</a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-class-levels.html"">IEC 62304 "
  & "safety classes</a></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""platform-support""><a class=""header"" href=""#platform-"
  & "support"">Platform support</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex is a zero-dependency Ada/SPARK binary. It uses o"
  & "nly the GNAT runtime and the standard library. As a result, "
  & "any platform with a working GNAT/Alire toolchain can build a"
  & "nd run it.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex makes no OS-specific assumptions beyond the CPU-"
  & "core and CI detection described below. These features fall b"
  & "ack to single-core operation when the host cannot be probed."
  & "</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""supported-platforms""><a class=""header"" href=""#suppor"
  & "ted-platforms"">Supported platforms</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Platform</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Linux x86-64</td><td><strong>Primary</strong></td><t"
  & "d>CI, releases, and the proof toolchain bundle all target it"
  & ".</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>WSL</strong></td><td><strong>Supported</stro"
  & "ng></td><td>Runs on the Linux/WSL targets below: <code>man</"
  & "code> installs to the WSL man root and <code>mandb</code> re"
  & "freshes it; VCS snapshot commands run via <code>sh -c</code>"
  & ".</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Linux aarch64</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from "
  & "source; the prebuilt toolchain bundle is x86-64 only.</td></"
  & "tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>macOS</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source ("
  & "Intel and Apple Silicon).</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>FreeBSD</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source"
  & ".</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Windows</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source"
  & "; core detection uses the Windows env var + PowerShell fallb"
  & "ack.</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""release-binaries""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-b"
  & "inaries"">Release binaries</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The CI release binary is Linux x86-64 only. The <code>ada"
  & "covex-vX. Y. Z.tar.gz</code> bundle (<code>adacovex</code> a"
  & "nd the <code>covex</code> alias) and the prebuilt GNATprove "
  & "toolchain asset are built on <code>ubuntu-latest</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every other platform builds adacovex from source via Alir"
  & "e (<code>alr build</code>). See <a href=""../README.html#inst"
  & "alling-adacovex"">Installing adacovex</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""cpu-core-count-detection""><a class=""header"" href=""#c"
  & "pu-core-count-detection"">CPU core-count detection</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Adacovex.CPUs.Detect_Core_Count</code> returns the "
  & "number of logical processors on the host. It falls back to <"
  & "code>1</code> when the host cannot be probed. Detection orde"
  & "r (pure GNAT runtime, no external library):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Linux</strong> &#8211; count <code>processor</co"
  & "de> entries in <code>/proc/cpuinfo</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>macOS / FreeBSD</strong> &#8211; <code>sysctl -n"
  & " hw.ncpu</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Linux fallback</strong> &#8211; <code>nproc</cod"
  & "e>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Windows</strong> &#8211; the <code>NUMBER_OF_PRO"
  & "CESSORS</code> environment variable.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Windows fallback</strong> &#8211; a PowerShell C"
  & "IM query (<code>Get-CimInstance Win32_ComputerSystem</code>)"
  & ".</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Each stage falls through to the next on failure. If all s"
  & "tages fail, the function returns <code>1</code>. adacovex st"
  & "ill runs when this happens. It runs single-threaded.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""ci-detection-and-prove-parallelism""><a class=""header"
  & """ href=""#ci-detection-and-prove-parallelism"">CI detection an"
  & "d prove parallelism</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Adacovex.CPUs.Is_Running_In_CI</code> detects the C"
  & "I markers set by GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines,"
  & " Buildkite, CircleCI, Travis CI, AppVeyor, Jenkins, and the "
  & "generic <code>CI</code> variable.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>GNATprove parallelism resolves as:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>--jobs=N</code> (<code>N &gt; 0</code>) &#8211; ex"
  & "actly <code>N</code> jobs.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>--jobs=0</code> / <code>-j0</code> &#8211; all cor"
  & "es (<code>gnatprove -j0</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>default (<code>--jobs</code> omitted) &#8211; <strong>al"
  & "l cores inside CI</strong>. Otherwise it uses <code>max(1, c"
  & "ores - 2)</code>. As a result, a developer machine keeps two"
  & " cores free for the system.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The chosen basis is printed in the verbose log (<code>Job"
  & "s_Justification</code>) and in the <a href=""#status-subcomma"
  & "nd""><code>status</code></a> report. As a result, a proof run"
  & " is auditable.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""status-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href=""#status-s"
  & "ubcommand""><code>status</code> subcommand</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex status</code> reports the toolchain and pl"
  & "atform state without running any assessment and <strong>with"
  & "out downloading or deploying anything</strong>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>adacovex status --target=PATH"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It checks and prints:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Alire</strong> (<code>alr</code>) is installed o"
  & "n <code>$PATH</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>gnatprove</strong> is dependency-managed (target"
  & " manifest pin) or detectable (global pin, on <code>$PATH</co"
  & "de>, or cached in <code>~/.adacovex/toolchain</code>). See <"
  & "a href=""#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand"">Ar"
  & "chitecture &#8211; toolchain resolution</a>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The <strong>logical CPU count</strong>, <strong>CI statu"
  & "s</strong>, and the resulting default <code>-j</code> parall"
  & "elism are reported.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>A <strong>VCS report</strong> lists the VCS command-line"
  & " tools available on <code>$PATH</code> for the differential "
  & "modes. The tools are git, mercurial/<code>hg</code>, subvers"
  & "ion/<code>svn</code>, fossil, jj, and the man-page tool <cod"
  & "e>mandb</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The VCS report shows the VCS detected for the target rep"
  & "ository.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The VCS report notes when the target&#8217;s VCS tool is"
  & " missing.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The VCS report notes when man-db (<code>mandb</code>) is"
  & " absent. You then know that <code>adacovex man</code> can in"
  & "stall the page but cannot refresh the man database.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The release note states that the CI binary is Linux x86-"
  & "64 only.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Base adacovex functionality does not require a version co"
  & "ntrol system. The functionality includes scanning, proof ana"
  & "lysis, test parsing, compliance assessment, SBOM generation,"
  & " dashboards, and caching. A VCS is only needed for the diffe"
  & "rential modes (<code>--compare-base</code> and <code>--cover"
  & "age-delta</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The status command returns exit code <code>0</code> when "
  & "a usable gnatprove is detectable without a download. <code>a"
  & "lr</code> must be present when the deploy path is the only o"
  & "ption. Otherwise, the command returns exit code <code>1</cod"
  & "e>. The VCS report is informational and does not affect the "
  & "exit code.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""local-man-page-linuxwsl""><a class=""header"" href=""#lo"
  & "cal-man-page-linuxwsl"">Local man page (Linux/WSL)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> installs the man page into the "
  & "local man database without root. The default root is <code>$"
  & "XDG_DATA_HOME/man</code> when set. Otherwise it is <code>~/."
  & "local/share/man</code>. This is the standard Linux/WSL per-u"
  & "ser man tree.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The index is refreshed with <code>mandb</code> when <code"
  & ">mandb</code> is present. Ubuntu and WSL ship <code>mandb</c"
  & "ode>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When man-db is not installed, or when <code>mandb</code> "
  & "fails, adacovex prints a warning. The warning states that th"
  & "e database was not refreshed. The page is still installed. Y"
  & "ou can read it with <code>man -l ~/.local/share/man/man1/ada"
  & "covex.1</code>. <code>adacovex status</code> reports whether"
  & " <code>mandb</code> is on <code>$PATH</code> up front.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--dir=PATH</code> overrides the root. The page embe"
  & "ds the binary version. <code>adacovex man --check</code> com"
  & "pares it to the installed page and exits <code>0</code> or <"
  & "code>1</code>. As a result, a prompt hook can auto-install w"
  & "hen a newer version is available. See <a href=""#man"">CLI ref"
  & "erence</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""vcs-support-linuxwsl""><a class=""header"" href=""#vcs-s"
  & "upport-linuxwsl"">VCS support (Linux/WSL)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--compare-base</code> and <code>--coverage-delta</c"
  & "ode> snapshot a base revision across git, Mercurial, Subvers"
  & "ion, Fossil, and jj. See <a href=""#vcs-support-and-different"
  & "ial-assessment"">VCS support</a>. The snapshot commands run t"
  & "hrough <code>sh -c</code>, which WSL provides. All temporary"
  & " snapshots live under <code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</"
  & "code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For VCS with poor snapshot UX (Subversion and Fossil), ad"
  & "acovex prints a note. The note recommends conversion to git."
  & "</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>See the <a href=""#adacovex-cli-reference"">CLI reference</"
  & "a> for the full flag surface.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""vcs-support-and-differential-assessment""><a class=""h"
  & "eader"" href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">VCS s"
  & "upport and differential assessment</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>A version control system is not required for base"
  & " adacovex functionality.</strong></p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This covers scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compl"
  & "iance assessment, SBOM generation, dashboards, and caching.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A VCS is only needed for the differential modes below. Th"
  & "ey snapshot a base revision to compare against the current t"
  & "ree.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>We assume that the audited project lives in a VCS. The ba"
  & "se tool never requires one.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex works on <strong>Linux and WSL</strong>. The sna"
  & "pshot commands run through <code>sh -c</code>, which WSL pro"
  & "vides.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""when-to-use-differential-modes""><a class=""header"" hr"
  & "ef=""#when-to-use-differential-modes"">When to use differentia"
  & "l modes</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Differential modes are useful when you want to enforce th"
  & "at changes do not regress quality gates:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>PR checks</strong> &#8211; <code>--coverage-delt"
  & "a</code> makes sure that docstring coverage does not drop be"
  & "tween the base branch and the PR head. This is the lightest "
  & "check. It works even when the base does not commit proof or "
  & "test artifacts.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Release gates</strong> &#8211; <code>adacovex --"
  & "compare-base=v1.2.0</code> compares the current tree against"
  & " the last release tag. It fails if a metric regressed. These"
  & " metrics are packages, docstrings, HLR tags, SPARK level, te"
  & "sts, and DAL status.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Audit trails</strong> &#8211; a side-by-side rep"
  & "ort shows exactly what changed between two revisions. This i"
  & "s useful for compliance audits that need a narrative diff.</"
  & "li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""supported-vcs""><a class=""header"" href=""#supported-vc"
  & "s"">Supported VCS</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The differential modes run against the VCS that manages t"
  & "he target. Detection is marker-file based, with a command-pr"
  & "obe fallback:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>VCS</th><th>Marker</th><th>Base snapshot mechanism</"
  & "th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>git</td><td><code>.git</code></td><td><code>git work"
  & "tree add --detach</code> (linked worktree)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>jj</td><td><code>.jj</code></td><td><code>jj git exp"
  & "ort</code> into the internal git store, then a git worktree "
  & "against <code>.jj/repo/store/git</code> (jj commits are git "
  & "commits)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Mercurial</td><td><code>.hg</code></td><td><code>hg "
  & "archive -r REF DIR</code> (pure export)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Subversion</td><td><code>.svn</code></td><td><code>s"
  & "vn info --show-item url</code> + <code>svn export -r REF URL"
  & " DIR</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Fossil</td><td><code>.fslckout</code> / <code>_FOSSI"
  & "L_</code></td><td>copy the repo DB and <code>fossil open</co"
  & "de> it at REF in a scratch dir</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For colocated git+jj repos, git wins (exact interop). All"
  & " snapshots land in <code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</cod"
  & "e> and are cleaned up afterwards. The working tree is never "
  & "touched.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>UX recommendation</strong>: Git gives the best ex"
  & "perience. Jj is its git-compatible sibling. Mercurial is ful"
  & "ly supported. For VCS whose snapshot UX is poor, adacovex pr"
  & "ints a note. The note recommends that developers convert the"
  & " repository to git (or a git-compatible VCS):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Subversion</strong> &#8211; no local history, ne"
  & "twork-dependent checkouts, slow <code>svn export</code> per "
  & "snapshot. Converting gives local branches, offline history, "
  & "and faster diffs.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Fossil</strong> &#8211; workable, but the toolin"
  & "g is niche and the single-file DB model complicates CI integ"
  & "ration.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>These notes are informational only. The assessment still "
  & "runs and gates still apply on every supported VCS.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex status</code> reports the VCS command-line"
  & " tools on <code>$PATH</code>. These tools are git, mercurial"
  & "/<code>hg</code>, subversion/<code>svn</code>, fossil, jj, a"
  & "nd <code>mandb</code>. It reports the VCS detected for the t"
  & "arget repository. It prints a note when the target&#8217;s V"
  & "CS tool is missing.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>See <a href=""#status-subcommand"">Platforms</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""--compare-baseref-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#--comp"
  & "are-baseref-1""><code>--compare-base=REF</code></a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Differential mode: adacovex snapshots a base revision in "
  & "a temporary directory (<code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;<"
  & "/code>). It prints a side-by-side comparison against the cur"
  & "rent tree. The comparison shows packages, subprograms, docst"
  & "ring percentage, traced HLR, orphan tags, SPARK level, prove"
  & "d VCs, tests, and DAL status.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>--target</code> directory must be a supported V"
  & "CS repository. The VCS command-line tool must be on <code>PA"
  & "TH</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Exit <code>0</code> only if there are no regressions and "
  & "the current DAL is Achieved. Otherwise, exit <code>1</code>."
  & " Artifacts that the base does not commit report <code>N/A</c"
  & "ode> and are not compared. These artifacts are <code>gnatpro"
  & "ve.out</code> and a test-result summary.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""--coverage-deltaref-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#--co"
  & "verage-deltaref-1""><code>--coverage-delta=REF</code></a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Lightweight docstring-coverage gate for PR-style CI check"
  & "s. It scans sources, patches, and computes docstring metrics"
  & " on a base revision and the current tree. It does not use GN"
  & "ATprove, tests, or DAL. Thus it works when the base does not"
  & " commit build artifacts.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It prints a compact coverage table and a machine-parseabl"
  & "e <code>coverage_delta:</code> line. Then it cleans up the s"
  & "napshot.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Exit <code>0</code> if the current docstring coverage is "
  & "<code>&gt;=</code> the base. Exit <code>0</code> also if the"
  & " base has no sources. Exit <code>1</code> if coverage regres"
  & "sed. This mode is mutually exclusive with <code>--compare-ba"
  & "se</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make release</code> runs the same gate against the "
  & "last release tag. For example, <code>--coverage-delta=v1.1.0"
  & "</code> aborts if docstring coverage regressed between relea"
  & "ses.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""adacovex-cicd""><a class=""header"" href=""#adacovex-cic"
  & "d"">adacovex CI/CD</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""github-actions""><a class=""header"" href=""#github-acti"
  & "ons"">GitHub Actions</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The composite action at <code>./action.yml</code> mirrors"
  & " the base CLI. CI can drive every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "assessment feature the same way the binary does.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""quick-start-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#quick-start-"
  & "1"">Quick start</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml""># .github/workflows/adacove"
  & "x.yml"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  push:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    branches: [main]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  pull_request:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "jobs:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  adacovex:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    steps:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: bladeacer/adacovex@v1"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "        with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          target: ."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          standard: all          # DO-178C + ISO 26262 + IEC"
  & " 62304"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          require-spark: Platinum"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          require-docstrings: 100"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          require-tests: 1173"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          run-tests: true"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          generate-sbom: true"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This job builds adacovex. It runs the target&#8217;s nati"
  & "ve tests and the full"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "assessment. It gates on Platinum SPARK, 100% docstring cover"
  & "age, and 900"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "passing tests. On failure, the job publishes <code>adacovex-"
  & "assessment</code> artifacts"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and Markdown summaries.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""pr-coverage-gate""><a class=""header"" href=""#pr-covera"
  & "ge-gate"">PR coverage gate</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Use <code>--coverage-delta</code> to fail PRs that drop d"
  & "ocstring coverage:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml""># .github/workflows/pr-cove"
  & "rage.yml"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  pull_request:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "jobs:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  coverage-delta:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    steps:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "        with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          fetch-depth: 0"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: bladeacer/adacovex@v1"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "        with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          target: ."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          coverage-delta: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base"
  & ".sha }}"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""release-workflow""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-w"
  & "orkflow"">Release workflow</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Tag a release. The bundled workflow (<code>release.yml</c"
  & "ode>) builds the binary and runs GNATprove. It validates the"
  & " self-assessment. It publishes `adacovex-vX.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Y. Z.tar.gz<code> and the composite action bundle. Floati"
  & "ng tags (</code>@latest<code>, </code>@v1<code>, </code>@v1."
  & "3<code>) always point at the newest release. Pin </code>@vX."
  & "</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Y. Z` for reproducibility.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""gitlab-ci""><a class=""header"" href=""#gitlab-ci"">GitLa"
  & "b CI</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The same inputs map to GitLab CI variables:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml""># .gitlab-ci.yml"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  image: ubuntu:latest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  before_script:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    - apt-get update -qq &amp;&amp; apt-get install -y -qq c"
  & "url"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    - curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bladeacer"
  & "/adacovex/main/install.sh | bash"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  script:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    - adacovex --target=. --standard=all --dal=C --require-s"
  & "park=Platinum --require-docstrings=100"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  artifacts:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    when: always"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    paths:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - sbom.json"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - docs/badges/*.svg"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>If your runner already has Alire, replace the <code>insta"
  & "ll.sh</code> step with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr install covex gnatprove</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""other-ci-systems""><a class=""header"" href=""#other-ci-"
  & "systems"">Other CI systems</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action is a pure composite of shell steps. It works o"
  & "n any runner that can"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "run <code>bash</code> and install Alire:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Install Alire + GNAT (<code>alr toolchain --install gnat"
  & "_native</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Download the release bundle or build from source.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Run <code>adacovex</code> with the same flags as the Git"
  & "Hub Action inputs.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The JSON API (<code>/api/metrics</code> when using <code>"
  & "--serve</code>, or <code>--emit-metrics</code>) lets"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "you parse results in any language.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Action/CLI/docs parity is a feature gate.</strong"
  & "> <code>ci.yml</code> runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make action-parity-check</code> (wired into <code>make"
  & " check</code>). The build fails when the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "action&#8217;s inputs stop mirroring the base CLI option set"
  & ". The build also fails"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "when the <code>### Inputs</code> table below drifts from <co"
  & "de>action.yml</code>. See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>tools/check-action-parity.py</code> for the mapping ru"
  & "les.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""composite-action-actionyml""><a class=""header"" href="""
  & "#composite-action-actionyml"">Composite action (<code>./actio"
  & "n.yml</code>)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The composite action installs Alire via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://github.com/alire-project/setup-alire""><code"
  & ">alire-project/setup-alire</code></a>."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "GNAT comes from <code>gnat-version</code> plus <code>gprbuil"
  & "d</code>. <code>gnatprove</code> is NOT an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr toolchain</code> component. The <code>prove</code>"
  & " subcommand resolves it through the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "target project&#8217;s manifest, <code>$PATH</code>, cached "
  & "toolchain, or download.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action obtains the version-matched adacovex binary. I"
  & "t downloads the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "release bundle by default. You can set <code>build: true</co"
  & "de> to build from source.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Optionally, the action runs GNATprove (<code>prove</code>"
  & ") and the native tests"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>run-tests</code>). Then it runs the assessment. It ge"
  & "nerates a proof-aware SBOM"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>generate-sbom</code>, default <code>true</code>). It "
  & "publishes a Markdown step summary,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "machine-readable outputs, and SVG badge artifacts.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>run-tests</code> <strong>builds the target&#8217;s "
  & "native test suite first</strong>. In a consumer"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "workspace, the <code>build: true</code> step builds adacovex"
  & " in a scratch checkout. It"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "leaves the target untouched.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action runs <code>alr build</code> in the target root"
  & " before executing"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>test-command</code>. The target root is a subdirectory"
  & " when <code>target</code> points at one."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "In the self-assessment case, the build is an incremental no-"
  & "op.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This design keeps <code>test-command: ./test_crdt</code>-"
  & "style usage working in consumer"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "repositories such as Ada_CRDT&#8217;s release workflow.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action is version-matched to the adacovex binary. The"
  & " release workflow bundles <code>adacovex-vX. Y. Z.tar.gz</co"
  & "de> for every `vX.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Y. Z` tag. The action downloads the binary for the tag it"
  & " is referenced by. Reference it by a floating tag to always "
  & "get the latest published release.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>You can pin to an exact release for reproducibility:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml"">steps:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  - uses: actions/checkout@v7"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  - uses: bladeacer/adacovex@v1"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      target: ."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      standard: all   # badges/reports for DO-178C + ISO 262"
  & "62 + IEC 62304"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
