  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""result-caching""><a class=""header"" href=""#result-cach"
  & "ing"">Result caching</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action restores <code>~/.adacovex/cache</code> before"
  & " running adacovex. It saves the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cache when the job finishes (<code>result-cache</code>, defa"
  & "ult <code>true</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every entry is keyed by its artifact&#8217;s SHA-256 cont"
  & "ent hash. Restoring a cache"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "from an earlier run or commit is always safe. Only files tha"
  & "t are byte-for-byte"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "unchanged are served from it. The remaining files are rescan"
  & "ned and re-parsed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "automatically.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""workflows""><a class=""header"" href=""#workflows"">Workf"
  & "lows</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code></strong> &"
  & "#8211; three jobs on push to <code>main</code> and pull"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "requests:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>self-assessment</code> &#8211; build + prove + ass"
  & "ess at <code>--standard=all</code> (so the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "DO-178C, ISO 26262, and IEC 62304 badges/reports are all emi"
  & "tted and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gated), with the Platinum / 100% docstrings / test-count / 1"
  & "00% proof"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "thresholds.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex-tests</code> &#8211; build + native test "
  & "suite (<code>run-tests</code>, <code>assess: false</code>).<"
  & "/li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>coverage-gate</code> (push only) &#8211; runs <cod"
  & "e>make coverage-gate</code>, comparing"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "docstring coverage between the latest two release tags.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/pr-check.yml</code></str"
  & "ong> &#8211; runs <code>--coverage-delta</code> against"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>pull_request.base.sha</code> to fail PRs that drop doc"
  & "string coverage.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code></stro"
  & "ng> &#8211; on a <code>v*</code> tag, builds the release"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "binary, runs GNATprove, validates the <code>--standard=all</"
  & "code> self-assessment, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "publishes the GitHub Release (see <a href=""#release-bundling"
  & """>Release bundling</a>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""markdown-summaries-and-loud-failures""><a class=""head"
  & "er"" href=""#markdown-summaries-and-loud-failures"">Markdown su"
  & "mmaries and loud failures</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every CI run leaves a <strong>Markdown summary at the bot"
  & "tom of the job page</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The composite action&#8217;s assessment step writes an <"
  & "code>## adacovex assessment</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "table. The table shows target, bundled version, compliance l"
  & "abel, SPARK"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "level, tests, and coverage. It also writes the full raw outp"
  & "ut.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>An <code>if: always()</code> <strong>Write run summary</"
  & "strong> step appends a run-overview table."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The table shows version, target, standard, DAL, and job resu"
  & "lt.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Each workflow adds a <strong><code>summary</code> job</s"
  & "trong> (<code>if: always()</code>, <code>needs:</code> all o"
  & "ther"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "jobs) that aggregates every job result into one table at the"
  & " bottom of the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "run.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Diagnostics are layered so a failure is debuggable from t"
  & "he Actions UI without"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "re-running locally:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The assessment output is folded into a GitHub <strong>lo"
  & "g group</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>::group::</code>). The step result stays visible. The"
  & " detail stays one click"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "away.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>WARNING</code> lines are re-surfaced as <code>::no"
  & "tice::</code> annotations.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>An <strong><code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifact</st"
  & "rong> (uploaded <code>if: always()</code>) carries the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "full, untruncated assessment output. It also carries the <co"
  & "de>--emit-metrics</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JSON export when <code>emit-metrics</code> is set. A flaky o"
  & "r unmet gate never requires"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a re-run to reproduce.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Badge and SBOM artifacts are uploaded even when the step"
  & " failed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>if: always()</code>). Partially produced reports stay"
  & " inspectable.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Threshold failures <strong>fail loudly</strong> at every "
  & "layer:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Unmet <code>--require-*</code> gates make the adacovex b"
  & "inary exit non-zero.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The assessment step re-surfaces each <code>CI GATE:</cod"
  & "e> line as a GitHub"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>::error::</code> annotation. The annotation is visible"
  & " at the top of the job"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "page, not just in the log. The step marks the summary table "
  & "<strong>FAILED</strong> with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the unmet gates.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The action&#8217;s <code>Write run summary</code> step ("
  & "runs on failure too) reports the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "failed job result.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The workflow <code>summary</code> job exits <code>1</cod"
  & "e> when any dependency failed. The whole"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "run is red even if the failing job was retried. An <code>if:"
  & " always()</code> cleanup"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "step does not mask this.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""debugging-guide-what-to-do-when-you-see-""><a class="""
  & "header"" href=""#debugging-guide-what-to-do-when-you-see-"">Deb"
  & "ugging guide: what to do when you see &#8230;</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Output</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: SPARK level X below required Y (--req"
  & "uire-spark)</code></td><td>Proven VCs or <code>gnatprove</co"
  & "de> version drift below the pinned gate</td><td>Check the <c"
  & "ode>gnatprove</code> pin in <code>alire-dev.toml</code> or t"
  & "he <code>gnat-version</code> input. Re-run <code>make prove<"
  & "/code>. Update <code>--require-spark</code> only if the prov"
  & "er legitimately tightened</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: docstring coverage N% below required "
  & "M% (--require-docstrings)</code></td><td>Missing <code>--</c"
  & "ode> docstrings or patches</td><td>Run <code>adacovex --verb"
  & "ose</code> to list undocumented subprogs. Add patches under "
  & "<code>.adacovex/patches/</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: proved-VC coverage N% below required "
  & "M% (--require-proof)</code></td><td>Some VCs unproved/justif"
  & "ied</td><td>Inspect <code>gnatprove.out</code>. Add contract"
  & "s or fix <code>SPARK_Mode</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Warning: N source file(s) skipped: line exceed"
  & "s Max_Line</code></td><td>A physical line &gt; <code>Max_Lin"
  & "e</code> (262144 on 64-bit)</td><td>Split the declaration. D"
  & "AL becomes <code>Unmet</code> by design (<code>docs/architec"
  & "ture.md#overflow-contract</code>)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>result cache: X hit(s), Y miss(es), Z evicted<"
  & "/code></td><td>Cache stats per run</td><td><code>Z&gt;0</cod"
  & "e> means <code>--cache-max</code> evicted the oldest entries"
  & ". Increase <code>--cache-max</code>. Pass <code>--no-cache</"
  & "code> to force a full rescan</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>Unknown option --foo (did you mean --bar?)</co"
  & "de></td><td>Typo</td><td>Use <code>adacovex --help</code> or"
  & " <code>adacovex help &lt;topic&gt;</code></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>::notice::WARNING ...</code> annotation</td><t"
  & "d>Non-fatal warning surfaced from <code>adacovex.out</code><"
  & "/td><td>Download the <code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifa"
  & "ct for the full log. Warnings do not fail the gate. They ind"
  & "icate missing tests or proof</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><code>make complexity-check</code> failed</td><td>Fi"
  & "le or function exceeds caps (<code>--max-file-loc</code>/<co"
  & "de>--max-file-pct</code>/<code>--max-fn-complexity</code>)</"
  & "td><td>Run <code>./bin/adacovex complexity --help</code>. Sp"
  & "lit god objects or functions</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Better debugging output contract.</strong> <code>"
  & "ci.yml</code> now has <code>timeout-minutes</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>concurrency.cancel-in-progress</code>, <code>fetch-tag"
  & "s: true</code>, and <code>actions/cache</code> for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "both toolchain and result-cache. After these brittleness fix"
  & "es, every failure"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "leaves three things without a re-run:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The <code>::error</code>/<code>::notice</code> annotatio"
  & "ns at the top of the job page.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The <code>## adacovex assessment</code> Markdown table i"
  & "n <code>GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The <code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifact (full untr"
  & "uncated <code>adacovex.out</code> +"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>adacovex-metrics.json</code> when <code>emit-metrics</"
  & "code> is set).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When the gate is flaky, start from the artifact, not a lo"
  & "cal repro.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""release-version-bundling""><a class=""header"" href=""#r"
  & "elease-version-bundling"">Release version bundling</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The release workflow builds the binary from the <code>vX."
  & " Y. Z</code> tag. It <strong>bundles that version into the b"
  & "inary</strong>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action&#8217;s build step sets <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION"
  & "</code> (from <code>github.ref_name</code>). It regenerates "
  & "<code>src/adacovex_version_info.ads</code> before <code>alr "
  & "build</code>. The shipped <code>adacovex --version</code> re"
  & "ports exactly the tag.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The download step of the published action verifies this w"
  & "ith <code>adacovex --version</code> after unpacking the rele"
  & "ase bundle. Locally, <code>make release VERSION=x.y.z</code>"
  & " does the same. Normal <code>make build</code> reads the ver"
  & "sion from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> instead.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""pr-coverage-gate-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#pr-cove"
  & "rage-gate-1"">PR coverage gate</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Gate every pull request so docstring coverage does not re"
  & "gress against the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "base branch. This is exactly what <code>--coverage-delta</co"
  & "de> was built for:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml""># .github/workflows/pr-chec"
  & "k.yml"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  pull_request:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "jobs:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  coverage-delta:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "    steps:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "        with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          fetch-depth: 0"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      - uses: bladeacer/adacovex@v1"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "        with:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          target: ."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          standard: all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          coverage-delta: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base"
  & ".sha }}"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The action exits non-zero when coverage drops, failing th"
  & "e check. This"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "workflow ships in the repo at <code>.github/workflows/pr-che"
  & "ck.yml</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""release-bundling""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-b"
  & "undling"">Release bundling</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag triggers <code>.github/wo"
  & "rkflows/release.yml</code>. The workflow calls the composite"
  & " action with <code>build</code>, <code>release-build</code>,"
  & " and <code>prove</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It builds the release binary, runs GNATprove, and validat"
  & "es the self-assessment. Then it packages and publishes:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> &#8211; the version-"
  & "matched binary (<code>adacovex</code> plus the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>covex</code> alias). The action downloads this asset f"
  & "or the tag it is referenced"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by, so <code>@v1.9.0</code> runs adacovex <code>v1.9.0</code"
  & ">.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>adacovex-action-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> &#8211; a cop"
  & "y of the composite action itself for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendoring or air-gapped use.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Both bundles are attested with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://github.com/actions/attest""><code>actions/at"
  & "test</code></a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on every tag. OIDC attestations appear under the release&#82"
  & "17;s attestations tab."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The release notes link the signed attestation via the action"
  & "&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>attestation-url</code> output. They also link a <em>Gi"
  & "t Changelog</em> compare link"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>compare/v1.9.0...v1.14.0</code>) and the human-readab"
  & "le changelogs.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Changelog listing.</strong> The <code>Create GitH"
  & "ub Release</code> step derives the changelog"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "list from the available <code>docs/changelogs/adacovex-*.md<"
  & "/code> entries. The entries"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "are between the previous release tag and the released versio"
  & "n.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It resolves the previous three-component release tag"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>git tag --sort=-version:refname</code>, for example <"
  & "code>v1.9.0</code> when releasing"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>v1.14.0</code>). Then it lists every changelog whose v"
  & "ersion is strictly above the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "previous release and at or below the released version. Relea"
  & "sing <code>v1.14.0</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "after <code>v1.9.0</code> links the <code>1.10.0</code>..<co"
  & "de>1.14.0</code> changelogs in one release.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The list is emitted <strong>newest-first</strong> (versio"
  & "n-sorted, not shell glob order)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The entries read <code>1.14.0</code> down to <code>1.10.0</c"
  & "ode>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The list is derived from the changelog files present in t"
  & "he tree, not from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tags. A version that was never released has no entry. A rele"
  & "ase that skips"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "versions still links every changelog in the range.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>The CI release binary is Linux x86-64 only for no"
  & "w.</strong> The release workflow"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "runs on <code>ubuntu-latest</code>. It packages the Linux bi"
  & "nary and the prebuilt"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "GNATprove toolchain bundle for that target. macOS, FreeBSD, "
  & "Windows, and Linux"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "aarch64 build adacovex from source via Alire instead. See"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#release-binaries"">Platforms</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make release VERSION=x.y.z</code> does the same loc"
  & "ally. It builds <code>--release</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "generates proofs, validates DAL-C, and bundles <code>dist/</"
  & "code>. Then it tags and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "pushes to trigger the workflow. <code>make build</code> rege"
  & "nerates"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>src/adacovex_version_info.ads</code> from <code>alire-"
  & "dev.toml</code> (or <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code>)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "before compiling. The bundled version is always the build&#8"
  & "217;s version.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""floating-tags""><a class=""header"" href=""#floating-tag"
  & "s"">Floating tags</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The release workflow force-pushes the floating tags <code"
  & ">vMAJOR</code>, <code>vMAJOR. MINOR</code>, and <code>latest"
  & "</code>. For example: <code>v1</code>, <code>v1.3</code>, an"
  & "d <code>latest</code> from <code>v1.3.0</code>. Reference <c"
  & "ode>@latest</code> to always get the newest published releas"
  & "e.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Use <code>@v1</code> or <code>@v1.3</code> for the latest"
  & " release within a major or minor version. Pin an exact <code"
  & ">@vX. Y. Z</code> for a fixed version.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Once the action is listed on the GitHub Actions marketpla"
  & "ce, each <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag auto-publishes that versi"
  & "on.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""consumer-manifest-prerequisites-avoid-a-broken-ci""><"
  & "a class=""header"" href=""#consumer-manifest-prerequisites-avoi"
  & "d-a-broken-ci"">Consumer manifest prerequisites (avoid a brok"
  & "en CI)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex&#8217;s <code>prove</code> subcommand and the Gi"
  & "tHub Action resolve <code>gnatprove</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "through the <em>target project&#8217;s</em> manifest. The pi"
  & "nned gnatprove crate is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "deployed via <code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</cod"
  & "e>. It is run directly, with no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr exec</code> over the whole workspace.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For the command to succeed in a clean checkout or on CI, "
  & "the consumer&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifests must follow two rules:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong><code>alire.toml</code> must be the clean publish"
  & "ing manifest.</strong> It must contain no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dev tooling (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin</code"
  & ">, <code>gnatformat_bin</code>, <code>covex</code>). It must"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contain <strong>no <code>[[pins]]</code></strong>. Alire rea"
  & "ds this manifest when the action runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr build</code>. It must resolve with nothing but Ali"
  & "re + GNAT.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong><code>alire-dev.toml</code> must declare <code>co"
  & "vex</code> as a normal index dependency</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>covex = ""*""</code>). It must never be pinned to a loc"
  & "al path such as"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>covex = { path = ""../adacovex"" }</code>. A path pin re"
  & "solves only on the machine"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that has the sibling checkout. In a consumer workspace or on"
  & " CI, Alire"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "fails the whole workspace load with a confusing error. This "
  & "happens before"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "adacovex or <code>alr</code> runs:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>ERROR: Failed to load alire.toml:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ERROR:    pins:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ERROR:    covex:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ERROR:    Pin path is not a valid directory: /home/runner/wo"
  & "rk/&lt;repo&gt;/&lt;repo&gt;/../adacovex"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>If you see that, drop the <code>covex</code> path pin. Us"
  & "e <code>covex = ""*""</code>. Strip the dev"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "deps and pins out of <code>alire.toml</code>. Keep them only"
  & " in <code>alire-dev.toml</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The Makefile pattern in many projects keeps the published"
  & " <code>alire.toml</code> clean."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "It swaps <code>alire-dev.toml</code> over <code>alire.toml</"
  & "code> only for the duration of a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>prove</code>/<code>fmt</code>/<code>doc</code> target,"
  & " then restores it. This gives local tooling the dev"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "deps.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""contributor-guide-codebase-structure-and-setup""><a c"
  & "lass=""header"" href=""#contributor-guide-codebase-structure-an"
  & "d-setup"">Contributor guide: codebase structure and setup</a>"
  & "</h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This page is a human-readable tour of the adacovex codeba"
  & "se for people who want"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to build, test, or modify it. It supplements"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""../CONTRIBUTING.html"">CONTRIBUTING.md</a> (process,"
  & " changelog format, PR rules)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "This page is about <strong>how the code is organised and how"
  & " to get a working"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "development environment</strong>. <code>AGENTS.md</code> is "
  & "the machine-facing version of the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same information.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""setting-up-the-repository""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
  & "setting-up-the-repository"">Setting up the repository</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Prerequisites:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Alire</strong> &gt;= 2.0 (<code>alr</code>) &#82"
  & "11; the Ada package manager. It downloads and manages"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the GNAT toolchain for you.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>GNAT</strong> Ada compiler &#8211; managed by Al"
  & "ire (<code>alr</code> pulls <code>gnat_native</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Python 3</strong> &#8211; only for build/dev too"
  & "ling (<code>tools/*.py</code>). The shipped binary"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "has no Python dependency.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>gnatprove</strong> &#8211; optional for <em>usin"
  & "g</em> adacovex, required for <code>make prove</code>."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "It is resolved at run time (manifest pin, <code>$PATH</code>"
  & ", cached toolchain, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "download). It lives in the dev manifest, never the published"
  & " one.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">git clone https://github.co"
  & "m/bladeacer/adacovex.git"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cd adacovex"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make build        # compiles bin/adacovex + bin/test_runner "
  & "(covex alias)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make test         # builds + runs the native test suite (117"
  & "3 tests)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make run-self     # assess adacovex itself: 100% docs, Plati"
  & "num, DAL-C"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make prove        # SPARK proof (Platinum gate) + regenerate"
  & "s docs/badges/"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make check        # the whole quality gate CI runs before a "
  & "release"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make check</code> is the pre-commit gate. It runs c"
  & "heap static checks first (ASCII, SPARK_Mode-Off policy, chan"
  & "gelog format, version source, doc-links, markdown links). Th"
  & "en it runs build, tests, proof, docs, and SBOM. Then it runs"
  & " tree-wide count-sync checks.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Everything must pass. The sync checks fail loudly when a "
  & "count in any documentation file is stale.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""repository-tour""><a class=""header"" href=""#repository"
  & "-tour"">Repository tour</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>src/"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- adacovex_main.adb              -- CLI entry point: parse"
  & " -&gt; pipeline -&gt; render -&gt; exit"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- adacovex.ads                   -- Version constant"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- core/                          -- config parsing, types,"
  & " cache, VCS, GNATprove runner, diff"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- parsers/                       -- input parsing: Ada sou"
  & "rce, gnatprove.out, tests, manifest, HLR/LLR"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- renderers/                     -- output: ANSI, HTML das"
  & "hboard, Markdown, SVG badges, SBOM, man page"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- compliance/                    -- DO-178C DAL assessment"
  & " logic"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- server/                        -- HTTP/1.1 server (4-wor"
  & "ker task pool) for --serve"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "|-- ir/                            -- bounded IR types + fut"
  & "ure-use synthesiser"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "`-- tests/                         -- the native test suite "
  & "(test_runner entry point)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resources/dashboard.html           -- the served dashboard's"
  & " page shell (plain HTML, bundled at build time)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tools/*.py                         -- pure-stdlib Python: do"
  & "c sync, count sync, generators, validators"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "docs/                              -- all documentation (thi"
  & "s guide, CLI reference, standards, and more)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <strong>execution pipeline</strong> (<code>adacovex_m"
  & "ain.adb</code>) is the spine of the tool:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>parse CLI -&gt; scan .ads sources -&gt; apply doc"
  & "string patches -&gt; compute doc metrics"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "-&gt; parse gnatprove.out -&gt; parse test results -&gt; ass"
  & "ess DAL -&gt; render ANSI report"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "-&gt; emit SVG badges -&gt; emit Markdown reports -&gt; emit"
  & " SBOM -&gt; serve dashboard (if --serve)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "-&gt; exit code (0 = Achieved)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A handful of modes exit before the pipeline: <code>--help"
  & "</code>, <code>--version</code>, <code>man</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>status</code>, the differential modes (<code>--compare"
  & "-base</code> / <code>--coverage-delta</code>), and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>sbom</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""where-things-live""><a class=""header"" href=""#where-th"
  & "ings-live"">Where things live</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
