  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""proving-and-writing-spark-proofs""><a class=""header"" "
  & "href=""#proving-and-writing-spark-proofs"">Proving and writing"
  & " SPARK proofs</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex runs gnatprove, reads its summary, and grades th"
  & "e result against"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.html"">SPARK assu"
  & "rance levels</a>. This page"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is the guide to both halves: <strong>how proving works</stro"
  & "ng> under adacovex, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>how to write proofs</strong> &#8211; contracts in yo"
  & "ur own code, and &#8211; when the code"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is vendored and cannot be modified &#8211; <strong>proof pat"
  & "ches</strong> that add the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contracts for you.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""proving-a-project-with-adacovex""><a class=""header"" h"
  & "ref=""#proving-a-project-with-adacovex"">Proving a project wit"
  & "h adacovex</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex prove --target=."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>prove</code> subcommand (full options:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#the-prove-subcommand"">CLI reference &#8211; the <c"
  & "ode>prove</code> subcommand</a>):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Resolves gnatprove</strong> without requiring th"
  & "e target to declare it:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest pin &gt; global pin &gt; <code>$PATH</code> &gt; ca"
  & "ched toolchain &gt; download. Full"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "order and per-method detail:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand"">A"
  & "rchitecture &#8211; GNATprove toolchain resolution</a>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Runs gnatprove</strong> against the target (or a"
  & "gainst a patched tree copy"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "when proof patches are present &#8211; see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">Proof"
  & " patches</a> below) and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "writes the summary to <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gna"
  & "tprove.out</code> &#8211; the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "location the assessment pipeline discovers.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Falls through to the full assessment</strong>. T"
  & "he assessment parses the fresh"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "summary. One command both proves and assesses. The <code>--r"
  & "equire-*</code> CI gates"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "apply to the proof run directly (<code>--require-spark=Plati"
  & "num --require-proof=100</code> and more; see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#ci-threshold-gates---require-"">CLI reference &#821"
  & "1; CI threshold gates</a>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The result cache serves unchanged targets so repeated run"
  & "s are cheap."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--force</code> bypasses the cache and forces a full gn"
  & "atprove reanalysis. A target"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "without a <code>gnatprove.out</code> at all is graded <code>"
  & "Stone</code> with proof metrics <code>N/A</code>."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Run <code>prove</code> to generate one.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""what-a-proof-contains""><a class=""header"" href=""#what"
  & "-a-proof-contains"">What a proof contains</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>gnatprove reports verification conditions (VCs) per check"
  & " category. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "summary in <code>gnatprove.out</code> breaks them down as:</"
  & "p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Category</th><th>What it covers</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Run-time checks</td><td>Index bounds, overflow, divi"
  & "sion-by-zero, range checks &#8211; absence of run-time error"
  & "s</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Assertions</td><td>User <code>pragma Assert</code> s"
  & "tatements and pre/postcondition checks</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Functional contracts</td><td><code>Pre</code> / <cod"
  & "e>Post</code> / <code>Global</code> contract satisfaction</t"
  & "d></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Data dependencies</td><td>Flow analysis: uninitializ"
  & "ed reads, effective <code>Global</code> contracts</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Initialization</td><td>All objects initialized befor"
  & "e first use</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td>Termination</td><td><code>Loop_Variant</code> / recu"
  & "rsion bounds (subprograms proved terminating)</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The honest <strong>proved</strong> count is <code>total -"
  & " justified - unproved</code> (flow plus"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "provers). The <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.html"">"
  & "assurance level</a> is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "derived from how many of each category were discharged:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Stone</strong> &#8211; no proof run or nothing a"
  & "nalyzable;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Bronze</strong> &#8211; flow analysis clean (dat"
  & "a dependencies, initialization);</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Silver</strong> &#8211; run-time checks proved, "
  & "assertions proved;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Gold</strong> &#8211; functional contracts prove"
  & "d on top;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Platinum</strong> &#8211; every VC proved: <stro"
  & "ng>0 unproved</strong> (and, in adacovex&#8217;s own"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gate, <strong>0 justified</strong> &#8211; no <code>pragma A"
  & "nnotate</code> justifications).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Justified VCs count neither as proved nor as unproved. On"
  & "ly unproved VCs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "downgrade the level. For a DAL assessment, the level must me"
  & "et the requirement"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "of the tier (<code>--dal=C</code> needs Bronze, <code>--dal="
  & "A</code> needs Gold, and more) &#8211; see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DAL levels</a>.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""writing-proofs-spark-contracts""><a class=""header"" hr"
  & "ef=""#writing-proofs-spark-contracts"">Writing proofs: SPARK c"
  & "ontracts</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A proof starts with contracts in the source, written as A"
  & "da aspects:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">package Body_Vec is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi :"
  & " in Integer)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     return Integer"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     with Pre  =&gt; Lo &lt;= Hi,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "          Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in Lo .. Hi;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end Body_Vec;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Rules that matter in practice:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> selects what gn"
  & "atprove analyses.</strong> Without it a unit"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is out of proof scope. It can be declared on the package"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>package P with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is</code>), on ind"
  & "ividual subprograms, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "both &#8211; adacovex&#8217;s own source uses package-level "
  & "On on pure units and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "per-subprogram On aspects inside default-off bodies.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>A body is analysed only when the body itself opt"
  & "s in.</strong> Declaring"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> on the <em>spec</em> does n"
  & "ot make gnatprove analyse the body."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The body must declare it too (on the <code>package body</cod"
  & "e> line or per subprogram)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "This is the rule that makes proof patches necessary for vend"
  & "ored code &#8211; see"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "below.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>I/O bodies are skipped by design.</strong> A bod"
  & "y that calls <code>Ada.Text_IO</code> (which"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "is <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code>) cannot be analysed. gnatprov"
  & "e reports the unit out of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof scope. This never drags the assessed level down &#8211"
  & "; it means those"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bodies are not proved.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Contracts are proved against the body.</strong> "
  & "gnatprove proves that every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "possible body execution satisfies the declared <code>Pre</co"
  & "de>/<code>Post</code>. Callers must in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "turn establish the <code>Pre</code> before calling.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>--steps</code> controls the proof budget.<"
  & "/strong> gnatprove&#8217;s default step limit can"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "produce solver-timeout false negatives. adacovex runs with <"
  & "code>--steps 10000</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by default so such timeouts are not reported as unproved. An"
  & " explicit"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--steps=N</code> overrides.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The goal for a clean proof: every VC in every category pr"
  & "oved, 0 unproved,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "0 justified.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies""><a clas"
  & "s=""header"" href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencie"
  & "s"">Proof patches: proving vendored dependencies</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Patch files at <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/</c"
  & "ode> exist so vendored code you"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cannot modify still counts toward the audit. Their best-know"
  & "n job is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "overlaying <strong>docstrings</strong> for strict-mode cover"
  & "age. A patch can also carry"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<strong>SPARK proof aspects</strong> so vendored dependencie"
  & "s participate in the proof"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "with real contracts &#8211; without forking or touching thei"
  & "r sources.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""why-proof-patches-are-necessary""><a class=""header"" h"
  & "ref=""#why-proof-patches-are-necessary"">Why proof patches are"
  & " necessary</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Three facts force the design:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Strict mode counts vendored code.</strong> By de"
  & "fault adacovex scans every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory except the always-excluded ones. The excluded dire"
  & "ctories are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code>, <code>tests</code>, <co"
  & "de>config</code>, and <code>.adacovex</code>. A vendored dep"
  & "endency&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "missing docstrings and missing contracts count against the t"
  & "arget."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--relaxed</code> skips vendored dirs but drops the aud"
  & "it to a quick pass &#8211; not"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "an option for a compliance assessment.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>gnatprove analyses a body only when the body its"
  & "elf opts in.</strong> (The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "rule from <a href=""#writing-proofs-spark-contracts"">Writing "
  & "proofs</a> above.) A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendored spec with no contracts contributes nothing to the p"
  & "roof. A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendored body without <code>SPARK_Mode</code> is skipped ent"
  & "irely.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>The vendored sources are immutable.</strong> The"
  & " dependency ships as-is. You"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cannot add contracts to it. Re-publishing a patched fork def"
  & "eats the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "point of vendoring.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A proof patch is the merge of these three constraints. It"
  & " re-declares the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendored spec with contracts (<code>.ads</code> patch). It o"
  & "pts the vendored body into"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the proof (<code>.adb</code> patch). The <code>prove</code> "
  & "subcommand merges both into a patched"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tree copy before running gnatprove &#8211; the originals are"
  & " never touched.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""how-proof-patches-are-applied""><a class=""header"" hre"
  & "f=""#how-proof-patches-are-applied"">How proof patches are app"
  & "lied</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Count_Proof_Patches</code> scans <code>&lt;target&"
  & "gt;/.adacovex/patches/</code> for <code>.ads</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.adb</code> files. A patch carrying any of <code>SPARK"
  & "_Mode</code>, <code>Pre =&gt;</code>, <code>Post =&gt;</code"
  & ">,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "or <code>Global =&gt;</code> is a <em>proof patch</em>. A do"
  & "cstring-only patch never engages"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the proof machinery. A target with no proof patches is prove"
  & "d against its"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "own tree exactly as before.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Build_Patched_Copy</code> copies the target tree ("
  & "excluding <code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>.adacovex</code>) into <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/ad"
  & "acovex-proof/</code> and overwrites each"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof-patched source with its merged form.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>gnatprove runs against the copy&#8217;s root project and"
  & " the resulting"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>gnatprove.out</code> is copied back to <code>&lt;targe"
  & "t&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "for the assessment pipeline.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Patch contents are folded into the prove result-cache ke"
  & "y, so a patch"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prove (<co"
  & "de>--force</code> also"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bypasses the cache).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The patched copy lives under the target&#8217;s <code>obj"
  & "/</code>, so it is excluded from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scanning, manifest graphs, and the prove input hash.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""writing-a-spec-patch-ads""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
  & "riting-a-spec-patch-ads"">Writing a spec patch (<code>.ads</c"
  & "ode>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A spec patch mirrors the vendored spec: same package name"
  & ", same subprogram"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "declarations (with docstrings, since strict mode requires th"
  & "em), plus the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "aspects you want gnatprove to prove:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/d"
  & "eps/vt100/vt100.ads"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package VT100 with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  Scroll a region of the screen up."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  @param From  Starting line of scroll region."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  @param To    Ending line of scroll region."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   procedure Scroll_Screen (From : in Natural; To : in Natur"
  & "al)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     with Pre =&gt; From &lt;= To;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end VT100;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The merge splices the package-level aspect onto the origi"
  & "nal package"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "declaration line and replaces each aspect-carrying subprogra"
  & "m declaration"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "with the patch&#8217;s declaration block. Subprograms the pa"
  & "tch does not re-declare"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "with aspects are left untouched, so a patch can add a contra"
  & "ct to one"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subprogram without disturbing its siblings.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""writing-a-body-patch-adb""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
  & "riting-a-body-patch-adb"">Writing a body patch (<code>.adb</c"
  & "ode>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The spec patch declares the contracts. The <strong>body p"
  & "atch</strong> is what makes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove actually analyse the vendored body (the body-must-"
  & "opt-in rule). It"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "lives at the body&#8217;s relative path and mirrors the body"
  & "&#8217;s declarations with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<em>stub bodies</em> that the merge ignores &#8211; the orig"
  & "inal implementation is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "preserved:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/d"
  & "eps/vecmath/vecmath.adb"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi :"
  & " in Integer)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     return Integer with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   begin"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      null;  --  stub: the original body's implementation is"
  & " kept"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   end Clamp;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end Vecmath;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The merge replaces the original declaration (up to its <c"
  & "ode>is</code>) with the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "patch&#8217;s aspect-carrying declaration and keeps the orig"
  & "inal body proper, so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the copy gnatprove sees is <code>package body Vecmath with S"
  & "PARK_Mode =&gt; On is ... &lt;original implementation&gt; .."
  & ".</code>. A fully SPARK-clean body needs only the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package-level aspect. The per-subprogram aspect covers bodie"
  & "s with a mix of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "clean and I/O-bound subprograms.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""matching-rules""><a class=""header"" href=""#matching-ru"
  & "les"">Matching rules</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The merge matches each patched declaration against the or"
  & "iginal by <strong>name and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "normalised parameter profile</strong>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Matching is whitespace-insensitive. A single-line parame"
  & "ter list matches a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "multi-line one.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The default <code>in</code> mode is equivalent to a bare"
  & " mode (<code>X : in Integer</code> matches"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>X : Integer</code>). <code>in out</code> and <code>out"
  & "</code> are distinct modes.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>an overloaded subprogram patches its exact signature &#8"
  & "211; a patched"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "two-argument <code>Scroll_Screen</code> replaces the two-arg"
  & "ument original, never a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same-named sibling;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>a spec declaration terminates at its <code>;</code>, a b"
  & "ody declaration at its <code>is</code>;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>a patched subprogram with <strong>no match</strong> in t"
  & "he original fails loudly (the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "patch is skipped and reported) rather than silently dropping"
  & " the contract.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""worked-example-vecmathclamp""><a class=""header"" href="
  & """#worked-example-vecmathclamp"">Worked example: <code>Vecmath"
  & ".Clamp</code></a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A vendored package whose spec and body carry no contracts"
  & ":</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmat"
  & "h.ads (vendored, unmodified)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package Vecmath is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi :"
  & " in Integer)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     return Integer;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end Vecmath;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmat"
  & "h.adb (vendored, unmodified)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package body Vecmath is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi :"
  & " in Integer)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     return Integer is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   begin"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      if Value &lt; Lo then"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "         return Lo;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      elsif Value &gt; Hi then"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "         return Hi;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      else"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "         return Value;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      end if;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   end Clamp;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end Vecmath;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The two patch files from above (spec with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Pre =&gt; Lo &lt;= Hi, Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in Lo ."
  & ". Hi</code>, and body with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code>) merge into the copy unchan"
  & "ged in behaviour. gnatprove"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proves the contract: 2 VCs (the <code>Clamp</code> postcondi"
  & "tion and its termination"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "check), 0 unproved. A caller in the target&#8217;s own code "
  & "can then rely on the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contract without the vendored sources ever changing.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""when-contracts-prove--and-when-they-are-skipped""><a "
  & "class=""header"" href=""#when-contracts-prove--and-when-they-ar"
  & "e-skipped"">When contracts prove &#8211; and when they are sk"
  & "ipped</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>SPARK-clean body + body patch</strong> &#8211; g"
  & "natprove proves the patched"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contracts outright (the example above).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>I/O-bound body</strong> (calls <code>Ada.Text_IO"
  & "</code>, which is <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code>) &#8211;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove skips the I/O bodies by design and reports the uni"
  & "t out of proof"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scope. The contracts are still <em>declared</em> and the mec"
  & "hanism is exercised,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "but the body is not proved &#8211; and crucially, it never d"
  & "rags the target&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof level down. This is the VT100 dogfood case in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/Ada_CRDT"">Ada_CRDT</a>"
  & ".</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""common-pitfalls""><a class=""header"" href=""#common-pit"
  & "falls"">Common pitfalls</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Spec patch without a body patch.</strong> A SPAR"
  & "K-clean vendored body stays out"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "of proof scope. gnatprove reports &#8220;no checks generated"
  & "&#8221; or skips the unit."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Add the <code>.adb</code> patch to opt the body in.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>A patched declaration that does not match anythi"
  & "ng.</strong> Check the name and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the parameter list (modes included) against the original. Th"
  & "e merge reports"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>could not be merged ... (unmatched subprogram or overs"
  & "ized file)</code> and skips"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the patch.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Patching the wrong overload.</strong> The match "
  & "is profile-aware, so a patch"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "entry replaces exactly the signature it re-declares &#8211; "
  & "verify you wrote the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "same parameter list as the overload you mean.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Expecting contracts to prove against a non-SPARK"
  & " body.</strong> <code>Ada.Text_IO</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and other <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code> dependencies cannot be"
  & " analysed; the patch still"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "applies, but the proof does not cover those bodies.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""see-also""><a class=""header"" href=""#see-also"">See als"
  & "o</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.html"">SPARK assu"
  & "rance levels</a> &#8211; Stone to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Platinum, per-category objectives</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#the-prove-subcommand"">CLI reference &#8211; th"
  & "e <code>prove</code> subcommand</a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "&#8211; flags, gnatprove resolution, the fall-through assess"
  & "ment</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#ci-threshold-gates---require-"">CLI reference &"
  & "#8211; CI threshold gates</a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "&#8211; <code>--require-spark</code> / <code>--require-proof"
  & "</code> / <code>--require-tests</code></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#target-project-requirements"">Target project re"
  & "quirements</a> &#8211; what a project must provide</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""#proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-de"
  & "pendencies"">Architecture &#8211; proof patches</a>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "&#8211; the design, the merge engine, and the patched-copy p"
  & "ipeline</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""proof/16.1.0-ledger.html"">The proof ledger</a> "
  & "&#8211; how adacovex&#8217;s own 487-VC"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof is tracked</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""adacovex-architecture-decisions""><a class=""header"" h"
  & "ref=""#adacovex-architecture-decisions"">adacovex Architecture"
  & " Decisions</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""dependency-management-alire""><a class=""header"" href="
  & """#dependency-management-alire"">Dependency Management: Alire<"
  & "/a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex uses <a href=""https://alire.ada.dev/"">Alire</a> "
  & "as its packaging and delivery mechanism. The publishing mani"
  & "fest <code>alire.toml</code> declares <strong>zero dependenc"
  & "ies</strong>. It declares no libraries beyond the GNAT runti"
  & "me. It declares no tool dependencies.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>In particular <code>gnatprove</code> is <em>not</em> a de"
  & "clared dependency. adacovex analyses <code>gnatprove.out</co"
  & "de> files produced externally. The <code>prove</code> subcom"
  & "mand resolves a gnatprove executable at run time (per-projec"
  & "t manifest, <code>$PATH</code>, cached toolchain, or downloa"
  & "d). Development-only tools (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gn"
  & "atdoc_bin</code>, <code>gnatformat_bin</code>) are declared "
  & "in <code>alire-dev.toml</code>, which is never published to "
  & "the Alire community index.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""manifest-distinction-aliretoml-vs-alire-devtoml""><a "
  & "class=""header"" href=""#manifest-distinction-aliretoml-vs-alir"
  & "e-devtoml"">Manifest distinction (<code>alire.toml</code> vs "
  & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code>)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>alire.toml</code></strong>: The clean publ"
  & "ishing manifest. Declares no dependencies at"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "all, so <code>alr install covex</code> (or <code>alr build</"
  & "code> from source) pulls nothing beyond"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the binary and the GNAT compiler. Used for SBOM generation a"
  & "nd dependency"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "graph scanning.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>alire-dev.toml</code></strong>: The develo"
  & "pment manifest. Extends <code>alire.toml</code> with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dev-only tools (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin</c"
  & "ode>, <code>gnatformat_bin</code>) needed for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make prove</code>, <code>make doc</code>, and <code>ma"
  & "ke fmt</code>. Used for toolchain resolution when"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "running <code>alr exec</code>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When both files exist, <code>Build_Dependency_Graph</code"
  & "> reads <strong>both</strong>: a dependency"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "declared in <code>alire.toml</code> is classified <code>Scop"
  & "e_Base</code> (explicit/clean dep) and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "one declared only in <code>alire-dev.toml</code> is <code>Sc"
  & "ope_Dev</code>. The scope is surfaced in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the SBOM as the <code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> property (<c"
  & "ode>base</code> / <code>dev</code> / <code>transitive</code>"
  & " /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>vendored</code>), so it is always clear which file a d"
  & "ependency came from."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> is also consulted for gnatprove "
  & "detection"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>Manifest_Declares_GNATprove</code> checks both manife"
  & "sts).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand""><a "
  & "class=""header"" href=""#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-s"
  & "ubcommand"">GNATprove toolchain resolution (<code>prove</code"
  & "> subcommand)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex declares <code>gnatprove</code> only in its own "
  & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> (keeping the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "publishing <code>alire.toml</code> clean). The <code>prove</"
  & "code> subcommand resolves the <code>gnatprove</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "executable in this order:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Per-project manifest (authoritative)</strong>: i"
  & "f <code>&lt;target&gt;/alire.toml</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/alire-dev.toml</code> declares a <code>"
  & "gnatprove</code> dependency, the pinned"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove binary crate is deployed standalone into <code>~/."
  & "adacovex/toolchain/</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "via <code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</code> and ex"
  & "ecuted directly (the version-set"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "expression, for example <code>^16.1.0</code>, is reduced to "
  & "the bare version alr"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "accepts). This isolates the proof run from the target&#8217;"
  & "s other dev-manifest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tools and never swaps manifests. A manifest pin always wins."
  & " When the pinned"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "version cannot be deployed, the run fails instead of falling"
  & " back.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Global version pin</strong>: the <code>ADACOVEX_"
  & "GNATPROVE_VERSION</code> environment"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "variable or the <code>[prove] gnatprove-version</code> key i"
  & "n"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>~/.adacovex/adacovex.toml</code>, deployed standalone "
  & "via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</code>. It uses t"
  & "he same never-fall-back"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "semantics. It is folded into the proof result-cache identity"
  & ".</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>$PATH</code></strong>: a <code>gnatprove</"
  & "code> already installed (for example <code>alr install gnatp"
  & "rove</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Cached toolchain</strong>: <code>~/.adacovex/too"
  & "lchain/</code>. The download layout"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>&lt;toolchain&gt;/bin/gnatprove</code>) is used. A pr"
  & "eviously <code>alr get</code>-deployed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>gnatprove_*/</code> crate is also used.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Download</strong>: last-resort platform toolchai"
  & "n bundle.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Effective order: <strong>manifest pin &gt; global pin (co"
  & "nfig/env) &gt; PATH &gt; cache &gt;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "download</strong>. If a project manifest declares <code>gnat"
  & "prove</code> but <code>alr</code> is missing,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "install Alire first. The remaining fallbacks then apply.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>make doc</code> / <code>make fmt</code> targets"
  & " still swap <code>alire-dev.toml</code> over"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire.toml</code> for the duration of <code>gnatdoc</c"
  & "ode> / <code>gnatformat</code> (the <code>_dev_cmd</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Makefile recipe backs up <code>alire.toml</code> / <code>ali"
  & "re.lock</code> / <code>alire/</code>, swaps, runs,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and restores via a <code>trap</code>). <code>prove</code> do"
  & "es not use that swap. It deploys only"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the single gnatprove crate.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The assessment and SBOM pipeline always scans the publish"
  & "ing <code>alire.toml</code>, so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dev-only tool declarations never leak into dependency graphs"
  & " or SBOMs.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""system-tool-dev-dependencies-sbom""><a class=""header"""
  & " href=""#system-tool-dev-dependencies-sbom"">System-tool dev d"
  & "ependencies (SBOM)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Beyond the Alire graph, <code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</c"
  & "ode> adds the system binaries a project interacts with at de"
  & "velopment time (<code>python3</code>, <code>git</code>, <cod"
  & "e>gnatprove</code>, <code>make</code>, and more) as <code>Sc"
  & "ope_Dev</code> SBOM components. It scans the project&#8217;s"
  & " dev-facing files (Makefile variants, <code>.sh</code> / <co"
  & "de>.py</code> / <code>.gpr</code> / <code>.yml</code> / <cod"
  & "e>.toml</code> / <code>.ads</code> / <code>.adb</code>) for "
  & "a curated toolchain list and registers every referenced tool"
  & " that is actually installed on <code>$PATH</code> under a <c"
  & "ode>pkg:generic/&lt;tool&gt;</code> purl. Tools referenced n"
  & "owhere in the project, or referenced but not installed, are "
  & "skipped. A Makefile at the project root implies <code>make</"
  & "code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The scan runs after the cached manifest graph is resolved"
  & " (so cache hits and misses agree). Each registered tool&#821"
  & "7;s version is probed by running <code>--version</code> (or "
  & "a tool-specific subcommand such as fossil&#8217;s <code>vers"
  & "ion</code>) and extracting the version token, so the SBOM re"
  & "cords the installed version. A probe that fails or prints no"
  & " digit token leaves the version empty. The source file decla"
  & "ring the <code>System_Tools</code> table is skipped by the s"
  & "can.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Otherwise, every installed tool on the list can be regist"
  & "ered as a self-reference.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""vendored-components-and-test-labelled-dependencies-s"
  & "bom""><a class=""header"" href=""#vendored-components-and-test-l"
  & "abelled-dependencies-sbom"">Vendored components and test-labe"
  & "lled dependencies (SBOM)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Discover_Generic_Vendored</code> walks the target t"
  & "ree for vendor roots"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>node_modules</code>, <code>vendor</code>, <code>third"
  & "_party</code>, and the other recognised names)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Each directory inside a vendor root that carries an ecosyste"
  & "m manifest"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code>, <code>g"
  & "o.mod</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>composer.js"
  & "on</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Gemfile</code>, <code>pom.xml</code>, <code>Package.sw"
  & "ift</code>, <code>requirements*.txt</code>) becomes one"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "component with its ecosystem purl (<code>pkg:npm/...</code>,"
  & " <code>pkg:cargo/...</code>, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "more).  Its scope defaults to <code>vendored</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A component is classified <code>test</code> when the proj"
  & "ect manifest that owns the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendor root declares it under a test-only label:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>package.json</code> sections whose key contains <c"
  & "ode>test</code> (for example"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>testDependencies</code>);</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Cargo <code>[dev-dependencies]</code> (Cargo&#8217;s nat"
  & "ive test-only section) and any"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "section containing <code>test</code>;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>composer <code>require-dev</code>;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Gemfile <code>group :test</code> blocks;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>pom.xml</code> dependencies whose <code>&lt;scope&"
  & "gt;</code> is <code>test</code>;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>pyproject.toml</code> test extras and Poetry <code"
  & ">[tool.poetry.group.test.*]</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "sections;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Package.swift</code> dependencies declared inside "
  & "a <code>.testTarget(...)</code> block.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <strong>name heuristic</strong> is the fallback for e"
  & "very ecosystem.  A component"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "whose name starts or ends with the literal word <code>test</"
  & "code> is test-labelled."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The check covers the full name and then the last segment aft"
  & "er any <code>/</code> or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>:</code>, so <code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>test"
  & "-case</code>, <code>github.com/stretchr/testify</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>org.testng:testng</code> all match.  Ecosystems withou"
  & "t a native test-only"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "section (<code>go.mod</code>, <code>requirements*.txt</code>"
  & ") rely on this heuristic.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The heuristic also applies to <strong>lockfile-resolved n"
  & "ames</strong>:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> / <code>package-lock.json</code>"
  & " / <code>yarn.lock</code> entries next to an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "owner <code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code> cra"
  & "te names, and <code>alire.lock</code> crates"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that the manifest sets leave transitive.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The scope is surfaced as the SBOM <code>adacovex:dep_scop"
  & "e</code> property (<code>test</code>)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and in the dashboard dependency badges, scope filter, legend"
  & ", and rings."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The Alire-side <code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> sections and"
  & " test project files are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the other source of <code>test</code> scope; see the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#test-dependencies"">SBOM reference</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""unix-philosophy""><a class=""header"" href=""#unix-philo"
  & "sophy"">Unix Philosophy</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex follows the Unix philosophy of doing one thing w"
  & "ell:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Single-purpose pipeline</strong>: Each step (sca"
  & "nning, proof parsing, test parsing, DAL assessment, renderin"
  & "g) is a focused, composable unit.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Text-based interfaces</strong>: Input and output"
  & " are plain text (Ada source, <code>.out</code> files, Markdo"
  & "wn reports, ANSI terminal output).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>No library dependencies</strong>: Only the GNAT "
  & "runtime is used. No external"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "libraries or frameworks. Alire is the packaging/delivery mec"
  & "hanism but adds"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "no runtime dependency. adacovex declares no library or tool "
  & "dependencies"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(gnatprove is resolved at run time by the <code>prove</code>"
  & " subcommand).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Composable tools</strong>: The <code>prove</code"
  & "> subcommand runs GNATprove and then falls through to the st"
  & "andard assessment pipeline. The <code>sbom</code> subcommand"
  & " generates a proof-aware SBOM independently.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Exit codes</strong>: <code>0</code> for success "
  & "(DAL achieved), <code>1</code> for compliance failure. This "
  & "enables straightforward CI integration.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Minimal user code</strong>: users write as littl"
  & "e code as possible while getting"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "maximum value. The tool accepts third-party and generated co"
  & "de as it is. It recognises common docstring conventions (Ada"
  & " <code>--  @param</code>, Google <code>Args:</code>/<code>Re"
  & "turns:</code>, Sphinx <code>:param:</code>/<code>:returns:</"
  & "code>). It recognises common test-result formats (TAP, Autom"
  & "ake, Surefire, Unity).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It lowers foreign type names (<code>int32_t</code>, <code"
  & ">size_t</code>, and more) onto bounded Ada types. Nothing ne"
  & "eds to be rewritten to be assessed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""zero-library-dependency-design""><a class=""header"" hr"
  & "ef=""#zero-library-dependency-design"">Zero-Library-Dependency"
  & " Design</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex declares no library dependencies beyond the GNAT"
  & " runtime. All data structures use either:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>GNAT runtime containers (<code>Ada.Containers.Vectors</c"
  & "ode> for unbounded collections)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Fixed-size string buffers (<code>Max_Line = 262144</code"
  & ">, <code>Max_Path = 4096</code>, etc.) for bounded I/O</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Max_Path</code> and <code>Max_Line</code> scale wit"
  & "h the auto-detected host word size"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>System.Word_Size</code>), keeping the classic 4096 / "
  & "262144 values on 64-bit"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hosts while using proportionally smaller limits on narrower "
  & "machines. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "semantic limits (<code>Max_Id_Str</code>, <code>Max_Desc_Str"
  & "</code>, <code>Max_Filename</code>) are not"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "storage-size dependent and remain fixed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Max_Line</code> is deliberately generous (256 KiB o"
  & "n 64-bit) so that single-line declarations from heavily code"
  & "-generated projects parse cleanly. When a physical line <em>"
  & "does</em> exceed the buffer, adacovex <strong>never truncate"
  & "s it and then processes it</strong>. Truncation can silently"
  & " produce a partial (and wrong) result. Instead the parser dr"
  & "ains the remainder, reports the file and line to standard er"
  & "ror, and fails that parse explicitly.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The source scanner counts the skipped file in <code>Skipp"
  & "ed_Ct</code>, which forces the DAL assessment to <code>Unmet"
  & "</code> and the exit code to <code>1</code> (no compliance c"
  & "laim can be made for unread code). The same explicit-failure"
  & " contract applies to every parser: HLR/LLR markdown, GNATpro"
  & "ve output (text and JSON), test results, and Alire manifest "
  & "/ lockfile / GPR dependency graphs. An exact buffer-length l"
  & "ine is not an overflow (it parses normally), and paths excee"
  & "ding <code>Max_Path</code> are likewise reported and skipped"
  & " rather than crashing.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Overflow contract (two tiers).</strong> Path and "
  & "line buffers <em>fail loudly</em>. An"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "overlong physical line is drained and reported (<code>line e"
  & "xceeds Max_Line buffer</code>). The file is not parsed. <cod"
  & "e>Skipped_Ct</code> increments. DAL becomes <code>Unmet</cod"
  & "e>. An overlong path is reported and the file/subtree is ski"
  & "pped.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>No partial results ever flow downstream. Semantic text fi"
  & "elds (subprogram names, HLR/LLR IDs, descriptions, docstring"
  & " tag names/values, CLI strings) are</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><em>clamped</em> to their fixed buffer with the length fi"
  & "eld (<code>Name_Len</code>, <code>Id_Len</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>D_Len</code>, &#8230;) recording the recorded prefix, "
  & "so adversarial or generated"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "input can never raise <code>Constraint_Error</code>. Clampin"
  & "g keeps the scan correct."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The full token is still consumed so following tokens are not"
  & " misparsed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Why no chunking / LEB128.</strong> adacovex audit"
  & "s in memory. Counts (packages,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subprograms, HLR tags, tests, SBOM components) are unbounded"
  & " vectors. Each scanned unit is processed line-at-a-time into"
  & " fixed per-item buffers. A single Ada declaration does not a"
  & "dmit streaming/chunked parsing. Truncating a declaration is "
  & "worse than a loud failure.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Chunking can gain nothing. LEB128 (variable-length intege"
  & "r encoding) is a serialization concern and does not apply to"
  & " an in-memory CLI audit. The design therefore scales to arbi"
  & "trarily large codebases by dynamic allocation, bounded per-i"
  & "tem buffers, and explicit overflow handling, without streami"
  & "ng encodings.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The bounded-buffer constants are tabulated in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>docs/api-docs/adacovex-types.md</code> (<code>Max_Line"
  & "</code>, <code>Max_Path</code>, <code>Max_Desc_Str</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Max_Filename</code>, <code>Max_Id_Str</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This ensures adacovex can be built and run on any system "
  & "with a GNAT toolchain,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "without requiring any additional package installation beyond"
  & " Alire for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "toolchain management.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""spark-formal-verification""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
  & "spark-formal-verification"">SPARK Formal Verification</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex itself is SPARK-proven at Platinum level (all VC"
  & "s proved,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "AoRTE-free). The tool analyses GNATprove output (<code>gnatp"
  & "rove.out</code>) to assess"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SPARK assurance levels (Stone through Platinum) for target p"
  & "rojects.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The tool does not perform verification itself. It parses "
  & "and reports on proof"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "results produced by GNATprove. This keeps the tool&#8217;s s"
  & "cope narrow and aligns"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "with the Unix philosophy of composing specialised tools.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""proof-scope-and-justification-policy""><a class=""head"
  & "er"" href=""#proof-scope-and-justification-policy"">Proof scope"
  & " and justification policy</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Proof scope is the target&#8217;s own units.</st"
  & "rong> adacovex proves the Ada/SPARK"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "code it is run against, never third-party dependencies. GNAT"
  & "prove units that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "are skipped (for example standard-library or vendor code tha"
  & "t GNATprove"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "itself does not analyse) are tracked via <code>Units_Skipped"
  & "</code> and reported in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ANSI and Markdown reports. They are out of proof scope by de"
  & "sign, not a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof failure.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Justifications are an accepted discharge mechani"
  & "sm.</strong> A <code>Total</code> row&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Justified</code> count (GNATprove <code>pragma Annotat"
  & "e</code> justifications for decidedly"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "unprovable checks, such as non-functional foreign-language c"
  & "alls) is counted"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "neither as proved nor as unproved: <code>Proved = Total - Ju"
  & "stified - Unproved</code>."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Justified VCs do <strong>not</strong> downgrade the SPARK le"
  & "vel. Only unproved VCs do."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "This is pinned by unit tests.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Gold is the minimum compliance baseline. Platinu"
  & "m is the ideal.</strong>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Min_SPARK_For</code> thresholds (A=Gold, B=Silver, C=B"
  & "ronze, D/E=Stone) are the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gate for DAL compliance. Platinum is achieved and reported w"
  & "hen every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "functional contract is proved, but it is a best-effort targe"
  & "t, not a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "compliance requirement at any DAL level.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""ir-synthesiser""><a class=""header"" href=""#ir-synthesi"
  & "ser"">IR Synthesiser</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>src/ir/</code> layer starts an intermediate rep"
  & "resentation for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cross-compilation assessments, so the tool can reason about "
  & "types as they"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "exist on a target rather than only as they appear in Ada sou"
  & "rce:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Adacovex.Target_Profiles</code> defines bounded ma"
  & "chine-integer types"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>IR_Int8</code>..<code>IR_Int64</code>, <code>IR_UInt8"
  & "</code>..<code>IR_UInt64</code>) with <code>Size</code> clau"
  & "ses and a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Target_Config</code> record (host/target/pointer word "
  & "sizes). The types are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SPARK-proved: <code>Checked_Add32</code> / <code>Checked_Add"
  & "64</code> show overflow is detected,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "not undefined.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Synthesiser</code> lowers foreign type"
  & " names (<code>int8_t</code>, <code>size_t</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>usize</code>, <code>ptrdiff_t</code>, &#8230;) onto th"
  & "e bounded IR types and synthesizes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package declarations from a comma/whitespace-separated type "
  & "list.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Bounds</code> is a gnatprove fixture d"
  & "eriving synthesized-style"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>int32_t</code> / <code>int64_t</code> types and provin"
  & "g their <code>Add32</code> / <code>Add64</code> overflow"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "checks, so absence of integer overflow on the lowered types "
  & "is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "machine-checked.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""do-178c-dal-compliance""><a class=""header"" href=""#do-"
  & "178c-dal-compliance"">DO-178C DAL Compliance</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The DAL assessment evaluates four criteria:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>All HLRs defined in <code>docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> "
  & "are traced by <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code> tags in source</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>No orphan tags (every in-source HLR maps to a defined HL"
  & "R)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>All tests passing (zero failures in <code>test_result.md"
  & "</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Minimum SPARK proof level met (varies by DAL level)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>DAL-C is the default target level. Higher levels (A, B) r"
  & "equire stricter proof levels (Gold, Silver respectively).</p"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""source-scanning""><a class=""header"" href=""#source-sca"
  & "nning"">Source Scanning</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The scanner walks the target directory tree, skipping alw"
  & "ays-excluded directories (<code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code"
  & ">, <code>tests</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>.adacovex<"
  & "/code>). For each <code>.ads</code> file found, it extracts:"
  & "</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Package name from filename</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Subprogram declarations (<code>procedure</code>, <code>f"
  & "unction</code>, <code>generic procedure</code>, <code>generi"
  & "c function</code>, and <code>overriding</code> / <code>not o"
  & "verriding</code> variants)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Docstring annotations (<code>--  </code> prefix with opt"
  & "ional <code>@param</code>, <code>@return</code>, <code>@fiel"
  & "d</code>, <code>@formal</code> tags, plus Google <code>Args:"
  & "</code>/<code>Returns:</code> blocks and Sphinx <code>:param"
  & ":</code>/<code>:returns:</code> fields)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR traceability tags (<code>-- HLR-XXXX</code>)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>In strict mode (default), the scanner also applies docstr"
  & "ing patches from <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> to document"
  & " vendored/third-party code without modifying the originals.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""patch-system""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-system"""
  & ">Patch System</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> directory overlays do"
  & "cstring information onto"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "third-party or vendored code that cannot be modified directl"
  & "y, so strict mode"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "can still reach 100% docstring coverage without touching the"
  & " originals.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""why-patches-exist""><a class=""header"" href=""#why-patc"
  & "hes-exist"">Why patches exist</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>In strict mode (default), all directories except <code>.g"
  & "it</code>, <code>obj</code>, <code>tests</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>config</code>, and <code>.adacovex</code> are scanned."
  & " Vendored dependencies (for example a copy of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vt100 in <code>demo/deps/vt100/</code>) are scanned, and the"
  & "ir undocumented subprograms"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "count against docstring coverage. Patches document them in p"
  & "lace.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""patch-file-format""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-fi"
  & "le-format"">Patch file format</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A patch file is a valid Ada <code>.ads</code> file contai"
  & "ning only the subprogram"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "declarations to document, each preceded by a docstring:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  Package-level comment (o"
  & "ptional, not used by patch engine)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package VT100 is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  Summary of the procedure."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  @param Name  Description."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   procedure Some_Procedure (Name : in Some_Type);"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  Another procedure with no params."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   procedure No_Param_Proc;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end VT100;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Rules:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>File name must match the original <code>.ads</code> (for"
  & " example <code>vt100.ads</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Subprogram names must match the originals exactly.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Only subprograms with preceding docstrings (<code>--  </"
  & "code> lines) are merged.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Overloaded subprograms: one patch entry per overload. Ea"
  & "ch patches the next"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "undocumented original with the same name.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The scanner merges <code>Has_Docstring</code>, <code>Doc"
  & "_Param_Ct</code>, and <code>Doc_Return</code> into"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the matching originals.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""patch-file-location""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-"
  & "file-location"">Patch file location</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>&lt;target-project&gt;/.adacovex/patches/&lt;rela"
  & "tive-path&gt;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>&lt;relative-path&gt;</code> is the path from the t"
  & "arget root to the <code>.ads</code> file. Example:"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to patch <code>Ada_CRDT/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code>, cr"
  & "eate"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Ada_CRDT/.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</"
  & "code>. The <code>.adacovex</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory is always excluded from source scanning.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-dependen"
  & "cies""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-patches-spark-contracts"
  & "-over-vendored-dependencies"">Proof patches: SPARK contracts "
  & "over vendored dependencies</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The same <code>.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;</c"
  & "ode> file can carry <strong>SPARK proof aspects</strong> in "
  & "addition to docstrings, so vendored dependencies participate"
  & " in the SPARK proof without modifying their sources. A patch"
  & " file that includes any of <code>SPARK_Mode</code>, <code>Pr"
  & "e =&gt;</code>, <code>Post =&gt;</code>, or <code>Global =&g"
  & "t;</code> (detected by <code>Adacovex. Prove_Patch. Has_Proo"
  & "f</code>) is a <em>proof patch</em>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A patch with only docstrings remains a docstring overlay "
  & "and never engages the proof machinery. This section is the d"
  & "esign. For the user-facing guide &#8211; how proving works, "
  & "writing SPARK contracts, and the <code>.ads</code>/<code>.ad"
  & "b</code> patch files with worked examples and pitfalls &#821"
  & "1; see <a href=""#proving-and-writing-spark-proofs"">Proving a"
  & "nd writing proofs</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">package VT100 with SPARK_Mod"
  & "e =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  Scroll a region of the screen up."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  @param From  Starting line of scroll region."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   --  @param To    Ending line of scroll region."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   procedure Scroll_Screen (From : in Natural; To : in Natur"
  & "al)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     with Pre =&gt; From &lt;= To;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end VT100;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>prove</code> subcommand merges proof patches be"
  & "fore running gnatprove:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Count_Proof_Patches</code> scans <code>&lt;target&"
  & "gt;/.adacovex/patches/</code> (<code>.ads</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.adb</code> patch files). A target with no proof patch"
  & "es is proved against"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "its own tree exactly as before.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>Build_Patched_Copy</code> copies the target tree ("
  & "excluding <code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>.adacovex</code>) into <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/ad"
  & "acovex-proof/</code> and overwrites each proof-patched sourc"
  & "e with its merged form &#8211; package-level aspects spliced"
  & " onto the package declaration line (for a <code>package body"
  & " ... is</code> declaration too), and each aspect-carrying su"
  & "bprogram declaration replaced by the patch&#8217;s declarati"
  & "on block. The merge matches on name <strong>and</strong> nor"
  & "malised parameter profile (<code>Param_Profile</code>), so a"
  & "n overloaded subprogram patches its exact signature and neve"
  & "r a same-named sibling. The default <code>in</code> mode is "
  & "equivalent to a bare mode. <code>in out</code> and <code>out"
  & "</code> are distinct. A spec declaration terminates at its <"
  & "code>;</code>, a body declaration at its <code>is</code> &#8"
  & "211; so a patched body declaration is replaced without touch"
  & "ing the body proper.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The original vendored sources are never touched.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol start=""3"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>gnatprove runs against the copy&#8217;s root project (<c"
  & "ode>&lt;copy&gt;/&lt;basename&gt;.gpr</code>)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and the resulting <code>gnatprove.out</code> is copied back "
  & "to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code> for "
  & "the assessment pipeline. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "copy lives under the target&#8217;s <code>obj/</code>, so it"
  & " is excluded from scanning,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "manifest graphs, and the prove input hash.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Proof-patch contents are folded into the prove result-ca"
  & "che key, so a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "patch edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prov"
  & "e.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h4 id=""the-two-patch-shapes""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-t"
  & "wo-patch-shapes"">The two patch shapes</a></h4>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A <strong>spec patch</strong> (<code>.ads</code> in the p"
  & "atch directory) re-declares the vendored"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "spec with contracts, exactly as the VT100 example above. gna"
  & "tprove analyses"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a unit&#8217;s body only when the <em>body itself</em> opts "
  & "in (<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> on"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the package body or a subprogram body), so a SPARK-clean ven"
  & "dored body also"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "needs a <strong>body patch</strong> (<code>.adb</code> in th"
  & "e patch directory) that declares the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "intended mode. The body patch mirrors the body&#8217;s decla"
  & "rations with stub"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bodies that the merge ignores &#8211; the original body prop"
  & "er is preserved:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/d"
  & "eps/vecmath/vecmath.adb"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi :"
  & " in Integer)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "     return Integer with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   begin"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "      null;  --  stub: replaced by the original body's imple"
  & "mentation"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "   end Clamp;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "end Vecmath;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A worked example end to end: a vendored <code>Vecmath.Cla"
  & "mp</code> whose original"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "spec and body carry no contracts, with the spec patch above "
  & "declaring"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> plus <code>Pre =&gt; Lo &lt"
  & ";= Hi, Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in Lo .. Hi</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and the body patch opting the body into the proof. The merge"
  & "d copy is what"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove sees &#8211; <code>package body Vecmath with SPARK"
  & "_Mode =&gt; On is</code> with the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "original <code>if Value &lt; Lo ... return Value</code> impl"
  & "ementation intact &#8211; and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contracts prove: 2 VCs (the <code>Clamp</code> postcondition"
  & " and its termination"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "check), 0 unproved.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Where the vendored body is SPARK-clean and opted in via a"
  & " body patch,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnatprove proves the patched contracts. Where it is not (for"
  & " example bodies"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that call <code>Ada.Text_IO</code>, which is <code>SPARK_Mod"
  & "e Off</code>), gnatprove skips the I/O"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bodies by design and reports the unit out of proof scope &#8"
  & "211; a proof patch"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "never drags the target&#8217;s proof level down. The Ada_CRD"
  & "T dogfood target"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proves the mechanism end to end: its"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code> dec"
  & "lares <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on the vendored package and pins the <code>Scroll_Screen</co"
  & "de> scroll-region"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contract (its bodies are Text_IO-bound, so gnatprove skips t"
  & "hem by design),"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> / Ada_CRDT&#8217;s <code>"
  & "make prove</code> run through the patched"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "copy, preserving the target&#8217;s proof.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""output-formats""><a class=""header"" href=""#output-form"
  & "ats"">Output Formats</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex supports multiple output formats:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>ANSI terminal report</strong>: Colour-coded summa"
  & "ry for interactive use."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Colour is suppressed under CI, <code>NO_COLOR</code>, or <co"
  & "de>TERM=dumb</code>, so CI logs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "stay plain (see <code>Adacovex.Ansi</code> and its pure deci"
  & "sion function"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Colour_Allowed</code>)</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>SVG badges</strong>: <code>spark.svg</code>, <cod"
  & "e>tests.svg</code>, <code>docs.svg</code>, plus <code>do178c"
  & ".svg</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>iso26262.svg</code> / <code>iec62304.svg</code> compli"
  & "ance badges (<code>--standard=all</code> emits all"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "three) for CI badges</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Markdown reports</strong>: <code>VERIFICATION.md<"
  & "/code> and <code>TRACE.md</code> for compliance documentatio"
  & "n</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>HTML dashboard</strong>: Interactive web dashboar"
  & "d with JSON API (<code>--serve</code>)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "It is standard-aware (defaults to all standards like <code>s"
  & "bom</code>) with light/dark"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "theme support (toggle button, respects <code>prefers-color-s"
  & "cheme</code>). The static"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "page shell (CSS, header, theme script) is a real HTML file,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>resources/dashboard.html</code>, bundled into the bina"
  & "ry at build time."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code> assembles the authored C"
  & "SS (<code>resources/css/dashboard.css</code>),"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the authored JS (<code>resources/js/*.js</code>), and the ve"
  & "ndored JavaScript"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "libraries at the <code>resources/</code> root (<code>graphre"
  & ".js</code>, <code>nomnoml.js</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>flexsearch.js</code>, <code>yace.js</code>) into a sin"
  & "gle minified page shell. The layout"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "separates dependency JavaScript (<code>resources/</code> roo"
  & "t) from authored dashboard"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "JavaScript (<code>resources/js/</code>), which is also how t"
  & "he SBOM asset scanner"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tells vendored components from the project&#8217;s own modul"
  & "es.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The tool regenerates <code>src/adacovex-dashboard_templat"
  & "e.ads</code> (a String"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "constant, committed and byte-identical when unchanged).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The Ada compiler includes that constant in the final bina"
  & "ry. Every released"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "binary - whether a GitHub release artifact or an Alire crate"
  & " binary - carries"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the complete dashboard with no external file dependencies.</"
  & "p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>At runtime, <code>Adacovex.Renderers.HTML.Render_Dashboar"
  & "d_Internal</code> only builds"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the dynamic card markup and injects it at the <code>__CARDS_"
  & "_</code> placeholder, filling"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the <code>__THEME__</code> initial-theme marker. The result "
  & "is a single self-contained"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "HTML document: no CDN, no network requests, works offline.</"
  & "p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>SBOM</strong>: CycloneDX 1.5, SPDX 2.3, or Markdo"
  & "wn format with proof, standard,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and DAL/level properties</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""result-caching-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#result-ca"
  & "ching-1"">Result caching</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex persists parsed analysis results on disk so unch"
  & "anged inputs are not re-scanned, re-parsed, or re-proved. So"
  & "urce scans, GNATprove summaries, test summaries, HLR.md/LLR."
  & "md requirement parses, the resolved SBOM dependency graph, a"
  & "nd the differential-mode scans are each keyed by a namespace"
  & " prefix plus the SHA-256 of the artifact(s) they were derive"
  & "d from. For example: <code>""scan:"" | ""prove:"" | ""tests:"" | """
  & "hlr:"" | ""llr:"" | ""graph:"" + digest</code>. Re-parsing a byte"
  & "-identical artifact yields a cache hit regardless of the tar"
  & "get directory or command line.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>An unchanged manifest/lockfile/.gpr set serves the cached"
  & " dependency graph. Unchanged HLR.md/LLR.md serve the cached "
  & "requirement parses. <code>--compare-base</code> / <code>--co"
  & "verage-delta</code> reuse cached source scans for the curren"
  & "t tree.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Schema namespace</strong>: the default cache roo"
  & "t is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>~/.adacovex/cache/&lt;version&gt;/&lt;Cache_Schema&gt;"
  & "</code>. <code>Cache_Schema</code> (in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>src/core/adacovex-cache.ads</code>) is bumped whenever"
  & " the serialized layout of a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cached record or the scanner/parser semantics change, so blo"
  & "bs written by an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "incompatible build are never served as if valid. System-tool"
  & " version probes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "are <em>not</em> under the result cache: they live in <code>"
  & "~/.adacovex/probes/</code> (a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "stable machine-level store; wiping the result cache must not"
  & " re-probe every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tool).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Graph key</strong>: the dependency-graph key has"
  & "hes the Alire manifests, the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire.lock</code>, every <code>.gpr</code>, the vendor"
  & "ed trees, and the root language mix."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "It also hashes the supported-language project manifests that"
  & " can own a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "vendored directory (<code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.t"
  & "oml</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code>, <code>go.mod</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>composer.json</code>, <code>Gemfile</code>, <code>pom."
  & "xml</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>Package.swift"
  & "</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and the npm lockfiles), so an edit to a test-labelled sectio"
  & "n or lockfile"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "invalidates the cached graph and the scope classification is"
  & " recomputed.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Eviction</strong>: <code>Put_Cached</code> evict"
  & "s oldest-first by modification time when more"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "than <code>--cache-max</code> entries (default <code>4096</c"
  & "ode>) accumulate. <code>Eviction_Count</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tracks removals and is reported in the ANSI cache line.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Overflow safety</strong>: <code>Serialize</code>"
  & " returns an empty blob when a package is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "larger than <code>Max_Cache_Blob</code>. Callers skip storin"
  & "g it and <code>Deserialize</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "rejects empty/oversized input, so truncated data can never b"
  & "e served as a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hit.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong><code>--target</code> normalization</strong>: <c"
  & "ode>--target</code> is normalised (<code>.</code>/<code>..</"
  & "code> collapsed to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a canonical absolute path) before scanning, keeping the <cod"
  & "e>File_Path</code> values in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cached <code>Package_Info</code> consistent across invocatio"
  & "ns that spell the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory differently.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>CI</strong>: the GitHub action persists <code>~/"
  & ".adacovex/cache</code> between workflow runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>result-cache</code> input, default true).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--no-cache</code> bypasses it entirely (useful when"
  & " artifacts change without their"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "content hash changing, or to measure rescan cost) and <code>"
  & "--cache-dir</code> relocates"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "it. The ANSI report shows a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>result cache: X hit(s), Y miss(es), Z evicted</code> l"
  & "ine per run.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""testing-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#testing-1"">Testi"
  & "ng</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex uses a native zero-dependency test framework (<c"
  & "ode>Adacovex.Test_Support</code>) with 1173 tests across 16 "
  & "categories. No external test framework (AUnit, and more) is "
  & "required. Test results are written to <code>docs/test_result"
  & ".md</code> in a parseable Markdown table format.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""complexity-check""><a class=""header"" href=""#complexit"
  & "y-check"">Complexity check</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <code>complexity</code> subcommand walks the whole ta"
  & "rget and scores many languages"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(C, C++, C#, Go, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Ruby,"
  & " PHP, Rust,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Shell, Kotlin, and the YAML/JSON/TOML/XML/Markdown/reStructu"
  & "redText"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "families) alongside Ada.  Per-subprogram analysis stays Ada-"
  & "specific; the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "other languages contribute file-level lines of code and deci"
  & "sion counts."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--excludes=EXT,EXT</code> skips listed file extensions"
  & " and is rejected unless the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>complexity</code> subcommand is given, so it can never"
  & " run on its own.  <code>make complexity-check</code> gates t"
  & "he tree through the same thresholds.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""timezone-resolution""><a class=""header"" href=""#timezo"
  & "ne-resolution"">Timezone resolution</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex honours the operating system&#8217;s timezone by"
  & " default.  The resolved"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "offset comes from <code>Ada.Calendar.Time_Zones.UTC_Time_Off"
  & "set</code>, the standard"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Ada runtime, which reads the <code>TZ</code> variable and th"
  & "e system timezone through"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the C library, so the default is always the operator&#8217;s"
  & " wall clock"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(DST-aware).  <code>status</code> reports the effective time"
  & "zone, the current date and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "time in it, and how many dated release changelogs the target"
  & " carries under"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>docs/changelogs</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>--tz</code> / <code>--timezone</code> override the "
  & "display zone for one invocation.  The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "value is either a well-known IANA name (for example <code>As"
  & "ia/Singapore</code>) or a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "fixed <code>UTC</code>/<code>GMT</code> offset (<code>UTC+8<"
  & "/code>, <code>GMT+8</code>, <code>UTC+08</code>, <code>GMT+0"
  & "8</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>UTC+08:30</code>).  adacovex ships no timezone databas"
  & "e, so a named zone"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "resolves from a built-in table of common IANA names and thei"
  & "r standard-time"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "offsets.  A zone that may observe daylight saving time (mark"
  & "ed in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "table), or one the table lacks, is probed against the platfo"
  & "rm tzdata"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>zdump</code> validates the name, <code>date +%z</code"
  & "> reads the current offset, both"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "through one shell command) for the DST-correct offset; the t"
  & "able offset is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the fallback when the probe is unavailable.  The date/time r"
  & "endering"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "compensates for GNAT&#8217;s local-time calendar accessors, "
  & "so the displayed wall"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "clock is correct in every zone.  <code>HLR-TZ</code> covers "
  & "this behaviour.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""build-and-documentation-gates""><a class=""header"" hre"
  & "f=""#build-and-documentation-gates"">Build and documentation g"
  & "ates</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Two cheap Python gates keep the dashboard and the hand-wr"
  & "itten docs in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "step with the code, and both run inside <code>make check</co"
  & "de>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>tools/csslint.py</code> (<code>make csslint-check<"
  & "/code>) enforces the dashboard spacing"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "convention: every <code>margin</code>, <code>padding</code>,"
  & " and <code>gap</code> pixel length is a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "multiple of 4px.  It also runs inside <code>make build</code"
  & ">.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>tools/check-docs.py</code> (<code>make docs-check<"
  & "/code>) fails when any paragraph in the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "user docs, README, or human changelogs exceeds four sentence"
  & "s, and it"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "rejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations (<code>i.e.</code>"
  & ", <code>e.g.</code>, <code>etc.</code>)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>tools/para-split.py</code> rewraps over-long paragraph"
  & "s to comply.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The generated <code>docs/api-docs</code> pages are exclud"
  & "ed from the paragraph rule;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "its source docstrings carry the same rule.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""supported-platforms-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#supp"
  & "orted-platforms-1"">Supported Platforms</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex supports the same platforms Alire itself support"
  & "s. Because Alire is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the packaging and delivery mechanism, adacovex inherits Alir"
  & "e&#8217;s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "supported-platform matrix. The crate builds via <code>alr bu"
  & "ild</code>. It is distributed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "through the Alire community index (<code>alr install covex</"
  & "code>). The release workflow"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "builds it with the Alire toolchain:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Binary distribution</strong>: Linux x86-64, Wind"
  & "ows x86-64, and macOS x86-64"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(the platforms for which Alire publishes binary releases and"
  & " GNAT FSF"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "toolchains, including cross compilers for ARM, RISC-V, and A"
  & "VR).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>From source</strong>: any platform with a GNAT F"
  & "SF 9.2+ compiler on which Alire"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "can be built (Alire lists FreeBSD and OpenBSD among buildabl"
  & "e hosts).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>GitHub release bundles</strong>: built on GitHub"
  & "&#8217;s Linux runners and distributed"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "as <code>adacovex-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> for every tag.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The GitHub Actions composite action pins <code>gnat-versi"
  & "on</code> (default <code>16.1.0</code>) via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire-project/setup-alire</code>, and CI runs on <code"
  & ">ubuntu-latest</code>, so the CI-verified"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "platform is Linux x86-64. The tool itself is written in port"
  & "able Ada 2012 using"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "only the GNAT runtime, so no adacovex code is platform-speci"
  & "fic beyond what the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "GNAT runtime and Alire toolchain provide.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""delivery-and-versioning""><a class=""header"" href=""#de"
  & "livery-and-versioning"">Delivery and Versioning</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex follows one version across every delivery channe"
  & "l, and each channel is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "version-locked to the same release:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Single source of truth</strong>: the <code>versi"
  & "on</code> field in <code>alire.toml</code> /"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> is the single source, resolved b"
  & "y installation method. <code>tools/gen-version.py</code> reg"
  & "enerates <code>src/adacovex_version_info.ads</code> at build"
  & " time (and <code>make bump-version</code>). It reads the fir"
  & "st available of <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> (release build"
  & "s), <code>alire-dev.toml</code> (source checkouts), or <code"
  & ">alire.toml</code> (dependency-managed installs). For depend"
  & "ency-managed installs, the published crate builds from its r"
  & "elease manifest, so the toml associated with the covex binar"
  & "y for dependency management carries the version. <code>Adaco"
  & "vex. Version</code> in <code>src/adacovex.ads</code> re-expo"
  & "rts the version.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>As a result, <code>--version</code>, the man page, the SB"
  & "OM tool version, and the result-cache namespace all derive f"
  & "rom the manifest and can never drift. Release builds bundle "
  & "the release tag instead via the <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code"
  & "> environment variable (release workflow / <code>make releas"
  & "e</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>CI is tied to the release version</strong>: the "
  & "GitHub Actions composite action"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>action.yml</code>) is version-matched to the adacovex"
  & " binary. The release workflow bundles <code>adacovex-vX. Y. "
  & "Z.tar.gz</code> and `adacovex-action-vX.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Y. Z.tar.gz<code>for every</code>vX. Y. Z<code> tag, and "
  & "the action downloads the binary for the tag it is referenced"
  & " by (</code>@vX.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Y. Z<code> runs that exact version). Floating tags (</cod"
  & "e>vMAJOR<code>, </code>vMAJOR. MINOR<code>, </code>latest<co"
  & "de>) are force-pushed at release time so </code>@latest<code"
  & ">/</code>@v1<code>/</code>@v1.3` always resolve to the newes"
  & "t matching release.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>CI platform/compiler</strong>: CI validates the "
  & "self-assessment (build, prove,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tests) with the pinned <code>gnat-version</code> on <code>ub"
  & "untu-latest</code>, so the CI-proven"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "combination is the released binary built against that exact "
  & "toolchain.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Attestation</strong>: every release bundle is at"
  & "tested with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>actions/attest</code> (OIDC), and the release notes li"
  & "nk the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "signed attestation.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""build-time-linker-output-sframe""><a class=""header"" h"
  & "ref=""#build-time-linker-output-sframe"">Build-time linker out"
  & "put (SFrame)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The Alire GNAT toolchain&#8217;s bundled <code>ld</code> "
  & "(2.44) emits a benign message"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>error in ...(.sframe); no .sframe will be created</co"
  & "de>) when it reads the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>.sframe</code> section that newer system binutils wrot"
  & "e into the glibc startup"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "objects. The link still succeeds. <code>make build</code> fi"
  & "lters only this one message;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "all compiler and gnatprove warnings remain fully visible, so"
  & " nothing real is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "ever suppressed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""read-only""><a class=""header"" href=""#read-only"">Read "
  & "Only</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex itself is read-only. It merely scans your codeba"
  & "se for target docstrings and proofs.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It does not make edits in place or on your behalf.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""flexible""><a class=""header"" href=""#flexible"">Flexibl"
  & "e</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex lets you write proofs and decide where proofs ar"
  & "e pointless (for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "example code that has to involve manual memory management). "
  & "You just have to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "justify your rationale. The tool is not rigid. It does not e"
  & "xpect 100% proving"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "for all use cases.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>You write the proofs yourself, so there is no magic or hi"
  & "dden abstractions here.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""pipeline-execution-order""><a class=""header"" href=""#p"
  & "ipeline-execution-order"">Pipeline (execution order)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When adacovex runs, it executes these steps in sequence:<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>0. Parse CLI args           -&gt; CLI_Config reco"
  & "rd (prove / sbom / diff / man / complexity / normal)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "0a. Early-exit modes        -&gt; --help / --version / man /"
  & " status / complexity exit before the pipeline"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "1. Determine ANSI color     -&gt; NO_COLOR check"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "2. (prove mode) Run GNATprove -&gt; fresh obj/gnatprove/gnat"
  & "prove.out"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "3. Scan source files        -&gt; Package_Vectors.Vector (su"
  & "bprograms, HLR tags, docstrings)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "4. Apply docstring patches  -&gt; Merge .adacovex/patches/ ("
  & "strict mode only)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "5. Compute doc metrics      -&gt; Docstring_Metrics (coverag"
  & "e %)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "6. Parse GNATprove output   -&gt; Proof_Summary (VC counts, "
  & "SPARK level)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "7. Parse test results       -&gt; Test_Summary (pass/fail co"
  & "unts)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "8. Assess DAL compliance    -&gt; DAL_Assessment (Achieved /"
  & " Unmet + reasons)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "9. Render ANSI summary      -&gt; stdout (terminal report)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "10. Emit SVG badges          -&gt; &lt;svg-dir&gt;/*.svg (if"
  & " enabled)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "11. Emit Markdown reports    -&gt; &lt;md-dir&gt;/VERIFICATI"
  & "ON.md + TRACE.md (if enabled)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "12. Emit automatic SBOM      -&gt; &lt;target&gt;/sbom.json "
  & "| sbom.spdx.json | docs/compliance/SBOM.md (unless --no-sbom"
  & ")"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "13. Start HTTP server        -&gt; :&lt;port&gt; (if --serve"
  & "; serves the dashboard,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "                              the JSON API, the SVG badges, "
  & "and the bundled"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "                              offline manual at /docs)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "14. Set exit code            -&gt; 0 if Achieved, 1 if Unmet"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Differential modes (<code>--compare-base</code> / <code>-"
  & "-coverage-delta</code>) run before the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "pipeline and snapshot a base revision via <code>Adacovex.VCS"
  & "</code> (git <code>worktree add</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hg <code>archive</code>, svn <code>export</code>, fossil <co"
  & "de>open</code> on a copied DB, or a git worktree"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "against the jj store), assess base and current tree, report "
  & "the delta, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "exit. <code>man</code> installs the generated man page (<cod"
  & "e>Adacovex.Renderers.Man</code>) into"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the local man database (<code>~/.local/share/man</code>, Lin"
  & "ux/WSL) and refreshes it with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>mandb</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""swapping-the-gnat-compiler-llvm-backend""><a class=""h"
  & "eader"" href=""#swapping-the-gnat-compiler-llvm-backend"">Swapp"
  & "ing the GNAT compiler (LLVM backend)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex and Alire both default to the GCC-based <strong>"
  & "GNAT</strong> (<code>gnat_native</code>)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "compiler. No action is needed. Only swap if you specifically"
  & " want an"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "LLVM-backend GNAT (for example GNAT LLVM) for your target pr"
  & "oject &#8211; for"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "example to exercise dissimilar redundancy via diverse code g"
  & "eneration.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>GNAT LLVM is <strong>not</strong> yet packaged as a stand"
  & "ard Alire toolchain crate, so two"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "paths exist:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>Alire-managed compiler (preferred when available)"
  & ".</strong> If a GNAT LLVM binary"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "release becomes available in the Alire index, declare it in "
  & "your"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code>:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-toml"">[[depends-on]]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "gnat_llvm = ""*"""
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>alr</code> then selects it automatically for that p"
  & "roject&#8217;s builds. You can also"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "pick a default compiler for all projects with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alr toolchain --select --disable-assistant</code> and "
  & "choosing the LLVM GNAT.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><strong>System-installed GNAT LLVM.</strong> Install GNAT"
  & " LLVM on <code>$PATH</code>, then force the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Ada toolchain in the root <code>.gpr</code> so <code>gprbuil"
  & "d</code> does not fall back to the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "GCC GNAT:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-gpr"">for Toolchain_Name (""Ada"") u"
  & "se ""GNAT_LLVM"";"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>You can confirm which compiler built a given <code>.ali</"
  & "code> file by its first line"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>GNAT</code> vs <code>GNAT-LLVM</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ol>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Notes:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>GNAT LLVM and GCC GNAT are not guaranteed ABI-compatible"
  & ". Compile all Ada in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a project with the same compiler.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>GNAT LLVM&#8217;s <code>-fstack-check</code> support is "
  & "partial and some features"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>Scalar_Storage_Order</code>, <code>Convention C++</co"
  & "de>) differ from GCC GNAT.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>SPARK proof results are compiler-independent, so <code>c"
  & "ovex prove</code> and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "DAL assessment are unaffected by the choice.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
