  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""performance""><a class=""header"" href=""#performance"">P"
  & "erformance</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>adacovex is a zero-dependency CLI. Its hot path is the as"
  & "sessment pipeline"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(scan -&gt; patch -&gt; doc metrics -&gt; proof parse -&gt; "
  & "test parse -&gt; DAL assess -&gt;"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "render, plus the SBOM). This page documents how to benchmark"
  & " it. It also"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "documents the expected numbers on a typical machine and the "
  & "optimisations"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "that keep those numbers low.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""benchmarking""><a class=""header"" href=""#benchmarking"""
  & ">Benchmarking</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make bench</code> benchmarks the assessment pipelin"
  & "e and reports binary size:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>It builds the project, then times <code>./bin/adacovex</"
  & "code> against the repo itself.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>cold</strong> runs (fresh result cache + probe c"
  & "ache) and <strong>warm</strong> runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(populated caches) are measured separately.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><code>make bench</code> uses <a href=""https://github.com"
  & "/sharkdp/hyperfine"">hyperfine</a> when"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "installed. It falls back to the bash <code>time</code> built"
  & "in otherwise. No tooling is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "required.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>It samples generously so the reported mean is stable. Hy"
  & "perfine runs <strong>10"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cold + 15 warm</strong> repetitions (2 warmup runs). Each co"
  & "ld repetition deletes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the cache dir first. This measures a truly empty result and "
  & "probe cache. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>time</code> fallback runs <strong>5 cold + 5 warm</str"
  & "ong>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>It reports the raw and stripped binary sizes (the stripp"
  & "ed size is measured"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on a <code>/tmp</code> copy; the build output is never modif"
  & "ied).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Example output (hyperfine, x86-64, 8-core CI-class machin"
  & "e, 1.28.0):</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code>=== Cold (fresh result cache) ==="
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  Time (mean +/- sigma):  88.1 ms +/- 3.8 ms   [User: 62.1 m"
  & "s, System: 14.0 ms]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  Range (min ... max):    84.8 ms ... 96.4 ms    10 runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "=== Warm (populated caches) ==="
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  Time (mean +/- sigma):  34.2 ms +/- 2.3 ms   [User: 15.3 m"
  & "s, System: 8.7 ms]"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "  Range (min ... max):    30.9 ms ... 39.2 ms    15 runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & ASCII.LF
  & "== Binary size =="
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bin/adacovex            9.0 MiB (9461040 bytes)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "after strip             4.3 MiB (4463704 bytes)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "savings                 52.8%"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The numbers shift with the machine and the codebase. What"
  & " matters is the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "shape: warm is now in the tens of milliseconds, and the cold"
  & " path is bounded"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by the work that genuinely must happen (hashing the changed "
  & "sources and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "building the SBOM).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>For single-shot timings, plain <code>time</code> works th"
  & "e same way:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">time ./bin/adacovex --no-ca"
  & "che          # cold, no result cache"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "time ./bin/adacovex --cache-dir=/tmp/c  # warm"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>When you compare two versions, always reset the cache bet"
  & "ween runs. Use"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--cache-dir=&lt;fresh dir&gt;</code> or delete the cac"
  & "he dir. The result cache must not"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "hide the real cost.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make perf-bench</code> profiles CPU and syscalls di"
  & "rectly with <code>perf</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>strace</code> over <code>bin/adacovex</code>. It print"
  & "s the cache-miss rates and the syscall"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "counts so a regression in I/O or data layout is visible befo"
  & "re a release.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""what-the-numbers-mean""><a class=""header"" href=""#what"
  & "-the-numbers-mean"">What the numbers mean</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Figures below are from <code>make bench</code>/<code>perf"
  & "-bench</code> on this machine (hyperfine,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cold + warm, 2 warmup). They shift with the machine and the "
  & "codebase. What"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "matters is the shape:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Cold ~0.1 s</strong>: dominated by source scanni"
  & "ng (Ada file enumeration and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SHA-256 of every scanned file), the SBOM tree walk and word "
  & "scan, and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "renderers. Nothing here can be skipped: the result cache is "
  & "empty, so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "every file must be read and hashed at least once. The system"
  & "-tool version"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "probes are <em>not</em> part of cold anymore (they live per-"
  & "machine and are"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cached across cache wipes).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Warm ~35 ms</strong>: the on-disk result cache ("
  & "content-addressed per file,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "oldest-first eviction) skips re-parsing unchanged sources. T"
  & "he stamp"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "fast-path skips the per-file SHA-256 entirely (a file unchan"
  & "ged in size is"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "not re-hashed). The tools-set cache skips the whole SBOM dev"
  & "-dependency"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "word scan and the tool probes for an unchanged project. The "
  & "remaining"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "time is process startup (dynamic loader hwcaps probing, elab"
  & "oration), the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory walks, and the blob deserialization.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>System time is the tell. Cold runs show ~13 ms of system"
  & " time (file I/O);"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "warm runs show ~9 ms.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""optimisation-history""><a class=""header"" href=""#optim"
  & "isation-history"">Optimisation history</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Kept in reverse-chronological order.  Every entry names t"
  & "he measurement that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "drove it so the next round of work can see whether the previ"
  & "ous assumption"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "still holds.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""stamp-fast-path-hashing-1280""><a class=""header"" href"
  & "=""#stamp-fast-path-hashing-1280"">Stamp fast-path hashing (1."
  & "28.0)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The warm-path profile showed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48% of CPU:"
  & " every <code>.ads</code> file was fully re-read and re-hashe"
  & "d on every run just to compute its cache key, even though th"
  & "e content was unchanged. <code>Hash_File</code> now keeps an"
  & " in-memory map of path -&gt; (size, digest). A file whose si"
  & "ze still matches the recorded size serves the recorded diges"
  & "t without opening or reading the file. The fast path is used"
  & " only within one process (the map is not persisted), so a co"
  & "ntent change is always caught (the size differs or the map i"
  & "s empty).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The same fast path serves the SBOM tree-walk hashing, whi"
  & "ch re-hashes files the source scan already touched in the sa"
  & "me run (the two hash passes collapse into one real read + on"
  & "e size check). Warm user time dropped roughly a third.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""stable-probe-store--probe-results-in-the-tools-blob-"
  & "1280""><a class=""header"" href=""#stable-probe-store--probe-res"
  & "ults-in-the-tools-blob-1280"">Stable probe store + probe resu"
  & "lts in the tools blob (1.28.0)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The cold profile was dominated by the system-tool version"
  & " probes: each"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "spawns a subprocess, and node/hg/mandb boot an interpreter ("
  & "hg alone cost"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "~330 ms on this machine; the full probe set ~150 ms end to e"
  & "nd). The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "probes were kept under the <em>result</em> cache (<code>&lt;"
  & "cache-dir&gt;/probes/</code>), so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "wiping the cache (or pointing <code>--cache-dir</code> elsew"
  & "here) re-probed every"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tool.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Two changes removed that cost:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Probes now live in <code>~/.adacovex/probes/</code> &#82"
  & "11; a stable, machine-level"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "store external to the result cache. Wiping the result cache "
  & "(or using a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "fresh <code>--cache-dir</code>) no longer re-probes; only th"
  & "e 7-day TTL ever"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "re-probes a known toolchain. Cold on a warm-probe machine dr"
  & "opped from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "~658 ms to ~86 ms (7.7 x).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The tools-set cache blob now also stores each referenced"
  & " tool&#8217;s probe"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "result (<code>tool=version</code> pairs), and a cache hit re"
  & "builds the SBOM tool"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "edges from those pairs without PATH lookups, probe file read"
  & "s, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subprocess spawns. Warm dropped from ~39.8 ms to ~34.6 ms. T"
  & "he blob"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "format is names-<code>|</code>-version-pairs; <code>Cache_Sc"
  & "hema</code> was bumped to s6 so"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "old names-only blobs are never served as if complete. Cold a"
  & "nd warm"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SBOM output stays byte-identical.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batching-1270""><a "
  & "class=""header"" href=""#file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batc"
  & "hing-1270"">File-stamp fast-path and eviction batching (1.27."
  & "0)</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>Put_Cached</code> ran eviction after every store; e"
  & "viction walks the whole cache"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "tree. It now runs every 32 stores (bounded overshoot under t"
  & "he soft cap)."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "The SBOM dev-dependency word scan was rewritten from a per-t"
  & "ool substring"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "match (60 tools x line length) to a single-pass word extract"
  & "ion (per-word x"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "distinct tool lengths), and tool-output directories (<code>g"
  & "natprove/</code>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>__pycache__</code>, <code>node_modules</code>, <code>."
  & "headroom</code>, <code>.lccst</code>) were excluded from"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "both tree walks so the proof-run output is not enumerated. T"
  & "hose changes"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "alone took the warm run from ~1.02 s to ~63 ms (16x) and col"
  & "d from ~1.4 s"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "to ~545 ms, and reduced the warm-run syscall count from ~15k"
  & " to ~12k.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""probe-cache""><a class=""header"" href=""#probe-cache"">P"
  & "robe cache</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><em>(Origin story.)</em> The SBOM builds a <em>dev-scope<"
  & "/em> dependency edge for every tool that the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "target&#8217;s build references. The tool must be installed "
  & "on <code>$PATH</code> (for example <code>gcc</code>, <code>a"
  & "lr</code>, <code>git</code>, <code>make</code>). The SBOM pr"
  & "obes each tool with <code>&lt;tool&gt; &lt;flag&gt;</code> t"
  & "o capture its version. Each probe spawns a subprocess.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The subprocess costs tens of milliseconds per referenced "
  & "tool (<code>System: 42 ms -&gt; 9 ms</code>, ~150 ms end to "
  & "end on an 11-tool toolchain). Originally the probed versions"
  & " were cached under <code>&lt;cache-root&gt;/probes/&lt;tool&"
  & "gt;</code> with a 7-day TTL. That location meant a wiped res"
  & "ult cache re-probed every tool on the next run &#8211; which"
  & " is why 1.28.0 moved the store and folded the probe results "
  & "into the tools-set cache blob (see above).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""binary-size""><a class=""header"" href=""#binary-size"">B"
  & "inary size</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The debug-symbol-carrying build is ~9 MiB. Stripping (<co"
  & "de>strip bin/adacovex</code>) yields ~3.6 MiB (~60% smaller)"
  & " without affecting behaviour. GNAT&#8217;s default build kee"
  & "ps symbols for debugging (<code>gdb</code> works). Release a"
  & "rtifacts are stripped. <code>make bench</code> always report"
  & "s both.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Regressions in code size are visible in the same command "
  & "that reports timings. If the symbols ever come out, the bina"
  & "ry size is the same and the page should say so.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""ci""><a class=""header"" href=""#ci"">CI</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>CI runs the self-assessment with result caching disabled "
  & "where determinism matters (<code>--no-cache</code>-equivalen"
  & "t fresh dirs). The <code>make</code> gates are timed loosely"
  & ". Timings are informational only. The <code>bench</code> tar"
  & "get is not part of <code>make check</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It makes the gate machine-dependent. A slow CI runner mus"
  & "t not fail a build. The target is run by hand before release"
  & "s.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""when-the-numbers-regress""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
  & "hen-the-numbers-regress"">When the numbers regress</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Run <code>make perf-bench</code> first. It reports the CP"
  & "U break-down (the wall-clock"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>perf</code> output) and the strace syscall counts. The"
  & " single-reader/single-writer"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cache walks are the usual suspects: a new tree walk that re-"
  & "enumerates a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "directory which a cache already covers, or a new per-file ha"
  & "sh that the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "stamp fast path does not cover. The numbers in this page are"
  & " from the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "self-assessment; the Ada_CRDT target is smaller and exercise"
  & "s the same"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "pipeline, so <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> is a handy secon"
  & "d datapoint.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""ste100-technical-names-for-adacovex""><a class=""heade"
  & "r"" href=""#ste100-technical-names-for-adacovex"">STE100 Techni"
  & "cal Names for adacovex</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English (Section 1, &#822"
  & "0;Words&#8221;) defines a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "controlled vocabulary. Most words in that vocabulary are sta"
  & "ndard STE words."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Some concepts have no accurate standard STE word. For those "
  & "concepts, the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "project approves a <strong>Technical Name (TN)</strong>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>A Technical Name is a non-STE word that the project expli"
  & "citly approves. The"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "project approves it because no standard STE word describes t"
  & "he concept with"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the same precision. A TN has a single mandatory part of spee"
  & "ch and a defined"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "scope. The scope is restricted to the software domain of ada"
  & "covex.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This page is the controlled list of Technical Names for a"
  & "dacovex. Writers of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "user documentation, API documentation, docstrings, and chang"
  & "elogs must use"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "these terms as defined here. If you need a term that is not "
  & "in this list,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "add it to the list first, then use it.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""categories-for-ada-technical-names""><a class=""header"
  & """ href=""#categories-for-ada-technical-names"">Categories for "
  & "Ada Technical Names</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Group the Technical Names by their structural role in the"
  & " software domain.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Hardware and System Entities.</strong> Physical "
  & "components, buses, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "microarchitectures that the Ada code interacts with. For exa"
  & "mple, CPU core.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Ada Language Constructs.</strong> Specific langu"
  & "age features that generic"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "English words cannot replace without losing technical precis"
  & "ion. For"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "example, pragma, discriminant, rendezvous, task.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Domain and Mathematical Terms.</strong> Algorith"
  & "mic, mathematical, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "mission-specific logic terms. For example, telemetry, checks"
  & "um,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "quaternion.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Code Identifier Names.</strong> Exact package, t"
  & "ype, subtype, subprogram, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "variable names as declared in the source code. For example,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>System.Storage_Elements</code>, <code>Buffer_Size</cod"
  & "e>. This category also covers exact"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "file names, tool commands, and flag names that appear in doc"
  & "umentation.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""required-data-fields-for-each-entry""><a class=""heade"
  & "r"" href=""#required-data-fields-for-each-entry"">Required data"
  & " fields for each entry</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>ASD-STE100 requires strict controls over how approved wor"
  & "ds are documented."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Every Technical Name in this dictionary has all five fields:"
  & "</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>Approved Word (TN)</strong></td><td>The exac"
  & "t word or identifier.</td><td><strong>Pragma</strong></td></"
  & "tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>Part of Speech</strong></td><td>STE permits "
  & "a word as only <em>one</em> part of speech (Noun, Verb, Modi"
  & "fier).</td><td>Noun</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>Approved Meaning / Definition</strong></td><"
  & "td>Clear, unambiguous definition restricted to the adacovex "
  & "domain.</td><td>A compiler directive in the Ada programming "
  & "language.</td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>Non-Approved Alternatives</strong></td><td>T"
  & "erms that authors must NOT use instead of this TN.</td><td><"
  & "em>Compiler directive</em>, <em>Annotation</em></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><td><strong>Example Sentence</strong></td><td>A complian"
  & "t STE sentence demonstrating usage.</td><td><em>Add the <str"
  & "ong>pragma</strong> to the top of the package specification."
  & "</em></td></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</tbody>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""key-rules-for-ada-technical-names""><a class=""header"""
  & " href=""#key-rules-for-ada-technical-names"">Key rules for Ada"
  & " Technical Names</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Nouns stay nouns.</strong> Technical Names are a"
  & "lmost always approved as Nouns"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "or Modifiers. Never approve a code action as a verb if a sta"
  & "ndard STE verb"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "exists. For example, use the approved verb <em>Calculate</em"
  & "> instead of creating"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "a TN verb <em>Compute</em>.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Exact case matching.</strong> Treat Ada identifi"
  & "ers (<code>Pascal_Case</code> or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>UPPER_CASE</code>) as literal Technical Names. Use the"
  & " exact casing in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "documentation. This rule distinguishes language concepts fro"
  & "m code"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "entities.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>No synonyms.</strong> If the project approves <e"
  & "m>Task</em> as a TN for an Ada"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "concurrent execution unit, do not use words like <em>Thread<"
  & "/em>, <em>Process</em>, or"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<em>Job</em> for that concept.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>One part of speech per word.</strong> A TN is a "
  & "Noun or a Modifier, never both."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "When you need the action, use the standard STE verb that mat"
  & "ches the noun"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "form.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""standard-entry-template""><a class=""header"" href=""#st"
  & "andard-entry-template"">Standard entry template</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-markdown"">### Technical Name: Tas"
  & "k"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Part of Speech:** Noun"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Category:** Ada Language Construct"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Definition:** A standalone unit of concurrent execution "
  & "in Ada."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Approved Form:** Task (singular), Tasks (plural)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Do Not Use:** Thread, Process, Job, Execution Unit"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Correct Example:** *The main **task** waits for the sens"
  & "or **task** to finish.*"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "- **Incorrect Example:** *The main process waits for the sen"
  & "sor thread to complete.*"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""dictionary""><a class=""header"" href=""#dictionary"">Dic"
  & "tionary</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h3 id=""category-ada-language-constructs""><a class=""header"" "
  & "href=""#category-ada-language-constructs"">Category: Ada Langu"
  & "age Constructs</a></h3>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h4 id=""technical-name-package""><a class=""header"" href=""#tec"
  & "hnical-name-package"">Technical Name: Package</a></h4>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A named collection of relat"
  & "ed declarations in Ada. A"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "package has a visible specification and a private body.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Package (singular), Pack"
  & "ages (plural)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Module, Library unit, Compo"
  & "nent</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>A <strong>package<"
  & "/strong> groups the related subprograms.</em></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>A module groups "
  & "the related subprograms.</em></li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h4 id=""technical-name-package-body""><a class=""header"" href="
  & """#technical-name-package-body"">Technical Name: Package Body<"
  & "/a></h4>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The implementation part of "
  & "a package. It contains the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "bodies of the subprograms that the package specification dec"
  & "lares.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Package Body (singular),"
  & " Package Bodies (plural)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Implementation file, Source"
  & " file (when ambiguous)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>packag"
  & "e body</strong> implements the declared subprograms.</em></l"
  & "i>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The implementati"
