  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""ai--llm-usage-in-this-project""><a class=""header"" hre"
  & "f=""#ai--llm-usage-in-this-project"">AI / LLM Usage in this Pr"
  & "oject</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This page collects everything about how AI tooling is use"
  & "d in the adacovex"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "project: the disclosure, why the code is trustworthy despite"
  & " AI assistance, how"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "LLM agents are expected to work on the codebase, and the hon"
  & "est limits of"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "machine-generated code.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""ai-assistance-disclosure""><a class=""header"" href=""#a"
  & "i-assistance-disclosure"">AI Assistance Disclosure</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>AI tools were used during development for boilerplate gen"
  & "eration, contract drafting, and docstring formatting. This i"
  & "s stated plainly rather than hidden. The project&#8217;s own"
  & " dogfood target is a zero-dependency, fully documented, SPAR"
  & "K-proven Ada codebase. AI-generated contributions must meet "
  & "the same bar as hand-written ones.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>That bar is 100% docstring coverage, Platinum proof, zero"
  & " justified VCs, and the full <code>make check</code> gate be"
  & "fore they count.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""why-trust-this-code""><a class=""header"" href=""#why-tr"
  & "ust-this-code"">Why trust this code?</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Given the use of AI assistance, healthy skepticism is nat"
  & "ural and encouraged."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Reliability is grounded in proof and design, not implicit tr"
  & "ust:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Formal Verification:</strong> core Ada logic is "
  & "formally verified. It is Platinum"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "under <code>gnatprove</code> 16.1.0, 723 VCs, 0 unproved (se"
  & "e"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""proof/16.1.0-ledger.html"">docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger."
  & "md</a>). The proof is re-run by"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make prove</code> on every change. It is a hard gate b"
  & "efore any release.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Read-Only Engine:</strong> adacovex assesses inp"
  & "ut payloads, build artifacts, and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "reports without modifying your source files in place. An AI-"
  & "assisted tool that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "cannot write to the tree it audits is a smaller blast radius"
  & " by design.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Open Auditability:</strong> fully open source un"
  & "der Apache-2.0. Every line, human"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "or AI-written, is inspectable.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><em>Still skeptical?</em> See Ken Thompson&#8217;s landma"
  & "rk paper,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""https://dl.acm.org/doi/epdf/10.1145/358198.358210"">"
  & "<em>Reflections on Trusting Trust</em></a>,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on the fundamental nature of trust in software toolchains. T"
  & "he point is that no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "software, compiler, or model is trustworthy purely by assert"
  & "ion. It must be"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "inspectable and independently verifiable.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</blockquote>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""how-llm-agents-work-on-this-codebase""><a class=""head"
  & "er"" href=""#how-llm-agents-work-on-this-codebase"">How LLM age"
  & "nts work on this codebase</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><a href=""../AGENTS.html""><code>AGENTS.md</code></a> at th"
  & "e repo root is the machine-readable project"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "brief. It carries the architecture tree, the pipeline, the S"
  & "PARK discipline,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the Makefile targets, and the verification gates. An agent ("
  & "or human) working"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "on the tree must read it first. It must follow it. In partic"
  & "ular:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Match existing conventions</strong> and prefer e"
  & "diting existing files. Verify"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "non-trivial changes with the project&#8217;s typecheck and t"
  & "ests.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Zero library dependency</strong> is a hard const"
  & "raint. Use only the GNAT runtime."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Keep <code>tools/*.py</code> pure-stdlib, <code>typing</code"
  & ">-annotated Python.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>SPARK proof discipline</strong> (enforced by <co"
  & "de>make prove</code> and the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>spark-off-check</code> gate): zero unproved VCs, zero "
  & "justified VCs, no"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> outside the <code>Types.Implem"
  & "entation</code> and <code>Complexity</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "container packages (non-formal <code>Ada.Containers</code> a"
  & "re illegal in"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "SPARK_Mode-On code; see <code>docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</c"
  & "ode>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>The quality gate is the contract.</strong> <code"
  & ">make check</code> runs the same gates that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "CI enforces before a release. A contribution that fails it i"
  & "s not done.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><strong>Generated files are regenerated, not hand-edited"
  & ".</strong> The version constant,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "the dashboard template package, the architecture tree, the c"
  & "ount-synced docs,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "and the descriptions all come from <code>tools/*.py</code> s"
  & "cripts. Their <code>--check</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "modes verify they did not drift.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The doc-sync tools (<code>tools/update-test-count.py</cod"
  & "e> and <code>tools/update-proof-status.py</code>) derive the"
  & "ir file set from the tree itself (<code>tools/live_files.py<"
  & "/code>). They do not use a hardcoded list. A stale metric ca"
  & "nnot survive anywhere. Generated outputs and historical reco"
  & "rds (past-release changelogs, past proof ledgers) are exclud"
  & "ed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>They keep their release-time numbers.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""verifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them""><a class="
  & """header"" href=""#verifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them"">V"
  & "erifying claims instead of trusting them</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Every number in this repository&#8217;s documentation is "
  & "anchored to a generated"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "artifact, not to a human- or AI-written claim:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>VC counts and the SPARK level come from <code>obj/gnatpr"
  & "ove/gnatprove.out</code> (via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make proof-status</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Test counts come from <a href=""test_result.html"">docs/te"
  & "st_result.md</a> (via"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make test-count</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Crate descriptions come from <code>alire/description.txt"
  & "</code> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>alire/long-description.txt</code> (via <code>make desc"
  & "ription</code>).</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The CI badge <code>docs/badges/*.svg</code> files are emi"
  & "tted by the assessment itself."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "If a document carries a number that does not match the artif"
  & "act, one of the"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>--check</code> gates in <code>make check</code> fails "
  & "loudly. That is the point.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""working-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human""><a class="""
  & "header"" href=""#working-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human"">Wor"
  & "king in a fork or branch (LLM or human)</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Because the gates are cheap and deterministic, the safest"
  & " workflow is to"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "iterate locally and let <code>make check</code> be the arbit"
  & "er:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">make build &amp;&amp; make "
  & "test      # native suite must stay 738/738"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make prove                   # Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justi"
  & "fied"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "make check                   # full gate: static checks, bui"
  & "ld, test, prove,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "                             # doc, sbom, then tree-wide cou"
  & "nt-sync checks"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</code></pre>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>make check</code> runs the cheap static gates first"
  & " (ascii, spark-off, changelog, version source, doc links). A"
  & " formatting or sync problem fails before the expensive build"
  & " and SPARK proof. Then it verifies the count-sync checks (<c"
  & "ode>test-count --check</code>, <code>proof-status --check</c"
  & "ode>, <code>description --check</code>). A stale metric anyw"
  & "here in the tree fails loudly.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Regenerated files that are byte-identical when nothing ch"
  & "anged (the version constant, the dashboard template) are lef"
  & "t untouched. <code>git status</code> stays quiet.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""the-served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface""><a class=""h"
  & "eader"" href=""#the-served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface"">The s"
  & "erved dashboard as a trust surface</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p><code>adacovex --serve</code> renders a live HTML dashboa"
  & "rd at <code>/</code>. It also renders a JSON API at <code>/a"
  & "pi/metrics</code> and SVG badges at <code>/badge/*.svg</code"
  & ">. The same numbers that an agent or reviewer quotes from th"
  & "e CLI are visible and machine-checkable in the browser. The "
  & "dashboard shell is a real file (<code>resources/dashboard.ht"
  & "ml</code>).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>It is bundled at build time by <code>tools/gen-dashboard."
  & "py</code>. Page chrome is a plain HTML edit with no Ada know"
  & "ledge required. The dynamic cards are injected by the Ada re"
  & "nderer. The theme resolution chain (query param, then explic"
  & "it <code>--theme</code>, then saved <code>localStorage</code"
  & ">, then system preference) and the localStorage-only persist"
  & "ence are documented in <a href=""#web-dashboard-and-json-api"""
  & ">dashboard.md</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""honest-limits""><a class=""header"" href=""#honest-limit"
  & "s"">Honest limits</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>AI assistance raises the pace of contribution but does no"
  & "t change the bar:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>An AI-written docstring that is not provably accurate is"
  & " a liability, not a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "contribution. The 100% docstring-coverage gate measures pres"
  & "ence. Review"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "measures accuracy.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>Generated code must still pass the SPARK proof. A <code>"
  & "pragma Assume</code> or a"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> outside the two allowed contai"
  & "ner packages is rejected"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "by the gates.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>The changelog, the traceability tags, and the HLRs are w"
  & "ritten by people."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "They are also written by agents following AGENTS.md. The <co"
  & "de>changelog-check</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "validator enforces the canonical format. A machine-generated"
  & " changelog that"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "does not conform is caught before release.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""high-level-requirements--adacovex""><a class=""header"""
  & " href=""#high-level-requirements--adacovex"">High-Level Requir"
  & "ements &#8211; adacovex</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""requirement-index""><a class=""header"" href=""#requirem"
  & "ent-index"">Requirement Index</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-ARCH: Architecture and build system</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-SCAN: Ada source scanning</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-PROOF: SPARK / GNATprove proof analysis</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-TEST: Test result parsing</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-COMPLIANCE: DO-178C compliance assessment (all DAL l"
  & "evels A-E)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-A to E: Per-level DAL criteria (see below)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A criteria &#8211; all HLRs traced, no or"
  & "phans, tests pass, Gold SPARK</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B criteria &#8211; all HLRs traced, no or"
  & "phans, tests pass, Silver SPARK</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C criteria &#8211; all HLRs traced, no or"
  & "phans, tests pass, Bronze SPARK</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D criteria &#8211; all HLRs traced, tests"
  & " pass</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E criteria &#8211; all HLRs traced</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: ANSI terminal rendering</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-RENDER-SVG: SVG badge generation</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-RENDER-MD: Markdown report generation</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-RENDER-HTML: HTML dashboard and JSON API</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-SERVER: HTTP server</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-ANSI: Terminal colour support</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-TZ: Timezone resolution and local-time formatting</l"
  & "i>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-CLI: CLI argument parsing</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-COMPLEXITY: Cyclomatic complexity and LOC gating</li"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-METRICS: Docstring coverage metrics</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-DIFF: Differential assessment (&#8211;compare-base /"
  & " &#8211;coverage-delta)</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-MANIFEST: Alire manifest and dependency-graph parsin"
  & "g</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-PROVE: GNATprove subcommand</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-SBOM: Proof-aware SBOM generation</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>HLR-IR: IR type profiles, host/target config, and foreig"
  & "n type-name lowering</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""requirements""><a class=""header"" href=""#requirements"""
  & ">Requirements</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-ARCH: The tool shall build with <code>alr build</code"
  & "> and support Makefile targets for build, prove, fmt, lint, "
  & "api-docs, changelog, and clean.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-SCAN: The tool shall recursively scan Ada source file"
  & "s. It shall extract subprogram declarations, docstring annot"
  & "ations, and HLR traceability tags.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-PROOF: The tool shall parse GNATprove summary output."
  & " It shall categorise verification conditions (flow, run-time"
  & ", assertions, contracts, termination).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-TEST: The tool shall parse AUnit test results (Markdo"
  & "wn or stdout). It shall report total passed / failed test co"
  & "unts.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-COMPLIANCE: The tool shall assess DO-178C compliance "
  & "for any DAL level A through E. The compliance package define"
  & "s and implements the assessment criteria per level. The crit"
  & "eria appear in HLR-DAL-A through HLR-DAL-E.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A assessment shall verify HLR trace covera"
  & "ge. All HLRs found in source must be traced. The assessment "
  & "shall find no orphan tags. All tests must pass. The SPARK Go"
  & "ld level is the minimum requirement. All run-time checks, as"
  & "sertions, functional contracts, and termination must be prov"
  & "ed.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B assessment shall verify HLR trace covera"
  & "ge. The assessment shall find no orphan tags. All tests must"
  & " pass. The SPARK Silver level is the minimum requirement. Al"
  & "l run-time checks and assertions must be proved. The code mu"
  & "st be AoRTE-free.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C assessment shall verify HLR trace covera"
  & "ge. The assessment shall find no orphan tags. All tests must"
  & " pass. The SPARK Bronze level is the minimum requirement. Fl"
  & "ow analysis must pass.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D assessment shall verify HLR trace covera"
  & "ge. All tests must pass. There is no SPARK proof requirement"
  & ".</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E assessment shall verify HLR trace covera"
  & "ge only. There is no test or proof requirement.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: The tool shall render a colour-annotated"
  & " summary report to standard output. It shall use ANSI escape"
  & " codes.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-RENDER-SVG: The tool shall generate Shields.io-style "
  & "SVG badges. The badges show SPARK level, test status, and DO"
  & "-178C compliance status.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-RENDER-MD: The tool shall generate Markdown verificat"
  & "ion reports (VERIFICATION.md). It shall generate traceabilit"
  & "y matrices (TRACE.md).</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-RENDER-HTML: The tool shall generate a self-contained"
  & " HTML dashboard page. It shall generate a JSON metrics API.<"
  & "/p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-SERVER: The tool shall serve the dashboard, API, and "
  & "badge endpoints. It shall use a built-in HTTP/1.1 server on "
  & "a configurable port.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-ANSI: The tool shall colour its terminal output, and "
  & "shall suppress colour inside CI or when NO_COLOR is set.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-TZ: The tool shall resolve a display timezone from th"
  & "e operating system or from a user timezone override, and for"
  & "mat the current date and time in that zone.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-CLI: The tool shall accept CLI arguments in &#8211;ke"
  & "y=value and &#8211;key value forms. It shall use sensible de"
  & "faults. It shall print usage help on &#8211;help.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-COMPLEXITY: The tool shall compute per-file and per-s"
  & "ubprogram cyclomatic complexity for Ada source files. The to"
  & "ol shall enforce configurable LOC and complexity gates. The "
  & "gates cover maximum file LOC, maximum file percentage of the"
  & " codebase, maximum function complexity, and maximum file com"
  & "plexity.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-METRICS: The tool shall compute docstring coverage as"
  & " a percentage of documented subprograms over total subprogra"
  & "ms.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-DIFF: The tool shall support differential assessment "
  & "via <code>--compare-base</code>. The tool shall compare the "
  & "target at a git base ref against its current working tree. T"
  & "he tool shall report deltas in docstring coverage, HLR trace"
  & "ability, SPARK proof level, test results, and DAL status. Th"
  & "e tool shall also support a lightweight docstring-coverage g"
  & "ate via <code>--coverage-delta</code>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-MANIFEST: The tool shall resolve the project dependen"
  & "cy graph from Alire manifest files (alire.toml / alire-dev.t"
  & "oml). It shall resolve the alire.lock solved-crate list and "
  & "GNAT project (.gpr) with clauses. It shall deduplicate resul"
  & "ts across sources.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-SBOM: The tool shall generate proof-aware software bi"
  & "lls of materials. It shall use CycloneDX 1.5 and SPDX 2.3 JS"
  & "ON. It shall extend every component with the adacovex:proof_"
  & "level and adacovex:dal_target properties.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-PROVE: The tool shall provide a <code>prove</code> su"
  & "bcommand that runs GNATprove against the root .gpr file of t"
  & "he target project. gnatprove is not a declared dependency of"
  & " the tool. When the alire.toml / alire-dev.toml of the targe"
  & "t project declares a gnatprove dependency, gnatprove is reso"
  & "lved through Alire (<code>alr exec</code>). The tool then re"
  & "quires only <code>alr</code> on PATH. Otherwise it falls bac"
  & "k to a gnatprove on PATH, a cached ~/.adacovex/toolchain/bin"
  & " gnatprove, and finally a platform toolchain download. It tr"
  & "ansfers control to the standard assessment pipeline.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>HLR-IR: The tool shall define bounded target machine-inte"
  & "ger types. The types are IR_Int8 through IR_Int64 and IR_UIn"
  & "t8 through IR_UInt64. The tool shall define a host/target wo"
  & "rd-size configuration. The tool shall lower foreign type nam"
  & "es (int32_t, size_t, usize, and more) onto these types. The "
  & "tool shall synthesise bounded Ada declarations. GNATprove ca"
  & "n prove these declarations free of integer overflow.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""low-level-requirements--adacovex""><a class=""header"" "
  & "href=""#low-level-requirements--adacovex"">Low-Level Requireme"
  & "nts &#8211; adacovex</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""llr-mapping""><a class=""header"" href=""#llr-mapping"">L"
  & "LR Mapping</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-ARCH-01: <code>alire.toml</code> shall declare proje"
  & "ct metadata [HLR-ARCH]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-ARCH-02: <code>Makefile</code> shall provide build, "
  & "prove, fmt, lint, api-docs, changelog targets [HLR-ARCH]</li"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-ARCH-03: <code>adacovex.gpr</code> shall compile all"
  & " sources with <code>-gnatwa</code> warnings [HLR-ARCH]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-SCAN-01: Scan_Project shall walk directories recursi"
  & "vely. It shall skip .git and obj [HLR-SCAN]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-SCAN-02: Scan_Ads_File shall extract procedure, func"
  & "tion, and generic declarations [HLR-SCAN]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-SCAN-03: Scan_Ads_File shall find &#8211; HLR-XXXX t"
  & "ags in source [HLR-SCAN]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-SCAN-04: Scan_Ads_File shall find @param, @return, @"
  & "field, @formal docstring tags [HLR-SCAN]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-PROOF-01: Parse_Prove_Out shall parse gnatprove.out "
  & "and extract VC counts per check type [HLR-PROOF]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-PROOF-02: Determine_SPARK_Level shall assign level b"
  & "ased on proved/unproved ratios [HLR-PROOF]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-TEST-01: Parse_Test_Result shall parse Markdown test"
  & " results for pass/fail counts [HLR-TEST]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-TEST-02: Parse_Test_Stdout shall parse raw test runn"
  & "er stdout for pass/fail counts [HLR-TEST]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-01: Assess_DAL_C shall make sure that all HLRs a"
  & "re traced in source [HLR-COMPLIANCE] [HLR-DAL-C]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-02: Assess_DAL_C shall find orphan tags that do "
  & "not match any HLR [HLR-COMPLIANCE] [HLR-DAL-C]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-03: Assess_DAL_C shall make sure that test resul"
  & "ts show zero failures [HLR-COMPLIANCE] [HLR-DAL-C]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-04: Assess_DAL_C shall make sure that SPARK leve"
  & "l is &gt;= Bronze [HLR-COMPLIANCE] [HLR-DAL-C]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-05: Assess_DAL_A shall require SPARK Gold + test"
  & "s passing + all HLRs + no orphans [HLR-DAL-A]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-06: Assess_DAL_B shall require SPARK Silver + te"
  & "sts passing + all HLRs + no orphans [HLR-DAL-B]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-07: Assess_DAL_D shall require tests passing + a"
  & "ll HLRs [HLR-DAL-D]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-DAL-08: Assess_DAL_E shall require all HLRs [HLR-DAL"
  & "-E]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-ANSI-01: Render_Summary shall output colour-h"
  & "ighlighted terminal report [HLR-RENDER-ANSI]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-SVG-01: Render_SPARK_Badge shall produce vali"
  & "d SVG with level colour [HLR-RENDER-SVG]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-SVG-02: Render_Tests_Badge shall show passed/"
  & "failed in green/red [HLR-RENDER-SVG]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-SVG-03: Render_DO178C_Badge shall show Achiev"
  & "ed/Unmet in green/red [HLR-RENDER-SVG]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-MD-01: Generate_Verification_Report shall wri"
  & "te coverage, proof, test, compliance tables [HLR-RENDER-MD]<"
  & "/li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-MD-02: Generate_Trace_Matrix shall map each p"
  & "ackage to its HLR tags [HLR-RENDER-MD]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-HTML-01: Render_Dashboard shall produce self-"
  & "contained HTML with embedded CSS [HLR-RENDER-HTML]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-RENDER-HTML-02: Render_Metrics_JSON shall produce JS"
  & "ON with key metrics [HLR-RENDER-HTML]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-SERVER-01: Start shall bind to port and serve dashbo"
  & "ard at /, API at /api/metrics, badges at /badge/*.svg [HLR-S"
  & "ERVER]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-CLI-01: Parse_CLI shall parse &#8211;target, &#8211;"
  & "dal, &#8211;serve, &#8211;port, &#8211;emit-svg, &#8211;emit"
  & "-markdown [HLR-CLI]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>LLR-CLI-02: Parse_CLI shall default target to the curren"
  & "t working directory and DAL to C [HLR-CLI]</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""proof-records""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-record"
  & "s"">Proof Records</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This directory holds the record of every SPARK proof run "
  & "for adacovex.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""reading-the-ledger""><a class=""header"" href=""#reading"
  & "-the-ledger"">Reading the ledger</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The <a href=""proof/16.1.0-ledger.html"">gnatprove 16.1.0 l"
  & "edger</a> documents the current"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "verified surface:</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the VC counts (currently 724 VCs, 0 unproved, 0 justifie"
  & "d, Platinum);</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the audit of the skipped units and the reason each stays"
  & " SPARK_Mode Off;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the empirical evidence that the non-formal <code>Ada.Con"
  & "tainers</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "instantiations in <code>Adacovex.Types.Implementation</code>"
  & " and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Adacovex.Complexity</code> are the only irreducible SP"
  & "ARK_Mode (Off)"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "packages;</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li>the <code>[assumed-global-null]</code> warnings that the"
  & " SPARK_Mode On"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>Adacovex.CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code> carries.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""how-to-verify-the-numbers""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
  & "how-to-verify-the-numbers"">How to verify the numbers</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Run <code>make prove</code> at any time.  It runs gnatpro"
  & "ve through the <code>prove</code>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "subcommand and enforces the Platinum gate: 0 unproved VCs an"
  & "d 0 justified"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "VCs.  <code>make proof-status</code> then syncs the measured"
  & " counts into the docs.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The full proving workflow, including proof patches over v"
  & "endored"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dependencies, lives in <a href=""#proving-and-writing-spark-p"
  & "roofs"">Proving and writing proofs</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>Documentation in this directory uses British English and "
  & "ASD-STE100"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "Simplified Technical English.  See the <a href=""#ste100-tech"
  & "nical-names-for-adacovex"">STE100 Technical Names"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dictionary</a> for the approved terms about"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "proof, verification condition, and SPARK.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""compliance-outputs""><a class=""header"" href=""#complia"
  & "nce-outputs"">Compliance Outputs</a></h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This directory holds the compliance documents that an ada"
  & "covex run"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "generates for its target.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""files""><a class=""header"" href=""#files"">Files</a></h2"
  & ">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""compliance/VERIFICATION.html"">VERIFICATION.md</"
  & "a> &#8211; the verification results report"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "for the target: proof level, test status, and DAL/ASIL/class"
  & " outcome.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""compliance/TRACE.html"">TRACE.md</a> &#8211; the"
  & " traceability matrix between source,"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "requirements, and compliance evidence.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""compliance/HLR.html"">HLR.md</a> &#8211; the Hig"
  & "h-Level Requirements index.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<li><a href=""compliance/LLR.html"">LLR.md</a> &#8211; the Low"
  & "-Level Requirements mapping.</li>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "</ul>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""how-they-are-produced""><a class=""header"" href=""#how-"
  & "they-are-produced"">How they are produced</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The Markdown renderer writes these files when the assessm"
  & "ent runs"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "(<code>--emit-markdown=PATH</code>).  They are generated per"
  & " target.  The full file"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "formats are documented in <a href=""#target-project-requireme"
  & "nts"">Target projects</a> and"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<a href=""#adacovex-cli-reference"">CLI reference</a>.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>The rendered text uses British English and ASD-STE100 Sim"
  & "plified Technical"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "English.  Technical terms follow the <a href=""#ste100-techni"
  & "cal-names-for-adacovex"">STE100 Technical Names"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "dictionary</a>.  Audit the generated prose"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "against the dictionary before you use a new word in these re"
  & "ports.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div style=""break-before: page; page-break-before: always;"">"
  & "</div>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h1 id=""badges""><a class=""header"" href=""#badges"">Badges</a><"
  & "/h1>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<p>This directory holds the SVG badges that adacovex renders"
  & " for a target."
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<code>make run-self</code> and <code>make prove</code> regen"
  & "erate them from the current"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "assessment.</p>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<h2 id=""badge-set""><a class=""header"" href=""#badge-set"">Badge"
  & " set</a></h2>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<table>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<thead>"
  & ASCII.LF
  & "<tr><th>File</th><th>Badge</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
  & ASCII.LF
